tlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/8a19ec8c194a3b47.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/3788d0413d447c7b.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/8580190afe0e7452.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/d9038181f2c2898b.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/0a0a0ce2e4938fc9.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/35bbdf6d88b2676d.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/2dde4f69686a7528.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/312e9c6f3342e700.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/d926b7bfcc39c019.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/e452a5c043e34035.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/6cadf48bb7ae1a16.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/6aa74f1cd21e5f42.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/225f902a6f67538e.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/70e04241df03d52b.js?dpl=dpl_2yNSHZZSV2gyLWeGebQ5NBGpF6jQ\"],\"ScopedNavProvider\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4f:T6e6,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieve an OAuth access token, to be used for authentication of 'private' requests.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Authentication](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/authentication)\n\n**Authentication Methods:**\n\nThree methods of authentication are supported:\n\n\n- ``client_credentials`` - Using the client id and client secret that can be found on the API page on the website. This is the simplest method, suitable for server-to-server applications and quick setup.\n\n- ``client_signature`` - Enhanced security method that uses a cryptographic signature instead of sending the client secret directly. You generate an HMAC-SHA256 signature of a string containing a timestamp, a random nonce, and optional data, using your Client Secret as the key. This method requires `` `client_id` ``, `` `timestamp` `` (current time in milliseconds), `` `nonce` ``, `` `signature` ``, and optionally a `` `data` `` field. Deribit verifies the signature instead of requiring the raw secret. Best for enhanced security, asymmetric key pairs, and avoiding secret transmission. See the [Client Signature (WebSocket) guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/authentication#client-signature-websocket) for detailed signature calculation instructions.\n\n- ``refresh_token`` - Using a refresh token that was received from an earlier invocation. This allows you to obtain a new access token without re-supplying your Client ID and Client Secret. Best for long-lived sessions, token renewal, and avoiding re-authentication.\n\n\n**Response:**\n\nThe response will contain an access token, expiration period (number of seconds that the token is valid) and a refresh token that can be used to get a new set of tokens.\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fauth)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"50:T741,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Gracefully terminate the current WebSocket connection and optionally invalidate all tokens associated with the session.\n\nThis method provides a clean way to close WebSocket connections while preserving active orders when [**Cancel On Disconnect (COD)**](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/session-management/private-enable_cancel_on_disconnect) is enabled.\n\n**Use Cases:**\n\n- **Clean Shutdown:** Properly close WebSocket connections during application shutdown or restart\n- **Order Preservation:** Close connections without triggering order cancellations when COD is enabled\n- **Session Management:** Invalidate tokens to ensure security when closing connections\n- **Maintenance Operations:** Temporarily disconnect for system maintenance without affecting trading positions\n\n**Cancel On Disconnect (COD) Behavior:**\n\nWhen Cancel On Disconnect is enabled for your connection, this method provides a safe way to close the connection without triggering automatic order cancellations. This is different from other disconnection scenarios:\n\n- **Graceful logout** (this method): Orders are **NOT cancelled**, even if COD is enabled\n- **Unexpected disconnection:** Orders are **cancelled** if COD is enabled\n- **Inactivity timeout:** Orders are **cancelled** if COD is enabled\n- **Heartbeat failure:** Orders are **cancelled** if COD is enabled\n\nThis distinction allows you to perform planned disconnections (e.g., for maintenance, updates, or reconnection) while preserving your active orders.\n\n**WebSocket Only:**\n\nThis method is designed exclusively for WebSocket connections. Attempting to use it via REST/HTTP will result in a 400 error response.\n\n**Note:** This method has no response. The WebSocket connection is closed immediately after the request is processed.\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Flogout)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"51:T41b,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the account summary for a specific currency. The summary includes cash `balance`, `equity`, `margin_balance`, `available_funds`, `available_withdrawal_funds`, initial/maintenance margin, session and total PnL, options greeks, and related fields.\n\nKey relationships (standard margin): `equity = balance + futures session PnL + options_value`, `margin_balance = equity - options_value`, `available_funds = max(0, margin_balance - initial_margin)`. Under portfolio margin, `margin_balance` equals `equity`. Session PnL fields reset at daily settlement; `total_pl` does not.\n\nTo retrieve the summary for a specific subaccount, use the `subaccount_id` parameter. When the `extended` parameter is set to `true`, additional account details such as account ID, username, email, and account type are included.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\n\n**Scope:** `account:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_account_summary)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"52:Tb1c,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves a detailed transaction log for the authenticated account. The log includes all account activities such as trades, deposits, withdrawals, transfers, fees, and other balance-affecting operations.\n\nResults can be filtered by currency, time range, and `query` keywords. `start_timestamp` must not exceed `end_timestamp`; both values are clamped to the current time, so a future `end_timestamp` is treated as now. The matching window includes `end_timestamp`.\n\n`count` defaults to 100 and is capped at 1000. Pass `continuation` (a log id from the previous response) to fetch the next older page. `continuation` is `null` when there are no more entries.\n\nTo retrieve transactions for a specific subaccount, pass `subaccount_id` from the main account. Removed subaccounts are accepted. The authenticated user id is always applied as a filter.\n\nTrade entries executed in Starbase include `starbase_match_id`, `starbase_order_id`, and `starbase_timestamp`. Those fields are omitted on spot trades. Block RFQ allocations appear as `type` `trade allocation` rather than `trade`.\n\nWhen an option expires out of the money, the transaction log type is `expiry`. As there is nothing to settle into futures in this case, this remains the only entry in the transaction log for that expiration. In-the-money expiries use `assignment` or `exercise`, and may be followed by a `future creation` entry.\n\nLSP and ADL position moves are logged as `type` `LSP transfer` / `ADL transfer`. Both the liquidated/deleveraged account and the receiving account get that same `type`. A separate optional `role` field (`source` or `destination`) is present on those transfer entries — and also on `liquidation transfer` and `position move` — and is omitted on all other types, including `LSP commission` / `ADL commission` and ordinary `trade`s. Do not confuse `role` with `user_role` (`maker` / `taker`) on trades.\n\nCorrection entries may include a `related` array of the original log entries they correct. While the platform is starting, the method may return `temporarily_unavailable`.\n\n**History Limit:** This API method has **no time limit** - users can query transaction history back to account creation. Note that the CSV export feature available on the website is year-limited to 2023.\n\n**Note - This method has distinct API rate limiting requirements:** Sustained rate: 1 request/second. For more information, see [Rate Limits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/rate-limits).\n\n**📖 Related Support Article:** [Transaction log](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/25944587269021-Transaction-log)\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\n\n**Scope:** `account:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_transaction_log)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"53:T41d,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Approves a pending block trade. `nonce` and `timestamp` are used to identify the block trade while `role` should be opposite to the trading counterparty.\n\nUse [private/get_block_trade_requests](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-get_block_trade_requests) to retrieve pending block trades that require approval.\n\nTo use the block trade approval feature, an [additional API key setting feature](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key#block-trade-approval-feature) called `enabled_features: block_trade_approval` is required. This key has to be given to the broker/registered partner who performs the trades on behalf of the user for the feature to be active. If the user wants to approve the trade, they must approve it from a different API key that doesn't have this feature enabled.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\n\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fapprove_block_trade)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"54:T629,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Executes a block trade. This is the second step in the block trade workflow - the second party calls this method with the signature received from the first party to execute the trade.\n\nThe whole request must be exactly the same as in [private/verify_block_trade](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-verify_block_trade), only the `role` field should be set appropriately - this means that both sides have to agree on the same `timestamp`, `nonce`, and `trades` fields, and the server will ensure that the `role` field is different between sides (each party accepts their own role).\n\nUsing the same `timestamp` and `nonce` by both sides in [private/verify_block_trade](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-verify_block_trade) ensures that even if unintentionally both sides execute the given block trade with a valid `counterparty_signature`, the block trade will be executed only once.\n\n**Note:** In the API, the `direction` field is always expressed from the maker's perspective. This means that when you accept a block trade as a taker, the direction shown in the API represents the opposite side of your trade. For example, if you are buying puts as a taker, the API will show the operation as a \"sell put\" (maker's perspective), and you will be verifying and accepting a \"sell put\" block trade.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\n\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fexecute_block_trade)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"55:T4db,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Provides a list of block trade requests including pending approvals, declined trades, and expired trades. `timestamp` and `nonce` received in response can be used with [private/approve_block_trade](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-approve_block_trade) or [private/reject_block_trade](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-reject_block_trade) to approve or reject the pending block trade.\n\nTo use the block trade approval feature, an [additional API key setting feature](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key#block-trade-approval-feature) called `enabled_features: block_trade_approval` is required. This key has to be given to the broker/registered partner who performs the trades on behalf of the user for the feature to be active. If the user wants to approve the trade, they must approve it from a different API key that doesn't have this feature enabled.\n\nOnly broker clients can use `broker_code` to query for their broker block trade requests.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\n\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_block_trade_requests)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"56:T587,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"**Broker Method** Returns a list of clients registered under the broker account. Each client record includes:\n\n- `client_id` — a numeric identifier that groups one or more linked users under a single client name. Use this value in other Broker Voice API calls (e.g. `private/execute_broker_trade`) to identify the client group.\n- `links` — an array of individual user connections belonging to that client. Each link contains a `client_link_id` that uniquely identifies a single user within the client group.\n\n**How to obtain `client_id` and `client_link_id`**\n\nCall this endpoint without parameters to retrieve all clients. Locate the client by name or company, read `client_id` from the top-level object, and read `client_link_id` from the relevant entry in the `links` array. Use these two values together in subsequent Broker Voice API calls to specify which user within a client should be the counterparty.\n\nA link `state` of `connected` means the user has accepted the broker invitation and is ready to trade. Links in `pending` state have not yet been accepted; links in `rejected` state are inactive.\n\nOptionally filter by a specific `client_id` to return only that client's record, or set `include_subaccounts` to `true` to include clients managed by broker sub-accounts.\n\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_broker_clients)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"57:T41b,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Rejects a pending block trade. `nonce` and `timestamp` are used to identify the block trade while `role` should be opposite to the trading counterparty.\n\nUse [private/get_block_trade_requests](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-get_block_trade_requests) to retrieve pending block trades that require approval.\n\nTo use the block trade approval feature, an [additional API key setting feature](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key#block-trade-approval-feature) called `enabled_features: block_trade_approval` is required. This key has to be given to the broker/registered partner who performs the trades on behalf of the user for the feature to be active. If the user wants to approve the trade, they must approve it from a different API key that doesn't have this feature enabled.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\n\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Freject_block_trade)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"58:T4f9,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves **active** combos for the specified settlement `currency` (`\"any\"` for every currency). Inactive, closed, and archivized combos are omitted. There is no `state` parameter on this method.\n\nEach result is a combo object (`id`, `legs`, `state`, timestamps, `instrument_id`), not the full instrument spec from `public/get_instrument`. Combo `state` here is the combo-book state (`active`), which is not the same as the instrument order-book `state`.\n\nThis is not the same list as `public/get_instruments` with `kind=future_combo` or `kind=option_combo`, which returns visible combo **instruments** (including `locked` / `halted` / `settlement` books) and omits inactive combos.\n\nFor IDs including inactive combos, use [public/get_combo_ids](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/combo-books/public-get_combo_ids). For one combo, use [public/get_combo_details](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/combo-books/public-get_combo_details). Expired or archivized combo names are looked up with `public/get_instrument`, not this method.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_combos)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"59:T40b,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the LSP (Liquidity Support Program) participant configuration for the authenticated account.\n\nLSP participants are designated subaccounts that receive assigned positions from liquidated users as an alternative to auto-deleveraging (ADL). This method must be called with an API key belonging to the LSP participant subaccount itself — it returns an error if the authenticated account has no LSP configuration.\n\nThe response includes the participant's enable/disable state and any per-cooldown-group limit overrides. When the platform-side participant position lock is switched on, enrolling a subaccount as an LSP participant also locks it to reduce-only trading; this lock is off by default, so participation does not by itself restrict the subaccount to reduce-only.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\n\n**Scope:** `account:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_lsp_participant_config)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5a:T414,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves per-cooldown-group assignment usage for all LSP (Liquidity Support Program) participant subaccounts configured under the authenticated main account.\n\nMust be called with an API key belonging to the main account — returns an error if called from a subaccount. Use the `user_id` parameter to filter the result down to a single participant.\n\nAs with `private/get_lsp_usage`, each participant's group usage reports `pct` (limit, as a percentage of equity), `used` (USD within the current fixed window — flat until the window closes, then resets to `0` in one step), and `cooldown_start`/`cooldown_end` (the current window's timing) — remaining capacity is not computed for you and the leverage-derived cap applied at assignment time is not exposed on any user-facing endpoint.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\n\n**Scope:** `account:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_lsp_participants_usage)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5b:T53e,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the current per-cooldown-group assignment usage for the authenticated LSP (Liquidity Support Program) participant subaccount within its current fixed cooldown window.\n\nMust be called with an API key belonging to the LSP participant subaccount itself — returns an error if the authenticated account is not an LSP participant.\n\nInstruments are bucketed into one of 7 cooldown groups (6 crypto tiers plus a real-world-asset group); each group has its own limit (`pct`, as a percentage of the participant's equity), fixed-window usage (`used`, in USD — this does not decay smoothly; it stays flat until the window closes at `cooldown_end`, then resets to `0` in one step), and the window's timing (`cooldown_start`/`cooldown_end`). Neither the absolute limit nor the remaining capacity is computed for you — derive it from `pct`, `used`, and the participant's own equity from `private/get_account_summary`. Even a self-computed remaining-capacity figure won't reflect the additional margin/leverage-derived cap applied at assignment time, which isn't exposed on any user-facing endpoint.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\n\n**Scope:** `account:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_lsp_usage)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5c:T4b0,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the contract size (also known as contract multiplier) for a given instrument. The contract size is the value of one contract, expressed in the same unit as the order amount: USD for inverse (reversed) futures and perpetuals, and the base currency coin for options, spots, and linear futures and perpetuals.\n\nThis value is essential for calculating position values, margin requirements, and P\u0026L calculations. Different instruments may have different contract sizes.\n\nThis is not the quantity increment used to validate order amounts. Use `min_trade_amount` from [public/get_instrument](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/market-data/public-get_instrument) / [public/get_instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/market-data/public-get_instruments). On Starbase the same increment is named `qty_tick_size`. `contract_size` and `min_trade_amount` are not guaranteed to match.\n\nLooks up by `instrument_name`, including combo IDs and expired or archivized instruments. Unknown names fail with `instrument not found`. The same field is included on the `public/get_instrument` object.\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_contract_size)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5d:T4b5,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves expiration **labels** for listed futures and options. Values are instrument-style date strings such as `21SEP24`, or `PERPETUAL` for perpetuals — not Unix timestamps. Daily 08:00 UTC expirations are date-only; other expiration times include hour and minute.\n\nSpots and combos are not included, even when `kind` is omitted or `\"any\"`.\n\n`currency` is a settlement currency, `\"any\"`, or `\"grouped\"`:\n- `\"any\"` — a flat map keyed by `future` / `option` (dates merged across currencies). This is the shape in the example.\n- a named currency — `{ \"\u003ccurrency\u003e\": { \"future\": [...], \"option\": [...] } }` with a lowercase currency key (for example `btc`).\n- `\"grouped\"` — the same nested shape for every tradable settlement currency.\n\nIf `currency` is omitted, `currency_pair` is used (default: all pairs). When `currency` is set, `currency_pair` is ignored. `kind` defaults to `\"any\"` (`future` and `option`); `\"spot\"`, `\"future_combo\"`, and `\"option_combo\"` are not useful filters here.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_expirations)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5e:T5aa,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves detailed information about a specific instrument, including instrument specifications, contract details, tick size, settlement currency, expiration date (for futures and options), strike price (for options), underlying type, and other instrument parameters.\n\nLooks up by `instrument_name`, including combo IDs and expired or archivized instruments that `public/get_instruments` no longer lists. Unknown names fail with `instrument not found`. For live combo legs and combo-book state, use `public/get_combo_details` / `public/get_combos` instead of this method.\n\n`is_active` is true while the order book is visible (`open`, `settlement`, `locked`, or `halted`). It is not the same as tradable: only `state` `open` accepts new orders. After delivery the book becomes `delivered` (`is_active` false) and is later archivized.\n\nSpot instruments omit `settlement_currency` and `settlement_period`. Spot routed to Coinbase Exchange also omit block-trade fields and include `is_cbe_routed` / `is_csr` (present only when `true`). Futures include `max_leverage` and `max_non_default_leverage`. Some USDC spot pairs that support margin loans also include `max_leverage`. Perpetuals still have `expiration_timestamp`.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_instrument)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5f:Tac5,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves trading instruments, filtered by `currency` and optional `kind`. Responses are cached for about 1 minute and can be stale relative to live book state.\n\n**Note - This method has distinct API rate limiting requirements:** Sustained rate: 1 request/second. To avoid rate limits, we recommend using either the REST requests for server-cached data or the WebSocket subscription to [instrument_state.{kind}.{currency}](https://docs.deribit.com/subscriptions/market-data/instrumentstatekindcurrency) for real-time updates. For more information, see [Rate Limits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/rate-limits).\n\nWith `expired=false` (default) the list is not limited to tradable books. It includes visible instruments (`open`, `settlement`, `locked`, `halted`) plus inactive non-combo instruments. Inactive combos are omitted; combo kinds (`future_combo`, `option_combo`) return only visible books. `is_active` can therefore be `false` on this default list. Only `state` `open` accepts new orders.\n\nWith `expired=true` the list is instruments still in the live table with `state` `delivered` — recently expired, not archivized. Older expired or archivized names are looked up with `public/get_instrument`, not this method.\n\n`currency` matches derivatives by settlement currency: inverse (reversed) contracts settle in the base coin (`BTC` for BTC-PERPETUAL), linear contracts typically settle in the quote coin (`USDC` for BTC_USDC-PERPETUAL). `currency=any` returns every settlement currency.\n\nSpot matching is different. A spot's settlement field is the pair symbol (for example `BTC_USDC`), not `BTC` or `USDC`. When `expired=false` and `kind` is omitted/`any` for a specific currency, the response unions (1) derivatives with that settlement currency and (2) spots whose base or quote is that currency. `kind=spot` with a specific currency matches spots on either side of the pair. `expired=true` does not apply that extra spot union, so recently delivered spots are not returned under `currency=BTC`.\n\nResults are sorted with perpetuals first, then by expiration. Each instrument includes `underlying_type`. Spot routed to Coinbase Exchange includes `is_cbe_routed` / `is_csr`. Set `extended=true` for extra commission and (on futures) margin/perpetual fields that `public/get_instrument` does not return.\n\n**📖 Related Articles:**\n- [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\n- [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_instruments)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"60:T540,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves historical settlement, delivery, and bankruptcy events from all instruments within a given currency.\n\n**Settlement vs. delivery:** Settlement is a daily event (at 08:00 UTC) for futures and perpetual positions that converts unrealized profit and loss into realized profit and loss. Option positions do not settle. Delivery is a one-time event that occurs when a futures or options contract expires — any remaining open position is closed at the delivery price. Delivery does not apply to perpetual or spot instruments. Both events take place at 08:00 UTC, which is why they are sometimes conflated.\n\nResults can be filtered by settlement type and timestamp. Use pagination parameters (`count` and `continuation`) to retrieve large settlement histories. This data is useful for analyzing historical contract settlements and understanding market events.\n\n**Note on `profit_loss` and `session_profit_loss`:** Because this is a public endpoint, these fields are **platform-wide aggregates**, not per-account values. `profit_loss` is the sum of realized P\u0026L of all position holders at the settlement price. `session_profit_loss` is the sum of each holder's total session P\u0026L (realized + unrealized) across all participants.\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_last_settlements_by_currency)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"61:T51d,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves historical settlement, delivery, and bankruptcy events for a specific instrument.\n\n**Settlement vs. delivery:** Settlement is a daily event (at 08:00 UTC) for futures and perpetual positions that converts unrealized profit and loss into realized profit and loss. Option positions do not settle. Delivery is a one-time event that occurs when a futures or options contract expires — any remaining open position is closed at the delivery price. Delivery does not apply to perpetual or spot instruments. Both events take place at 08:00 UTC, which is why they are sometimes conflated.\n\nResults can be filtered by settlement type and timestamp. Use pagination parameters (`count` and `continuation`) to retrieve large settlement histories. This method is useful for tracking settlement history for a specific instrument.\n\n**Note on `profit_loss` and `session_profit_loss`:** Because this is a public endpoint, these fields are **platform-wide aggregates**, not per-account values. `profit_loss` is the sum of realized P\u0026L of all position holders at the settlement price. `session_profit_loss` is the sum of each holder's total session P\u0026L (realized + unrealized) across all participants.\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_last_settlements_by_instrument)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"62:T4cc,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the latest trades that have occurred for instruments in a specific currency. Returns trade details including price, amount, direction, timestamp, and trade ID for all instruments in the currency.\n\nResults can be filtered by instrument kind and trade ID range or timestamp range. Use the `count` parameter to limit the number of trades returned, and `sorting` to control the order (ascending or descending by trade ID).\n\n**Note:** For currencies with spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, this call is not supported when `kind` is `spot` or `any` — and `any` is the default when `kind` is omitted. A currency counts as routed when it is the base or the quote of a routed pair. Other kinds are unaffected. Use [Get product trades](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/api-reference/exchange-api/rest-api/products/get-product-trades) directly for full trade history by instrument.\n\n**📖 Related Articles:** \n- [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_last_trades_by_currency)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"63:T4c2,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the latest trades that have occurred for instruments in a specific currency within a specified time range. Returns trade details including price, amount, direction, timestamp, and trade ID.\n\nResults can be filtered by instrument kind. Use the `count` parameter to limit the number of trades returned, and `sorting` to control the order (ascending or descending by trade ID).\n\n**Note:** For currencies with spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, this call is not supported when `kind` is `spot` or `any` — and `any` is the default when `kind` is omitted. A currency counts as routed when it is the base or the quote of a routed pair. Other kinds are unaffected. Use [Get product trades](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/api-reference/exchange-api/rest-api/products/get-product-trades) directly for full trade history by instrument.\n\n**📖 Related Articles:** \n- [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_last_trades_by_currency_and_time)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"64:T4e3,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Enable Cancel On Disconnect for the connection. After enabling, all orders created via this connection will be automatically cancelled when the connection is closed.\n\nCancel is triggered in the following cases: when the TCP connection is properly terminated, when the connection is closed due to 10 minutes of inactivity, or when a heartbeat detects a disconnection. To reduce the inactivity timeout, consider using [public/set_heartbeat](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/session-management/public-set_heartbeat).\n\n**Note:** If the connection is gracefully closed using [private/logout](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/authentication/private-logout), cancel-on-disconnect will **not** be triggered.\n\n**Notice:** Cancel-on-Disconnect does not affect orders created by other connections - they will remain active! When change is applied on the `account` scope, then every newly opened connection will start with **active** Cancel on Disconnect.\n\n**WebSocket Only:** This method is designed exclusively for WebSocket connections. Attempting to use it via REST/HTTP will result in an error response.\n\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fenable_cancel_on_disconnect)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"65:T578,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves Market Maker Protection (MMP) configuration for an index. Returns all currently active MMP parameters for the selected index, including the interval, `frozen_time`, quantity/delta/vega limits, and `max_quote_quantity`.\n\nIf the `index_name` parameter is not provided, a list of all MMP configurations is returned. An empty list means no MMP configuration exists. This method is useful for verifying your configuration or confirming applied updates.\n\nFor Mass Quotes, specify the `mmp_group` parameter to retrieve configuration for a specific MMP group. If no group is provided, returns configuration for regular orders. Set `block_rfq` to `true` to retrieve MMP configuration for Block RFQ (requires `block_rfq:read` scope).\n\nEach entry in the response includes an `id` field (integer) that uniquely identifies the MMP group. This integer ID is the programmatic identifier for the group and can be used to reference it in contexts where the string `mmp_group` name is not accepted. Entries that have no `mmp_group` name in the response correspond to the orders MMP group (the default group).\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Market Maker Protection API Configuration](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/market-maker-protection)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read` or `block_rfq:read` (when `block_rfq` = `true`)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_mmp_config)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"66:T465,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the current state of an order identified by its order ID. The response includes order details such as status (open, filled, cancelled), filled amount, remaining amount, price, and other order properties.\n\n**Important Note for Mass Quotes:** Quote orders are order-like structures that don't fully translate to normal orders. When checking order state for quotes, the `amount` field represents the remaining amount, not the original order amount.\n\n**Note:** This method does not support the `historical` flag and only returns an order that closed within the last 30 minutes (same recency window as `historical=false`). For orders older than that, use [`private/get_order_history_by_currency`](#private-get_order_history_by_currency) or [`private/get_order_history_by_instrument`](#private-get_order_history_by_instrument) with `historical=true`.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Accessing Historical Trades and Orders Using API](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/accessing-historical-trades-orders)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_order_state)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"67:T4fa,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the state of recent orders that have a specific label. This is useful for tracking orders that share the same label, which is helpful for managing related orders.\n\nResults are filtered by currency and label. The response includes order details such as status, filled amount, remaining amount, and other order properties for all orders with the specified label.\n\n**Note:** This method does not support the `historical` flag and only returns orders that closed within the last 30 minutes (same recency window as `historical=false`). This also applies to a trigger order and the order it creates upon triggering — once either has been closed for more than 30 minutes, it will no longer appear here, even though the same `label` was carried over between them. For orders older than that, use [`private/get_order_history_by_currency`](#private-get_order_history_by_currency) or [`private/get_order_history_by_instrument`](#private-get_order_history_by_instrument) with `historical=true`.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Accessing Historical Trades and Orders Using API](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/accessing-historical-trades-orders)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_order_state_by_label)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"68:T40f,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves settlement, delivery, and bankruptcy events that have affected your account for a specific currency.\n\n**Settlement vs. delivery:** Settlement is a daily event (at 08:00 UTC) for futures and perpetual positions that converts unrealized profit and loss into realized profit and loss. Option positions do not settle. Delivery is a one-time event that occurs when a futures or options contract expires — any remaining open position is closed at the delivery price. Delivery does not apply to perpetual or spot instruments. Both events take place at 08:00 UTC, which is why they are sometimes conflated.\n\nResults can be filtered by settlement type and timestamp. Use pagination parameters (`count` and `continuation`) to retrieve large settlement histories. This data is useful for tracking account-affecting settlement events and understanding how contract expirations impact your account.\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_settlement_history_by_currency)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"69:T456,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Places buy and/or sell orders (quotes) on one or more instruments simultaneously. This method is designed for market makers who need to quote on multiple instruments efficiently.\n\n**Requirements:**\n- Cancel-on-Disconnect must be enabled (see [private/enable_cancel_on_disconnect](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/session-management/private-enable_cancel_on_disconnect)), otherwise the request will return an error.\n- This endpoint can only be used after approval from the administrators.\n\nEach quote can include both bid and ask sides, or just one side. Quotes are identified by `quote_set_id` for targeted cancellation. Use the `wait_for_response` parameter to control whether to wait for all orders to be processed before returning.\n\nAccepted quotes are published to the standard Deribit order book and are visible in the UI and non-Starbase market data feeds.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Mass Quotes Specifications](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/mass-quotes-specifications)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fmass_quote)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"6a:T457,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Moves positions from a source subaccount to a target subaccount. This operation transfers open positions between subaccounts, which is useful for rebalancing or reorganizing trading activities.\n\nPositions can be filtered by currency. The operation creates trades to transfer positions, which may affect P\u0026L and margin calculations.\n\n**Note - This method has distinct API rate limiting requirements:** \n- Sustained rate: 6 requests/minute\n- Weekly limit: 100 move_position uses per week (168 hours)\n\nFor more information, see [Rate Limits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/rate-limits).\n\n**Important:** In rare cases, the request may return an `internal_server_error`. This does not necessarily mean the operation failed entirely. Part or all of the position transfer might have still been processed successfully. Check the positions in both accounts to verify the transfer status.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Moving Positions](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/moving-positions-api)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fmove_positions)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"6b:T456,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Resets Market Maker Protection (MMP) limits for the specified currency pair or MMP group. If MMP protection has been triggered and quoting is frozen, this method allows you to manually resume quoting.\n\nIf the configured `frozen_time` has expired, the system will automatically reset MMP. If `frozen_time` is set to `0` (automatic reset disabled), you must call this method to re-enable quoting. You can also perform a manual reset during the frozen period if you want to resume quoting early.\n\nFor regular MMP (`block_rfq = false`), the `index_name` must be a specific currency pair (e.g., \"btc_usd\", \"eth_usd\"). For Block RFQ MMP (`block_rfq = true`), you can set `index_name` to `\"all\"` to reset limits across all currency pairs. Use the `mmp_group` parameter to reset limits for a specific MMP group.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Market Maker Protection API Configuration](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/market-maker-protection)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write` or `block_rfq:read_write` (when `block_rfq` = `true`)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Freset_mmp)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"6c:T7d1,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Configures Market Maker Protection (MMP) for a specific index. This method sets the monitoring window, freeze duration, and exposure limits (quantity, delta, vega, and Maximum Quote Quantity).\n\nAt least one limit parameter must be set. Maximum Quote Quantity (MQQ) is a required parameter that limits the total combined size of open MMP orders. MQQ is configured per index but enforced per side, per order book (instrument).\n\nThe `interval` parameter defines the monitoring window duration in seconds. The `frozen_time` parameter sets how long MMP remains active after being triggered. Set `frozen_time` to `0` to disable automatic reset (manual reset required).\n\nFor Mass Quotes, use the `mmp_group` parameter to configure MMP for a specific group. Set `block_rfq` to `true` to configure MMP for Block RFQ (requires `block_rfq:read_write` scope). Set `interval` to `0` to remove MMP configuration.\n\n**MMP margin reservation (MQQ-based Initial Margin)**\n\nSetting a non-zero `max_quote_quantity` immediately reserves Initial Margin equal to `MQQ × 3%`. This reservation is **unconditional and continuous** — it is held from the moment the config is active regardless of whether you have any open positions or open orders. Multiple MMP groups on the same currency pair each contribute independently. The reserved margin is visible in the **Portfolio Margin** section of the platform.\n\n**To release the reserved margin**, remove the MMP configuration entirely by calling this method with `interval = 0`. Setting `interval` to `0` deletes the configuration entry for the specified `index_name` (and `mmp_group` if provided), which immediately frees all margin reserved by that config entry.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Market Maker Protection API Configuration](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/market-maker-protection)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write` or `block_rfq:read_write` (when `block_rfq` = `true`)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fset_mmp_config)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"6d:T59e,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Adds a new address to the address book. The address book allows you to store addresses for withdrawals, along with beneficiary information for compliance purposes.\n\n**Coinbase wallet type**\n\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts the method supports network selection and CTN (Coinbase Travel Network) counterparties, and behaves differently:\n\n- Required parameters are `type` and `label`, plus one of:\n  - `address` together with `currency` and `network` (optional `tag`) — an on-chain address on the selected network, or\n  - `counterparty_id` — a CTN counterparty; `currency` is then omitted and the entry applies to all currencies.\n- `type` accepts only `withdrawal` and `transfer`.\n- Travel rule data is provided with the fields `name`, `country`, `address`, `financial_institution`, `account`, `account_location`, `entity_type` (`organization` or `individual`), `wallet_type` (`exchange` or `self_hosted`) and `is_self` instead of the legacy `beneficiary_*`, `agreed` and `personal` fields.\n- `extra_currencies` is not supported.\n- The response contains a Coinbase address book entry object, including the entry `id` which can be used instead of `address` in the other address book methods.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\n\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fadd_to_address_book)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"6e:T47f,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Creates a new deposit address for the specified currency. Each currency can have multiple deposit addresses. Use this method to generate a new address for receiving deposits.\n\n**Coinbase wallet type**\n\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts the `network` parameter is required and selects the blockchain network of the deposit address. The networks available for each currency are returned by `public/get_currencies` in the `coinbase_networks` field; a network that is not configured for the currency is rejected. An optional `label` can be provided, defaulting to `\"deposit address\"`. This method is available to institutional Coinbase accounts only.\n\n**Note:**\n\nFor Bitcoin, a new address can be generated every 24 hours.\n\nFor ERC20, Solana and XRP only one address can be generated.\n\n**Note:**\n\nIf an ERC20 address is generated, this address will be automatically added for every asset that uses ERC20 addresses.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Deposits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-deposits-api)\n\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcreate_deposit_address)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"6f:T412,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the address book entries of the given type. Returns all saved addresses that can be used for withdrawals, along with their labels and beneficiary information if available.\n\n**Coinbase wallet type**\n\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts `currency` accepts any portfolio currency or `\"all\"`, and `type` accepts `withdrawal`, `transfer` or `deposit` (deposit addresses created via `private/create_deposit_address`). The returned entries are Coinbase address book entry objects: they include the entry `id` (usable instead of `address` in the other address book methods), `kind` (`onchain` or `ctn`), `network`, `network_display_name`, `tag` and the Coinbase travel rule fields (`name`, `country`, `financial_institution`, `account`, `account_location`, `entity_type`, `wallet_type`, `is_self`) when set.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\n\n**Scope:** `wallet:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_address_book)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"70:T50f,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Updates beneficiary information for an address in the address book. This method allows you to add or modify beneficiary details required for compliance purposes when making withdrawals to certain addresses.\n\n**Coinbase wallet type**\n\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts the method behaves differently:\n\n- Required parameters are `currency` (portfolio currencies or `\"all\"`) and `type`, plus one of `address` or `id` (the entry identifier returned by `private/get_address_book`). Use `network` and `tag` together with `address` to disambiguate entries sharing the same address.\n- `type` accepts only `withdrawal` and `transfer`.\n- `label` is optional.\n- Travel rule data is provided with the fields `name`, `country`, `address`, `financial_institution`, `account`, `account_location`, `entity_type` (`organization` or `individual`), `wallet_type` (`exchange` or `self_hosted`) and `is_self` instead of the legacy `beneficiary_*`, `agreed` and `personal` fields.\n- The response contains the updated Coinbase address book entry object instead of `\"ok\"`.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\n\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fupdate_in_address_book)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"71:T8ed,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Creates a new withdrawal request. This method allows you to withdraw funds from your account to an external address. The withdrawal can be configured with priority settings and must use an address from your address book.\n\n**Withdrawal Checks \u0026 Balance Updates**\n\nWithdrawal funds are checked twice: when a user requests a withdrawal and again when they confirm it via the email link. If available funds decrease between these steps, the withdrawal may be rejected.\n\nA withdrawal may also be rejected if the on-chain fee increases between the request and confirmation.\n\nThe withdrawal amount is deducted only after all checks pass and the transaction is scheduled. The web-interface Withdrawal tab displays all withdrawals regardless of their status (pending, cancelled, rejected, or completed).\n\n**Coinbase wallet type**\n\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts the method supports network selection and CTN (Coinbase Travel Network) counterparties, and behaves differently:\n\n- Required parameters are `currency` (any portfolio currency) and `amount`, plus one of `address` or `id` (the address book entry identifier returned by `private/get_address_book`).\n- When `address` is an on-chain address, pass `network` (and `tag` when applicable) to identify the address book entry. For a CTN withdrawal, pass the CTN counterparty identifier of the entry as `address`.\n- `priority` and `nonce` are not supported. Use `private/coinbase/estimate_withdrawal_fee` to estimate the network fee.\n- Subaccounts can withdraw only when enabled by the main account via `private/set_coinbase_subaccount_withdrawals_allowed`.\n- The response is a Coinbase withdrawal object instead of the legacy withdrawal object. Its `state` is one of `prepared`, `awaiting_second_email`, `unconfirmed`, `completed` or `cancelled`; withdrawals to an address that is not trusted start as `prepared` and require email confirmation, in which case `transfer_idem` is absent until the withdrawal is submitted to the custodian. Fields that are not set are omitted from the response.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\n\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write` and mainaccount\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fwithdraw)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"72:T4b0,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Real-time order book updates for a specific instrument.\n\n- The first notification contains a full snapshot of the book (bids and asks for **all price levels** — no depth limit).\n- Subsequent notifications contain only incremental changes to individual price levels.\n- Updates are tuples in the form `[action, price, amount]`, where `action` is one of: `new`, `change`, `delete`.\n\nEach notification includes a `change_id`. Every message except the first also contains `prev_change_id`. If `prev_change_id` equals the `change_id` of the previous message, it indicates that no messages were missed.\n\nFor Starbase-routed instruments, the published price levels include accepted mass-quote liquidity.\n\n**Depth:** This channel delivers the complete order book with no depth restriction. If you need a depth-limited, price-grouped snapshot, use `book.{instrument_name}.{group}.{depth}.{interval}` instead.\n\n**Units:** For perpetuals and futures, `amount` is in USD units. For options, `amount` is in the corresponding cryptocurrency contracts (e.g., BTC or ETH).\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"73:T6a2,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Real-time ticker data providing comprehensive market information for the specified instrument.\n\nThis subscription delivers key market metrics including:\n\n- **Price data:** Best bid/ask prices and amounts, last trade price, mark price, index price, settlement price, and estimated delivery price\n- **Market statistics:** 24-hour volume (in base currency and USD for futures), high/low prices, price change percentage, and open interest\n- **Order book state:** Current state of the instrument (open, settlement, delivered, inactive, locked, halted, or archivized)\n- **Price limits:** Minimum and maximum price constraints for order placement\n- **Options-specific data:** Implied volatility (bid/ask/mark IV), Greeks (delta, gamma, theta, vega, rho), underlying price, and interest rate\n- **Perpetual-specific data:** Current funding rate and 8-hour funding rate\n- **Futures-specific data:** Interest value and delivery price\n\nThe `interval` parameter controls the frequency of updates: `raw` (finest granularity - events aggregated over a 1 millisecond interval, authorized users only), `100ms` (aggregated every 100 milliseconds), or `agg2` (aggregated every 2 seconds).\n\nThis is the recommended method for real-time market data updates, as it provides efficient push-based notifications instead of requiring polling.\n\n**Note:** For spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, `volume_notional` and `volume_usd` are omitted from `stats`.\n\n**📖 Related Articles:** \n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\n- [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"74:T4d5,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Real-time notifications for Market Maker Protection (MMP) triggers. This subscription provides feedback when MMP protection is activated for a given index, enabling clients to react promptly when protection is triggered.\n\nUpon MMP being triggered for a given index, the client will receive a trigger notification containing:\n\n- **frozen_until**: Unix timestamp in milliseconds indicating until when the MMP is active (orders remain blocked). If `frozen_until: 0`, it means MMP will remain active until manually reset using the `private/reset_mmp` method.\n- **index_name**: Index identifier of derivative instrument on the platform. For Block RFQ MMP, this will be \"all\" when triggered by trade count limit.\n- **mmp_group**: Triggered MMP group (optional, appears only for Mass Quote orders trigger)\n- **block_rfq**: If true, indicates that the MMP trigger is for Block RFQ. Block RFQ MMP triggers are completely separate from normal order/quote MMP triggers.\n\nThis notification allows the client to track MMP state per index and avoid submitting new orders that would be rejected due to ongoing MMP freeze.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Market Maker Protection API Configuration](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/market-maker-protection)\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"75:T543,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Real-time notifications for user portfolio information. This subscription provides comprehensive account and portfolio data for the specified currency, including balances, margins, profit and loss, and Greeks.\n\nEach notification includes:\n\n- **Account balances:** Current balance, equity, margin balance, available funds, and available withdrawal funds\n- **Margin information:** Initial margin, maintenance margin, and projected margins\n- **Profit and Loss:** Total P\u0026L, session unrealized P\u0026L (UPL), session realized P\u0026L (RPL), and separate P\u0026L for options and futures\n- **Options Greeks:** Delta, gamma, theta, vega, and options value, with per-index mappings\n- **Position data:** Delta total, projected delta total, and delta total map per index\n- **Account settings:** Portfolio margining status, cross collateral status, and margin model\n- **Cross collateral data:** Total equity, margins, and delta in USD (when cross collateral is enabled)\n- **Additional reserves:** Fee balance and additional reserve information\n\nWhen cross collateral is enabled, aggregated values are calculated by converting the sum of each cross collateral currency's value to the given currency, using each cross collateral currency's index.\n\nSubscribe to a specific currency (BTC, ETH, USDC, USDT, etc.) or use `any` to receive portfolio updates for all currencies.\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"76:T5b1,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Notifications about the authenticated account's own liquidation, auto-deleveraging (ADL), and LSP (Liquidity Support Program) activity — both as the account being liquidated/deleveraged and, for ADL, as a counterparty receiving a deleveraged position.\n\nThis includes the liquidated account's own transfer events (`lsp_transfer`, `adl_transfer`) as well as `adl_transfer_received` for any account that absorbs a position via ADL. See `user.lsp` for the additional notifications sent to the LSP participant *receiving* an assigned position (enable/disable and configuration changes).\n\nA successful `lsp_transfer` or `adl_transfer` is also delivered on the [Starbase FIX Drop Copy](https://docs.deribit.com/starbase/fix-drop-copy-api) session of the Starbase Member that owns that portfolio, as a TradeCaptureReport (`35=AE`) with TradeType (828) `3`. On that report TransferReason (830) is `LIQUIDATED`. The receiving side's report has TransferReason (830) `ASSIGNED` and LiquidationMechanism (8002) `LSP` or `ADL`. Started/completed states and failed assignment attempts are WebSocket-only. Only a position move whose reason is admin is omitted from Drop Copy.\n\nEvery notification includes a `state` field identifying the stage of the process — see the notification schema for the full list of states and which fields accompany each.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"77:T5f3,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Notifications for an LSP (Liquidity Support Program) participant subaccount: assignment attempts (successful or failed), enable/disable state changes, and effective configuration changes.\n\nSubscribe to this channel with an API key belonging to the LSP participant subaccount itself. See `user.liquidation` for the notification sent to the liquidated (source) user whose position was transferred.\n\nA **successful** assignment is also delivered on the [Starbase FIX Drop Copy](https://docs.deribit.com/starbase/fix-drop-copy-api) session of the Starbase Member that owns that portfolio: a TradeCaptureReport (`35=AE`) with TradeType (828) `3` (position move), TransferReason (830) `ASSIGNED`, and LiquidationMechanism (8002) `LSP`. TrdMatchID (880) on that report is `starbase_match_id` on the successful `transfer` notification. You do not need this WebSocket channel to receive successful assignments if that Member's Drop Copy session already covers the portfolio.\n\nThis channel is still required for what Drop Copy does not send: a failed assignment attempt (`success: false`), and `enabled`, `disabled`, and `configuration_changed`. Only a position move whose reason is admin is omitted from Drop Copy. LSP and ADL assignments are sent.\n\nEvery notification includes a `type` field identifying the event kind — see the notification schema for the full list of types and which fields accompany each.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"78:T7ca,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Real-time notifications for Block RFQs (Request for Quotes) that are available for the subscribed maker to respond to.\n\nThis subscription notifies makers when new Block RFQs are created in the specified currency (or all currencies if `any` is used) that they can potentially quote on. Each notification includes:\n\n- **RFQ identification:** Unique Block RFQ ID, creation timestamp, and expiration timestamp\n- **RFQ structure:** Multi-leg trade structure with instrument names, directions (buy/sell), and ratios for each leg\n- **Trade parameters:** Total amount (multiplied by leg ratios determines trade size), minimum trade amount, and optional combo identifier\n- **Hedge information:** Optional hedge leg details including instrument, direction, amount, and price\n- **RFQ state:** Current state (open, filled, cancelled, or expired)\n- **Counterparty information:** Taker rating, taker alias (if disclosed), and disclosure status\n- **Execution details:** For filled RFQs, includes trade information with prices, amounts, directions, and maker aliases\n- **Index prices:** List of index prices for underlying instruments at trade execution time (for filled RFQs)\n- **Rating information:** Whether the RFQ is included in taker rating calculation (for closed RFQs)\n\nMakers can subscribe to specific currencies (BTC, ETH, USDC, USDT) or use `any` to receive notifications for all supported currencies. This enables makers to monitor incoming RFQ opportunities and respond with competitive quotes in a timely manner.\n\n**Scope required:** `block_rfq:read`\n\n**Trade cross-posting:** When a Block RFQ is filled, the resulting trades are also delivered through the `user.trades.{instrument_name}.{interval}` and `user.trades.{kind}.{currency}.{interval}` channels. Those notifications include `block_rfq_id`, `block_trade_id`, and — for the maker side — `block_rfq_quote_id`.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"79:T5cc,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Returns all currently-open orders belonging to the authenticated portfolio. Orders are returned regardless of instrument or order type; filtering by instrument kind and order type is not currently supported.\n\nEach order includes `instrument_id`, `product_group`, and the `post_only`, `reject_post_only`, and `reduce_only` flags. `instrument_id` is the numeric instrument id. `product_group` is the Starbase routing group (`BTC`, `ETH`, `TIER_2`, or `TIER_3`). `post_only` and `reject_post_only` correspond to the SBE `postOnly` and `postOnlyReject` bits and are mutually exclusive. `reduce_only` reflects per-order reduce-only from [classic JSON-RPC](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/json-rpc-overview) or FIX (it cannot be set per order in SBE).\n\nThe portfolio is resolved from the authenticated session. There is no parameter to query another portfolio's orders. MMP-flagged orders are visible via this endpoint. Orders placed via Mass Quote (MassQuoteRequest) are included.\n\nThis endpoint is rate-limited to 10 requests per minute per portfolio on each REST gateway. The A and B gateways enforce this cap independently. Exceeding the limit returns HTTP 429. Because this limit is heavily restrictive relative to typical order-book activity, this endpoint is best used for periodic reconciliation rather than to maintain live order state. To track open orders in real time, maintain a dedicated [FIX Drop Copy](/starbase/fix-drop-copy-api) session instead of polling this endpoint."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"7a:T4c8,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Returns the effective position (\"risk\") limits for the authenticated portfolio, one entry per underlying (currency pair).\n\nEach numeric field is resolved per field: a portfolio override wins when that field is set, otherwise the currency-pair default is used. A field unset at both levels is omitted. `-1` means the limit is explicitly unlimited (distinct from unset). The call is read-only and does not change limits.\n\nOnly underlyings that have a currency-pair default or an override for this portfolio are included. Overrides that belong to other portfolios do not create an entry.\n\nPass `currency` to select one underlying. The value is the currency-pair name returned in `currency` (for example `BTC_USDC`). Matching is case-insensitive and ignores separators, so `btc-usdc` and `BTCUSDC` resolve to the same pair. An unknown name returns HTTP 400. A known pair with no configured limit for this portfolio returns an empty list.\n\nThe portfolio is resolved from the authenticated session. There is no parameter to query another portfolio.\n\nThis endpoint is rate-limited to 1 request per minute per portfolio on each REST gateway. The A and B gateways enforce this cap independently. Exceeding the limit returns HTTP 429."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"7b:T6a0,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Returns the list of tradeable instruments, including `index_id` and `product_group`, optionally filtered by base currency, instrument kind, expiration status, instrument id, product group, and lifecycle state.\n\nThis endpoint requires no authentication, but it is served by the Starbase REST gateway and is reachable only through hosted colocation, a cross-connect, or AWS Private Link. The internet-accessible [classic JSON-RPC](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/json-rpc-overview) `public/get_instruments` method also documents `index_id` and `product_group`; backend rollout of those fields may temporarily differ between the two endpoints.\n\nFilter semantics (supplied filters are combined):\n- `currency` filters by the **base** currency of the instrument's currency pair (case-insensitive exact match, for example `BTC` or `ETH`). Omit `currency` to return instruments for every base currency. A value that is not a listed base currency, including `any`, matches no instrument: the call succeeds and `result` is an empty array. `any` is compared as a base-currency name.\n- `kind` filters by instrument type (case-insensitive match against the `kind` value enum).\n- `expired = true` returns only instruments whose `expiration_timestamp` is in the past; `expired = false` returns only non-expired instruments. Omit the parameter to get both.\n- `instrument_id` returns the instrument with that numeric id.\n- `product_group` filters by Starbase product group (case-insensitive match against `BTC`, `ETH`, `TIER_2`, `TIER_3`).\n- `state` filters by instrument lifecycle state (case-insensitive). Values match SBE `InstrumentStatus`: `open`, `inactive`, `settlement`, `delivered`, `locked`, `halted`."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"7c:T6e6,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieve an OAuth access token, to be used for authentication of 'private' requests.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Authentication](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/authentication)\n\n**Authentication Methods:**\n\nThree methods of authentication are supported:\n\n\n- ``client_credentials`` - Using the client id and client secret that can be found on the API page on the website. This is the simplest method, suitable for server-to-server applications and quick setup.\n\n- ``client_signature`` - Enhanced security method that uses a cryptographic signature instead of sending the client secret directly. You generate an HMAC-SHA256 signature of a string containing a timestamp, a random nonce, and optional data, using your Client Secret as the key. This method requires `` `client_id` ``, `` `timestamp` `` (current time in milliseconds), `` `nonce` ``, `` `signature` ``, and optionally a `` `data` `` field. Deribit verifies the signature instead of requiring the raw secret. Best for enhanced security, asymmetric key pairs, and avoiding secret transmission. See the [Client Signature (WebSocket) guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/authentication#client-signature-websocket) for detailed signature calculation instructions.\n\n- ``refresh_token`` - Using a refresh token that was received from an earlier invocation. This allows you to obtain a new access token without re-supplying your Client ID and Client Secret. Best for long-lived sessions, token renewal, and avoiding re-authentication.\n\n\n**Response:**\n\nThe response will contain an access token, expiration period (number of seconds that the token is valid) and a refresh token that can be used to get a new set of tokens.\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fauth)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"7d:T741,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Gracefully terminate the current WebSocket connection and optionally invalidate all tokens associated with the session.\n\nThis method provides a clean way to close WebSocket connections while preserving active orders when [**Cancel On Disconnect (COD)**](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/session-management/private-enable_cancel_on_disconnect) is enabled.\n\n**Use Cases:**\n\n- **Clean Shutdown:** Properly close WebSocket connections during application shutdown or restart\n- **Order Preservation:** Close connections without triggering order cancellations when COD is enabled\n- **Session Management:** Invalidate tokens to ensure security when closing connections\n- **Maintenance Operations:** Temporarily disconnect for system maintenance without affecting trading positions\n\n**Cancel On Disconnect (COD) Behavior:**\n\nWhen Cancel On Disconnect is enabled for your connection, this method provides a safe way to close the connection without triggering automatic order cancellations. This is different from other disconnection scenarios:\n\n- **Graceful logout** (this method): Orders are **NOT cancelled**, even if COD is enabled\n- **Unexpected disconnection:** Orders are **cancelled** if COD is enabled\n- **Inactivity timeout:** Orders are **cancelled** if COD is enabled\n- **Heartbeat failure:** Orders are **cancelled** if COD is enabled\n\nThis distinction allows you to perform planned disconnections (e.g., for maintenance, updates, or reconnection) while preserving your active orders.\n\n**WebSocket Only:**\n\nThis method is designed exclusively for WebSocket connections. Attempting to use it via REST/HTTP will result in a 400 error response.\n\n**Note:** This method has no response. The WebSocket connection is closed immediately after the request is processed.\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Flogout)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"7e:T41b,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the account summary for a specific currency. The summary includes cash `balance`, `equity`, `margin_balance`, `available_funds`, `available_withdrawal_funds`, initial/maintenance margin, session and total PnL, options greeks, and related fields.\n\nKey relationships (standard margin): `equity = balance + futures session PnL + options_value`, `margin_balance = equity - options_value`, `available_funds = max(0, margin_balance - initial_margin)`. Under portfolio margin, `margin_balance` equals `equity`. Session PnL fields reset at daily settlement; `total_pl` does not.\n\nTo retrieve the summary for a specific subaccount, use the `subaccount_id` parameter. When the `extended` parameter is set to `true`, additional account details such as account ID, username, email, and account type are included.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\n\n**Scope:** `account:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_account_summary)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"7f:Tb1c,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves a detailed transaction log for the authenticated account. The log includes all account activities such as trades, deposits, withdrawals, transfers, fees, and other balance-affecting operations.\n\nResults can be filtered by currency, time range, and `query` keywords. `start_timestamp` must not exceed `end_timestamp`; both values are clamped to the current time, so a future `end_timestamp` is treated as now. The matching window includes `end_timestamp`.\n\n`count` defaults to 100 and is capped at 1000. Pass `continuation` (a log id from the previous response) to fetch the next older page. `continuation` is `null` when there are no more entries.\n\nTo retrieve transactions for a specific subaccount, pass `subaccount_id` from the main account. Removed subaccounts are accepted. The authenticated user id is always applied as a filter.\n\nTrade entries executed in Starbase include `starbase_match_id`, `starbase_order_id`, and `starbase_timestamp`. Those fields are omitted on spot trades. Block RFQ allocations appear as `type` `trade allocation` rather than `trade`.\n\nWhen an option expires out of the money, the transaction log type is `expiry`. As there is nothing to settle into futures in this case, this remains the only entry in the transaction log for that expiration. In-the-money expiries use `assignment` or `exercise`, and may be followed by a `future creation` entry.\n\nLSP and ADL position moves are logged as `type` `LSP transfer` / `ADL transfer`. Both the liquidated/deleveraged account and the receiving account get that same `type`. A separate optional `role` field (`source` or `destination`) is present on those transfer entries — and also on `liquidation transfer` and `position move` — and is omitted on all other types, including `LSP commission` / `ADL commission` and ordinary `trade`s. Do not confuse `role` with `user_role` (`maker` / `taker`) on trades.\n\nCorrection entries may include a `related` array of the original log entries they correct. While the platform is starting, the method may return `temporarily_unavailable`.\n\n**History Limit:** This API method has **no time limit** - users can query transaction history back to account creation. Note that the CSV export feature available on the website is year-limited to 2023.\n\n**Note - This method has distinct API rate limiting requirements:** Sustained rate: 1 request/second. For more information, see [Rate Limits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/rate-limits).\n\n**📖 Related Support Article:** [Transaction log](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/25944587269021-Transaction-log)\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\n\n**Scope:** `account:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_transaction_log)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"80:T41d,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Approves a pending block trade. `nonce` and `timestamp` are used to identify the block trade while `role` should be opposite to the trading counterparty.\n\nUse [private/get_block_trade_requests](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-get_block_trade_requests) to retrieve pending block trades that require approval.\n\nTo use the block trade approval feature, an [additional API key setting feature](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key#block-trade-approval-feature) called `enabled_features: block_trade_approval` is required. This key has to be given to the broker/registered partner who performs the trades on behalf of the user for the feature to be active. If the user wants to approve the trade, they must approve it from a different API key that doesn't have this feature enabled.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\n\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fapprove_block_trade)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"81:T629,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Executes a block trade. This is the second step in the block trade workflow - the second party calls this method with the signature received from the first party to execute the trade.\n\nThe whole request must be exactly the same as in [private/verify_block_trade](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-verify_block_trade), only the `role` field should be set appropriately - this means that both sides have to agree on the same `timestamp`, `nonce`, and `trades` fields, and the server will ensure that the `role` field is different between sides (each party accepts their own role).\n\nUsing the same `timestamp` and `nonce` by both sides in [private/verify_block_trade](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-verify_block_trade) ensures that even if unintentionally both sides execute the given block trade with a valid `counterparty_signature`, the block trade will be executed only once.\n\n**Note:** In the API, the `direction` field is always expressed from the maker's perspective. This means that when you accept a block trade as a taker, the direction shown in the API represents the opposite side of your trade. For example, if you are buying puts as a taker, the API will show the operation as a \"sell put\" (maker's perspective), and you will be verifying and accepting a \"sell put\" block trade.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\n\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fexecute_block_trade)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"82:T4db,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Provides a list of block trade requests including pending approvals, declined trades, and expired trades. `timestamp` and `nonce` received in response can be used with [private/approve_block_trade](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-approve_block_trade) or [private/reject_block_trade](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-reject_block_trade) to approve or reject the pending block trade.\n\nTo use the block trade approval feature, an [additional API key setting feature](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key#block-trade-approval-feature) called `enabled_features: block_trade_approval` is required. This key has to be given to the broker/registered partner who performs the trades on behalf of the user for the feature to be active. If the user wants to approve the trade, they must approve it from a different API key that doesn't have this feature enabled.\n\nOnly broker clients can use `broker_code` to query for their broker block trade requests.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\n\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_block_trade_requests)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"83:T587,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"**Broker Method** Returns a list of clients registered under the broker account. Each client record includes:\n\n- `client_id` — a numeric identifier that groups one or more linked users under a single client name. Use this value in other Broker Voice API calls (e.g. `private/execute_broker_trade`) to identify the client group.\n- `links` — an array of individual user connections belonging to that client. Each link contains a `client_link_id` that uniquely identifies a single user within the client group.\n\n**How to obtain `client_id` and `client_link_id`**\n\nCall this endpoint without parameters to retrieve all clients. Locate the client by name or company, read `client_id` from the top-level object, and read `client_link_id` from the relevant entry in the `links` array. Use these two values together in subsequent Broker Voice API calls to specify which user within a client should be the counterparty.\n\nA link `state` of `connected` means the user has accepted the broker invitation and is ready to trade. Links in `pending` state have not yet been accepted; links in `rejected` state are inactive.\n\nOptionally filter by a specific `client_id` to return only that client's record, or set `include_subaccounts` to `true` to include clients managed by broker sub-accounts.\n\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_broker_clients)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"84:T41b,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Rejects a pending block trade. `nonce` and `timestamp` are used to identify the block trade while `role` should be opposite to the trading counterparty.\n\nUse [private/get_block_trade_requests](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-get_block_trade_requests) to retrieve pending block trades that require approval.\n\nTo use the block trade approval feature, an [additional API key setting feature](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key#block-trade-approval-feature) called `enabled_features: block_trade_approval` is required. This key has to be given to the broker/registered partner who performs the trades on behalf of the user for the feature to be active. If the user wants to approve the trade, they must approve it from a different API key that doesn't have this feature enabled.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\n\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Freject_block_trade)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"85:T4f9,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves **active** combos for the specified settlement `currency` (`\"any\"` for every currency). Inactive, closed, and archivized combos are omitted. There is no `state` parameter on this method.\n\nEach result is a combo object (`id`, `legs`, `state`, timestamps, `instrument_id`), not the full instrument spec from `public/get_instrument`. Combo `state` here is the combo-book state (`active`), which is not the same as the instrument order-book `state`.\n\nThis is not the same list as `public/get_instruments` with `kind=future_combo` or `kind=option_combo`, which returns visible combo **instruments** (including `locked` / `halted` / `settlement` books) and omits inactive combos.\n\nFor IDs including inactive combos, use [public/get_combo_ids](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/combo-books/public-get_combo_ids). For one combo, use [public/get_combo_details](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/combo-books/public-get_combo_details). Expired or archivized combo names are looked up with `public/get_instrument`, not this method.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_combos)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"86:T40b,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the LSP (Liquidity Support Program) participant configuration for the authenticated account.\n\nLSP participants are designated subaccounts that receive assigned positions from liquidated users as an alternative to auto-deleveraging (ADL). This method must be called with an API key belonging to the LSP participant subaccount itself — it returns an error if the authenticated account has no LSP configuration.\n\nThe response includes the participant's enable/disable state and any per-cooldown-group limit overrides. When the platform-side participant position lock is switched on, enrolling a subaccount as an LSP participant also locks it to reduce-only trading; this lock is off by default, so participation does not by itself restrict the subaccount to reduce-only.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\n\n**Scope:** `account:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_lsp_participant_config)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"87:T414,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves per-cooldown-group assignment usage for all LSP (Liquidity Support Program) participant subaccounts configured under the authenticated main account.\n\nMust be called with an API key belonging to the main account — returns an error if called from a subaccount. Use the `user_id` parameter to filter the result down to a single participant.\n\nAs with `private/get_lsp_usage`, each participant's group usage reports `pct` (limit, as a percentage of equity), `used` (USD within the current fixed window — flat until the window closes, then resets to `0` in one step), and `cooldown_start`/`cooldown_end` (the current window's timing) — remaining capacity is not computed for you and the leverage-derived cap applied at assignment time is not exposed on any user-facing endpoint.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\n\n**Scope:** `account:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_lsp_participants_usage)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"88:T53e,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the current per-cooldown-group assignment usage for the authenticated LSP (Liquidity Support Program) participant subaccount within its current fixed cooldown window.\n\nMust be called with an API key belonging to the LSP participant subaccount itself — returns an error if the authenticated account is not an LSP participant.\n\nInstruments are bucketed into one of 7 cooldown groups (6 crypto tiers plus a real-world-asset group); each group has its own limit (`pct`, as a percentage of the participant's equity), fixed-window usage (`used`, in USD — this does not decay smoothly; it stays flat until the window closes at `cooldown_end`, then resets to `0` in one step), and the window's timing (`cooldown_start`/`cooldown_end`). Neither the absolute limit nor the remaining capacity is computed for you — derive it from `pct`, `used`, and the participant's own equity from `private/get_account_summary`. Even a self-computed remaining-capacity figure won't reflect the additional margin/leverage-derived cap applied at assignment time, which isn't exposed on any user-facing endpoint.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\n\n**Scope:** `account:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_lsp_usage)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"89:T4b0,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the contract size (also known as contract multiplier) for a given instrument. The contract size is the value of one contract, expressed in the same unit as the order amount: USD for inverse (reversed) futures and perpetuals, and the base currency coin for options, spots, and linear futures and perpetuals.\n\nThis value is essential for calculating position values, margin requirements, and P\u0026L calculations. Different instruments may have different contract sizes.\n\nThis is not the quantity increment used to validate order amounts. Use `min_trade_amount` from [public/get_instrument](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/market-data/public-get_instrument) / [public/get_instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/market-data/public-get_instruments). On Starbase the same increment is named `qty_tick_size`. `contract_size` and `min_trade_amount` are not guaranteed to match.\n\nLooks up by `instrument_name`, including combo IDs and expired or archivized instruments. Unknown names fail with `instrument not found`. The same field is included on the `public/get_instrument` object.\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_contract_size)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8a:T4b5,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves expiration **labels** for listed futures and options. Values are instrument-style date strings such as `21SEP24`, or `PERPETUAL` for perpetuals — not Unix timestamps. Daily 08:00 UTC expirations are date-only; other expiration times include hour and minute.\n\nSpots and combos are not included, even when `kind` is omitted or `\"any\"`.\n\n`currency` is a settlement currency, `\"any\"`, or `\"grouped\"`:\n- `\"any\"` — a flat map keyed by `future` / `option` (dates merged across currencies). This is the shape in the example.\n- a named currency — `{ \"\u003ccurrency\u003e\": { \"future\": [...], \"option\": [...] } }` with a lowercase currency key (for example `btc`).\n- `\"grouped\"` — the same nested shape for every tradable settlement currency.\n\nIf `currency` is omitted, `currency_pair` is used (default: all pairs). When `currency` is set, `currency_pair` is ignored. `kind` defaults to `\"any\"` (`future` and `option`); `\"spot\"`, `\"future_combo\"`, and `\"option_combo\"` are not useful filters here.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_expirations)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8b:T5aa,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves detailed information about a specific instrument, including instrument specifications, contract details, tick size, settlement currency, expiration date (for futures and options), strike price (for options), underlying type, and other instrument parameters.\n\nLooks up by `instrument_name`, including combo IDs and expired or archivized instruments that `public/get_instruments` no longer lists. Unknown names fail with `instrument not found`. For live combo legs and combo-book state, use `public/get_combo_details` / `public/get_combos` instead of this method.\n\n`is_active` is true while the order book is visible (`open`, `settlement`, `locked`, or `halted`). It is not the same as tradable: only `state` `open` accepts new orders. After delivery the book becomes `delivered` (`is_active` false) and is later archivized.\n\nSpot instruments omit `settlement_currency` and `settlement_period`. Spot routed to Coinbase Exchange also omit block-trade fields and include `is_cbe_routed` / `is_csr` (present only when `true`). Futures include `max_leverage` and `max_non_default_leverage`. Some USDC spot pairs that support margin loans also include `max_leverage`. Perpetuals still have `expiration_timestamp`.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_instrument)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8c:Tac5,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves trading instruments, filtered by `currency` and optional `kind`. Responses are cached for about 1 minute and can be stale relative to live book state.\n\n**Note - This method has distinct API rate limiting requirements:** Sustained rate: 1 request/second. To avoid rate limits, we recommend using either the REST requests for server-cached data or the WebSocket subscription to [instrument_state.{kind}.{currency}](https://docs.deribit.com/subscriptions/market-data/instrumentstatekindcurrency) for real-time updates. For more information, see [Rate Limits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/rate-limits).\n\nWith `expired=false` (default) the list is not limited to tradable books. It includes visible instruments (`open`, `settlement`, `locked`, `halted`) plus inactive non-combo instruments. Inactive combos are omitted; combo kinds (`future_combo`, `option_combo`) return only visible books. `is_active` can therefore be `false` on this default list. Only `state` `open` accepts new orders.\n\nWith `expired=true` the list is instruments still in the live table with `state` `delivered` — recently expired, not archivized. Older expired or archivized names are looked up with `public/get_instrument`, not this method.\n\n`currency` matches derivatives by settlement currency: inverse (reversed) contracts settle in the base coin (`BTC` for BTC-PERPETUAL), linear contracts typically settle in the quote coin (`USDC` for BTC_USDC-PERPETUAL). `currency=any` returns every settlement currency.\n\nSpot matching is different. A spot's settlement field is the pair symbol (for example `BTC_USDC`), not `BTC` or `USDC`. When `expired=false` and `kind` is omitted/`any` for a specific currency, the response unions (1) derivatives with that settlement currency and (2) spots whose base or quote is that currency. `kind=spot` with a specific currency matches spots on either side of the pair. `expired=true` does not apply that extra spot union, so recently delivered spots are not returned under `currency=BTC`.\n\nResults are sorted with perpetuals first, then by expiration. Each instrument includes `underlying_type`. Spot routed to Coinbase Exchange includes `is_cbe_routed` / `is_csr`. Set `extended=true` for extra commission and (on futures) margin/perpetual fields that `public/get_instrument` does not return.\n\n**📖 Related Articles:**\n- [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\n- [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_instruments)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8d:T540,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves historical settlement, delivery, and bankruptcy events from all instruments within a given currency.\n\n**Settlement vs. delivery:** Settlement is a daily event (at 08:00 UTC) for futures and perpetual positions that converts unrealized profit and loss into realized profit and loss. Option positions do not settle. Delivery is a one-time event that occurs when a futures or options contract expires — any remaining open position is closed at the delivery price. Delivery does not apply to perpetual or spot instruments. Both events take place at 08:00 UTC, which is why they are sometimes conflated.\n\nResults can be filtered by settlement type and timestamp. Use pagination parameters (`count` and `continuation`) to retrieve large settlement histories. This data is useful for analyzing historical contract settlements and understanding market events.\n\n**Note on `profit_loss` and `session_profit_loss`:** Because this is a public endpoint, these fields are **platform-wide aggregates**, not per-account values. `profit_loss` is the sum of realized P\u0026L of all position holders at the settlement price. `session_profit_loss` is the sum of each holder's total session P\u0026L (realized + unrealized) across all participants.\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_last_settlements_by_currency)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8e:T51d,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves historical settlement, delivery, and bankruptcy events for a specific instrument.\n\n**Settlement vs. delivery:** Settlement is a daily event (at 08:00 UTC) for futures and perpetual positions that converts unrealized profit and loss into realized profit and loss. Option positions do not settle. Delivery is a one-time event that occurs when a futures or options contract expires — any remaining open position is closed at the delivery price. Delivery does not apply to perpetual or spot instruments. Both events take place at 08:00 UTC, which is why they are sometimes conflated.\n\nResults can be filtered by settlement type and timestamp. Use pagination parameters (`count` and `continuation`) to retrieve large settlement histories. This method is useful for tracking settlement history for a specific instrument.\n\n**Note on `profit_loss` and `session_profit_loss`:** Because this is a public endpoint, these fields are **platform-wide aggregates**, not per-account values. `profit_loss` is the sum of realized P\u0026L of all position holders at the settlement price. `session_profit_loss` is the sum of each holder's total session P\u0026L (realized + unrealized) across all participants.\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_last_settlements_by_instrument)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8f:T4cc,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the latest trades that have occurred for instruments in a specific currency. Returns trade details including price, amount, direction, timestamp, and trade ID for all instruments in the currency.\n\nResults can be filtered by instrument kind and trade ID range or timestamp range. Use the `count` parameter to limit the number of trades returned, and `sorting` to control the order (ascending or descending by trade ID).\n\n**Note:** For currencies with spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, this call is not supported when `kind` is `spot` or `any` — and `any` is the default when `kind` is omitted. A currency counts as routed when it is the base or the quote of a routed pair. Other kinds are unaffected. Use [Get product trades](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/api-reference/exchange-api/rest-api/products/get-product-trades) directly for full trade history by instrument.\n\n**📖 Related Articles:** \n- [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_last_trades_by_currency)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"90:T4c2,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the latest trades that have occurred for instruments in a specific currency within a specified time range. Returns trade details including price, amount, direction, timestamp, and trade ID.\n\nResults can be filtered by instrument kind. Use the `count` parameter to limit the number of trades returned, and `sorting` to control the order (ascending or descending by trade ID).\n\n**Note:** For currencies with spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, this call is not supported when `kind` is `spot` or `any` — and `any` is the default when `kind` is omitted. A currency counts as routed when it is the base or the quote of a routed pair. Other kinds are unaffected. Use [Get product trades](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/api-reference/exchange-api/rest-api/products/get-product-trades) directly for full trade history by instrument.\n\n**📖 Related Articles:** \n- [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_last_trades_by_currency_and_time)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"91:T4e3,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Enable Cancel On Disconnect for the connection. After enabling, all orders created via this connection will be automatically cancelled when the connection is closed.\n\nCancel is triggered in the following cases: when the TCP connection is properly terminated, when the connection is closed due to 10 minutes of inactivity, or when a heartbeat detects a disconnection. To reduce the inactivity timeout, consider using [public/set_heartbeat](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/session-management/public-set_heartbeat).\n\n**Note:** If the connection is gracefully closed using [private/logout](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/authentication/private-logout), cancel-on-disconnect will **not** be triggered.\n\n**Notice:** Cancel-on-Disconnect does not affect orders created by other connections - they will remain active! When change is applied on the `account` scope, then every newly opened connection will start with **active** Cancel on Disconnect.\n\n**WebSocket Only:** This method is designed exclusively for WebSocket connections. Attempting to use it via REST/HTTP will result in an error response.\n\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fenable_cancel_on_disconnect)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"92:T578,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves Market Maker Protection (MMP) configuration for an index. Returns all currently active MMP parameters for the selected index, including the interval, `frozen_time`, quantity/delta/vega limits, and `max_quote_quantity`.\n\nIf the `index_name` parameter is not provided, a list of all MMP configurations is returned. An empty list means no MMP configuration exists. This method is useful for verifying your configuration or confirming applied updates.\n\nFor Mass Quotes, specify the `mmp_group` parameter to retrieve configuration for a specific MMP group. If no group is provided, returns configuration for regular orders. Set `block_rfq` to `true` to retrieve MMP configuration for Block RFQ (requires `block_rfq:read` scope).\n\nEach entry in the response includes an `id` field (integer) that uniquely identifies the MMP group. This integer ID is the programmatic identifier for the group and can be used to reference it in contexts where the string `mmp_group` name is not accepted. Entries that have no `mmp_group` name in the response correspond to the orders MMP group (the default group).\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Market Maker Protection API Configuration](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/market-maker-protection)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read` or `block_rfq:read` (when `block_rfq` = `true`)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_mmp_config)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"93:T465,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the current state of an order identified by its order ID. The response includes order details such as status (open, filled, cancelled), filled amount, remaining amount, price, and other order properties.\n\n**Important Note for Mass Quotes:** Quote orders are order-like structures that don't fully translate to normal orders. When checking order state for quotes, the `amount` field represents the remaining amount, not the original order amount.\n\n**Note:** This method does not support the `historical` flag and only returns an order that closed within the last 30 minutes (same recency window as `historical=false`). For orders older than that, use [`private/get_order_history_by_currency`](#private-get_order_history_by_currency) or [`private/get_order_history_by_instrument`](#private-get_order_history_by_instrument) with `historical=true`.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Accessing Historical Trades and Orders Using API](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/accessing-historical-trades-orders)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_order_state)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"94:T4fa,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the state of recent orders that have a specific label. This is useful for tracking orders that share the same label, which is helpful for managing related orders.\n\nResults are filtered by currency and label. The response includes order details such as status, filled amount, remaining amount, and other order properties for all orders with the specified label.\n\n**Note:** This method does not support the `historical` flag and only returns orders that closed within the last 30 minutes (same recency window as `historical=false`). This also applies to a trigger order and the order it creates upon triggering — once either has been closed for more than 30 minutes, it will no longer appear here, even though the same `label` was carried over between them. For orders older than that, use [`private/get_order_history_by_currency`](#private-get_order_history_by_currency) or [`private/get_order_history_by_instrument`](#private-get_order_history_by_instrument) with `historical=true`.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Accessing Historical Trades and Orders Using API](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/accessing-historical-trades-orders)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_order_state_by_label)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"95:T40f,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves settlement, delivery, and bankruptcy events that have affected your account for a specific currency.\n\n**Settlement vs. delivery:** Settlement is a daily event (at 08:00 UTC) for futures and perpetual positions that converts unrealized profit and loss into realized profit and loss. Option positions do not settle. Delivery is a one-time event that occurs when a futures or options contract expires — any remaining open position is closed at the delivery price. Delivery does not apply to perpetual or spot instruments. Both events take place at 08:00 UTC, which is why they are sometimes conflated.\n\nResults can be filtered by settlement type and timestamp. Use pagination parameters (`count` and `continuation`) to retrieve large settlement histories. This data is useful for tracking account-affecting settlement events and understanding how contract expirations impact your account.\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_settlement_history_by_currency)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"96:T456,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Places buy and/or sell orders (quotes) on one or more instruments simultaneously. This method is designed for market makers who need to quote on multiple instruments efficiently.\n\n**Requirements:**\n- Cancel-on-Disconnect must be enabled (see [private/enable_cancel_on_disconnect](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/session-management/private-enable_cancel_on_disconnect)), otherwise the request will return an error.\n- This endpoint can only be used after approval from the administrators.\n\nEach quote can include both bid and ask sides, or just one side. Quotes are identified by `quote_set_id` for targeted cancellation. Use the `wait_for_response` parameter to control whether to wait for all orders to be processed before returning.\n\nAccepted quotes are published to the standard Deribit order book and are visible in the UI and non-Starbase market data feeds.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Mass Quotes Specifications](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/mass-quotes-specifications)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fmass_quote)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"97:T457,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Moves positions from a source subaccount to a target subaccount. This operation transfers open positions between subaccounts, which is useful for rebalancing or reorganizing trading activities.\n\nPositions can be filtered by currency. The operation creates trades to transfer positions, which may affect P\u0026L and margin calculations.\n\n**Note - This method has distinct API rate limiting requirements:** \n- Sustained rate: 6 requests/minute\n- Weekly limit: 100 move_position uses per week (168 hours)\n\nFor more information, see [Rate Limits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/rate-limits).\n\n**Important:** In rare cases, the request may return an `internal_server_error`. This does not necessarily mean the operation failed entirely. Part or all of the position transfer might have still been processed successfully. Check the positions in both accounts to verify the transfer status.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Moving Positions](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/moving-positions-api)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fmove_positions)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"98:T456,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Resets Market Maker Protection (MMP) limits for the specified currency pair or MMP group. If MMP protection has been triggered and quoting is frozen, this method allows you to manually resume quoting.\n\nIf the configured `frozen_time` has expired, the system will automatically reset MMP. If `frozen_time` is set to `0` (automatic reset disabled), you must call this method to re-enable quoting. You can also perform a manual reset during the frozen period if you want to resume quoting early.\n\nFor regular MMP (`block_rfq = false`), the `index_name` must be a specific currency pair (e.g., \"btc_usd\", \"eth_usd\"). For Block RFQ MMP (`block_rfq = true`), you can set `index_name` to `\"all\"` to reset limits across all currency pairs. Use the `mmp_group` parameter to reset limits for a specific MMP group.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Market Maker Protection API Configuration](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/market-maker-protection)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write` or `block_rfq:read_write` (when `block_rfq` = `true`)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Freset_mmp)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"99:T7d1,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Configures Market Maker Protection (MMP) for a specific index. This method sets the monitoring window, freeze duration, and exposure limits (quantity, delta, vega, and Maximum Quote Quantity).\n\nAt least one limit parameter must be set. Maximum Quote Quantity (MQQ) is a required parameter that limits the total combined size of open MMP orders. MQQ is configured per index but enforced per side, per order book (instrument).\n\nThe `interval` parameter defines the monitoring window duration in seconds. The `frozen_time` parameter sets how long MMP remains active after being triggered. Set `frozen_time` to `0` to disable automatic reset (manual reset required).\n\nFor Mass Quotes, use the `mmp_group` parameter to configure MMP for a specific group. Set `block_rfq` to `true` to configure MMP for Block RFQ (requires `block_rfq:read_write` scope). Set `interval` to `0` to remove MMP configuration.\n\n**MMP margin reservation (MQQ-based Initial Margin)**\n\nSetting a non-zero `max_quote_quantity` immediately reserves Initial Margin equal to `MQQ × 3%`. This reservation is **unconditional and continuous** — it is held from the moment the config is active regardless of whether you have any open positions or open orders. Multiple MMP groups on the same currency pair each contribute independently. The reserved margin is visible in the **Portfolio Margin** section of the platform.\n\n**To release the reserved margin**, remove the MMP configuration entirely by calling this method with `interval = 0`. Setting `interval` to `0` deletes the configuration entry for the specified `index_name` (and `mmp_group` if provided), which immediately frees all margin reserved by that config entry.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Market Maker Protection API Configuration](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/market-maker-protection)\n\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write` or `block_rfq:read_write` (when `block_rfq` = `true`)\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fset_mmp_config)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"9a:T59e,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Adds a new address to the address book. The address book allows you to store addresses for withdrawals, along with beneficiary information for compliance purposes.\n\n**Coinbase wallet type**\n\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts the method supports network selection and CTN (Coinbase Travel Network) counterparties, and behaves differently:\n\n- Required parameters are `type` and `label`, plus one of:\n  - `address` together with `currency` and `network` (optional `tag`) — an on-chain address on the selected network, or\n  - `counterparty_id` — a CTN counterparty; `currency` is then omitted and the entry applies to all currencies.\n- `type` accepts only `withdrawal` and `transfer`.\n- Travel rule data is provided with the fields `name`, `country`, `address`, `financial_institution`, `account`, `account_location`, `entity_type` (`organization` or `individual`), `wallet_type` (`exchange` or `self_hosted`) and `is_self` instead of the legacy `beneficiary_*`, `agreed` and `personal` fields.\n- `extra_currencies` is not supported.\n- The response contains a Coinbase address book entry object, including the entry `id` which can be used instead of `address` in the other address book methods.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\n\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fadd_to_address_book)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"9b:T47f,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Creates a new deposit address for the specified currency. Each currency can have multiple deposit addresses. Use this method to generate a new address for receiving deposits.\n\n**Coinbase wallet type**\n\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts the `network` parameter is required and selects the blockchain network of the deposit address. The networks available for each currency are returned by `public/get_currencies` in the `coinbase_networks` field; a network that is not configured for the currency is rejected. An optional `label` can be provided, defaulting to `\"deposit address\"`. This method is available to institutional Coinbase accounts only.\n\n**Note:**\n\nFor Bitcoin, a new address can be generated every 24 hours.\n\nFor ERC20, Solana and XRP only one address can be generated.\n\n**Note:**\n\nIf an ERC20 address is generated, this address will be automatically added for every asset that uses ERC20 addresses.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Deposits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-deposits-api)\n\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcreate_deposit_address)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"9c:T412,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Retrieves the address book entries of the given type. Returns all saved addresses that can be used for withdrawals, along with their labels and beneficiary information if available.\n\n**Coinbase wallet type**\n\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts `currency` accepts any portfolio currency or `\"all\"`, and `type` accepts `withdrawal`, `transfer` or `deposit` (deposit addresses created via `private/create_deposit_address`). The returned entries are Coinbase address book entry objects: they include the entry `id` (usable instead of `address` in the other address book methods), `kind` (`onchain` or `ctn`), `network`, `network_display_name`, `tag` and the Coinbase travel rule fields (`name`, `country`, `financial_institution`, `account`, `account_location`, `entity_type`, `wallet_type`, `is_self`) when set.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\n\n**Scope:** `wallet:read`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_address_book)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"9d:T50f,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Updates beneficiary information for an address in the address book. This method allows you to add or modify beneficiary details required for compliance purposes when making withdrawals to certain addresses.\n\n**Coinbase wallet type**\n\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts the method behaves differently:\n\n- Required parameters are `currency` (portfolio currencies or `\"all\"`) and `type`, plus one of `address` or `id` (the entry identifier returned by `private/get_address_book`). Use `network` and `tag` together with `address` to disambiguate entries sharing the same address.\n- `type` accepts only `withdrawal` and `transfer`.\n- `label` is optional.\n- Travel rule data is provided with the fields `name`, `country`, `address`, `financial_institution`, `account`, `account_location`, `entity_type` (`organization` or `individual`), `wallet_type` (`exchange` or `self_hosted`) and `is_self` instead of the legacy `beneficiary_*`, `agreed` and `personal` fields.\n- The response contains the updated Coinbase address book entry object instead of `\"ok\"`.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\n\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fupdate_in_address_book)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"9e:T8ed,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Creates a new withdrawal request. This method allows you to withdraw funds from your account to an external address. The withdrawal can be configured with priority settings and must use an address from your address book.\n\n**Withdrawal Checks \u0026 Balance Updates**\n\nWithdrawal funds are checked twice: when a user requests a withdrawal and again when they confirm it via the email link. If available funds decrease between these steps, the withdrawal may be rejected.\n\nA withdrawal may also be rejected if the on-chain fee increases between the request and confirmation.\n\nThe withdrawal amount is deducted only after all checks pass and the transaction is scheduled. The web-interface Withdrawal tab displays all withdrawals regardless of their status (pending, cancelled, rejected, or completed).\n\n**Coinbase wallet type**\n\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts the method supports network selection and CTN (Coinbase Travel Network) counterparties, and behaves differently:\n\n- Required parameters are `currency` (any portfolio currency) and `amount`, plus one of `address` or `id` (the address book entry identifier returned by `private/get_address_book`).\n- When `address` is an on-chain address, pass `network` (and `tag` when applicable) to identify the address book entry. For a CTN withdrawal, pass the CTN counterparty identifier of the entry as `address`.\n- `priority` and `nonce` are not supported. Use `private/coinbase/estimate_withdrawal_fee` to estimate the network fee.\n- Subaccounts can withdraw only when enabled by the main account via `private/set_coinbase_subaccount_withdrawals_allowed`.\n- The response is a Coinbase withdrawal object instead of the legacy withdrawal object. Its `state` is one of `prepared`, `awaiting_second_email`, `unconfirmed`, `completed` or `cancelled`; withdrawals to an address that is not trusted start as `prepared` and require email confirmation, in which case `transfer_idem` is absent until the withdrawal is submitted to the custodian. Fields that are not set are omitted from the response.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\n\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write` and mainaccount\n\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fwithdraw)\n\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"9f:T4b0,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Real-time order book updates for a specific instrument.\n\n- The first notification contains a full snapshot of the book (bids and asks for **all price levels** — no depth limit).\n- Subsequent notifications contain only incremental changes to individual price levels.\n- Updates are tuples in the form `[action, price, amount]`, where `action` is one of: `new`, `change`, `delete`.\n\nEach notification includes a `change_id`. Every message except the first also contains `prev_change_id`. If `prev_change_id` equals the `change_id` of the previous message, it indicates that no messages were missed.\n\nFor Starbase-routed instruments, the published price levels include accepted mass-quote liquidity.\n\n**Depth:** This channel delivers the complete order book with no depth restriction. If you need a depth-limited, price-grouped snapshot, use `book.{instrument_name}.{group}.{depth}.{interval}` instead.\n\n**Units:** For perpetuals and futures, `amount` is in USD units. For options, `amount` is in the corresponding cryptocurrency contracts (e.g., BTC or ETH).\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a0:T6a2,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Real-time ticker data providing comprehensive market information for the specified instrument.\n\nThis subscription delivers key market metrics including:\n\n- **Price data:** Best bid/ask prices and amounts, last trade price, mark price, index price, settlement price, and estimated delivery price\n- **Market statistics:** 24-hour volume (in base currency and USD for futures), high/low prices, price change percentage, and open interest\n- **Order book state:** Current state of the instrument (open, settlement, delivered, inactive, locked, halted, or archivized)\n- **Price limits:** Minimum and maximum price constraints for order placement\n- **Options-specific data:** Implied volatility (bid/ask/mark IV), Greeks (delta, gamma, theta, vega, rho), underlying price, and interest rate\n- **Perpetual-specific data:** Current funding rate and 8-hour funding rate\n- **Futures-specific data:** Interest value and delivery price\n\nThe `interval` parameter controls the frequency of updates: `raw` (finest granularity - events aggregated over a 1 millisecond interval, authorized users only), `100ms` (aggregated every 100 milliseconds), or `agg2` (aggregated every 2 seconds).\n\nThis is the recommended method for real-time market data updates, as it provides efficient push-based notifications instead of requiring polling.\n\n**Note:** For spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, `volume_notional` and `volume_usd` are omitted from `stats`.\n\n**📖 Related Articles:** \n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\n- [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a1:T4d5,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Real-time notifications for Market Maker Protection (MMP) triggers. This subscription provides feedback when MMP protection is activated for a given index, enabling clients to react promptly when protection is triggered.\n\nUpon MMP being triggered for a given index, the client will receive a trigger notification containing:\n\n- **frozen_until**: Unix timestamp in milliseconds indicating until when the MMP is active (orders remain blocked). If `frozen_until: 0`, it means MMP will remain active until manually reset using the `private/reset_mmp` method.\n- **index_name**: Index identifier of derivative instrument on the platform. For Block RFQ MMP, this will be \"all\" when triggered by trade count limit.\n- **mmp_group**: Triggered MMP group (optional, appears only for Mass Quote orders trigger)\n- **block_rfq**: If true, indicates that the MMP trigger is for Block RFQ. Block RFQ MMP triggers are completely separate from normal order/quote MMP triggers.\n\nThis notification allows the client to track MMP state per index and avoid submitting new orders that would be rejected due to ongoing MMP freeze.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Market Maker Protection API Configuration](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/market-maker-protection)\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a2:T543,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Real-time notifications for user portfolio information. This subscription provides comprehensive account and portfolio data for the specified currency, including balances, margins, profit and loss, and Greeks.\n\nEach notification includes:\n\n- **Account balances:** Current balance, equity, margin balance, available funds, and available withdrawal funds\n- **Margin information:** Initial margin, maintenance margin, and projected margins\n- **Profit and Loss:** Total P\u0026L, session unrealized P\u0026L (UPL), session realized P\u0026L (RPL), and separate P\u0026L for options and futures\n- **Options Greeks:** Delta, gamma, theta, vega, and options value, with per-index mappings\n- **Position data:** Delta total, projected delta total, and delta total map per index\n- **Account settings:** Portfolio margining status, cross collateral status, and margin model\n- **Cross collateral data:** Total equity, margins, and delta in USD (when cross collateral is enabled)\n- **Additional reserves:** Fee balance and additional reserve information\n\nWhen cross collateral is enabled, aggregated values are calculated by converting the sum of each cross collateral currency's value to the given currency, using each cross collateral currency's index.\n\nSubscribe to a specific currency (BTC, ETH, USDC, USDT, etc.) or use `any` to receive portfolio updates for all currencies.\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a3:T5b1,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Notifications about the authenticated account's own liquidation, auto-deleveraging (ADL), and LSP (Liquidity Support Program) activity — both as the account being liquidated/deleveraged and, for ADL, as a counterparty receiving a deleveraged position.\n\nThis includes the liquidated account's own transfer events (`lsp_transfer`, `adl_transfer`) as well as `adl_transfer_received` for any account that absorbs a position via ADL. See `user.lsp` for the additional notifications sent to the LSP participant *receiving* an assigned position (enable/disable and configuration changes).\n\nA successful `lsp_transfer` or `adl_transfer` is also delivered on the [Starbase FIX Drop Copy](https://docs.deribit.com/starbase/fix-drop-copy-api) session of the Starbase Member that owns that portfolio, as a TradeCaptureReport (`35=AE`) with TradeType (828) `3`. On that report TransferReason (830) is `LIQUIDATED`. The receiving side's report has TransferReason (830) `ASSIGNED` and LiquidationMechanism (8002) `LSP` or `ADL`. Started/completed states and failed assignment attempts are WebSocket-only. Only a position move whose reason is admin is omitted from Drop Copy.\n\nEvery notification includes a `state` field identifying the stage of the process — see the notification schema for the full list of states and which fields accompany each.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a4:T5f3,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Notifications for an LSP (Liquidity Support Program) participant subaccount: assignment attempts (successful or failed), enable/disable state changes, and effective configuration changes.\n\nSubscribe to this channel with an API key belonging to the LSP participant subaccount itself. See `user.liquidation` for the notification sent to the liquidated (source) user whose position was transferred.\n\nA **successful** assignment is also delivered on the [Starbase FIX Drop Copy](https://docs.deribit.com/starbase/fix-drop-copy-api) session of the Starbase Member that owns that portfolio: a TradeCaptureReport (`35=AE`) with TradeType (828) `3` (position move), TransferReason (830) `ASSIGNED`, and LiquidationMechanism (8002) `LSP`. TrdMatchID (880) on that report is `starbase_match_id` on the successful `transfer` notification. You do not need this WebSocket channel to receive successful assignments if that Member's Drop Copy session already covers the portfolio.\n\nThis channel is still required for what Drop Copy does not send: a failed assignment attempt (`success: false`), and `enabled`, `disabled`, and `configuration_changed`. Only a position move whose reason is admin is omitted from Drop Copy. LSP and ADL assignments are sent.\n\nEvery notification includes a `type` field identifying the event kind — see the notification schema for the full list of types and which fields accompany each.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a5:T7ca,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Real-time notifications for Block RFQs (Request for Quotes) that are available for the subscribed maker to respond to.\n\nThis subscription notifies makers when new Block RFQs are created in the specified currency (or all currencies if `any` is used) that they can potentially quote on. Each notification includes:\n\n- **RFQ identification:** Unique Block RFQ ID, creation timestamp, and expiration timestamp\n- **RFQ structure:** Multi-leg trade structure with instrument names, directions (buy/sell), and ratios for each leg\n- **Trade parameters:** Total amount (multiplied by leg ratios determines trade size), minimum trade amount, and optional combo identifier\n- **Hedge information:** Optional hedge leg details including instrument, direction, amount, and price\n- **RFQ state:** Current state (open, filled, cancelled, or expired)\n- **Counterparty information:** Taker rating, taker alias (if disclosed), and disclosure status\n- **Execution details:** For filled RFQs, includes trade information with prices, amounts, directions, and maker aliases\n- **Index prices:** List of index prices for underlying instruments at trade execution time (for filled RFQs)\n- **Rating information:** Whether the RFQ is included in taker rating calculation (for closed RFQs)\n\nMakers can subscribe to specific currencies (BTC, ETH, USDC, USDT) or use `any` to receive notifications for all supported currencies. This enables makers to monitor incoming RFQ opportunities and respond with competitive quotes in a timely manner.\n\n**Scope required:** `block_rfq:read`\n\n**Trade cross-posting:** When a Block RFQ is filled, the resulting trades are also delivered through the `user.trades.{instrument_name}.{interval}` and `user.trades.{kind}.{currency}.{interval}` channels. Those notifications include `block_rfq_id`, `block_trade_id`, and — for the maker side — `block_rfq_quote_id`.\n\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a6:T5cc,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Returns all currently-open orders belonging to the authenticated portfolio. Orders are returned regardless of instrument or order type; filtering by instrument kind and order type is not currently supported.\n\nEach order includes `instrument_id`, `product_group`, and the `post_only`, `reject_post_only`, and `reduce_only` flags. `instrument_id` is the numeric instrument id. `product_group` is the Starbase routing group (`BTC`, `ETH`, `TIER_2`, or `TIER_3`). `post_only` and `reject_post_only` correspond to the SBE `postOnly` and `postOnlyReject` bits and are mutually exclusive. `reduce_only` reflects per-order reduce-only from [classic JSON-RPC](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/json-rpc-overview) or FIX (it cannot be set per order in SBE).\n\nThe portfolio is resolved from the authenticated session. There is no parameter to query another portfolio's orders. MMP-flagged orders are visible via this endpoint. Orders placed via Mass Quote (MassQuoteRequest) are included.\n\nThis endpoint is rate-limited to 10 requests per minute per portfolio on each REST gateway. The A and B gateways enforce this cap independently. Exceeding the limit returns HTTP 429. Because this limit is heavily restrictive relative to typical order-book activity, this endpoint is best used for periodic reconciliation rather than to maintain live order state. To track open orders in real time, maintain a dedicated [FIX Drop Copy](/starbase/fix-drop-copy-api) session instead of polling this endpoint."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a7:T4c8,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Returns the effective position (\"risk\") limits for the authenticated portfolio, one entry per underlying (currency pair).\n\nEach numeric field is resolved per field: a portfolio override wins when that field is set, otherwise the currency-pair default is used. A field unset at both levels is omitted. `-1` means the limit is explicitly unlimited (distinct from unset). The call is read-only and does not change limits.\n\nOnly underlyings that have a currency-pair default or an override for this portfolio are included. Overrides that belong to other portfolios do not create an entry.\n\nPass `currency` to select one underlying. The value is the currency-pair name returned in `currency` (for example `BTC_USDC`). Matching is case-insensitive and ignores separators, so `btc-usdc` and `BTCUSDC` resolve to the same pair. An unknown name returns HTTP 400. A known pair with no configured limit for this portfolio returns an empty list.\n\nThe portfolio is resolved from the authenticated session. There is no parameter to query another portfolio.\n\nThis endpoint is rate-limited to 1 request per minute per portfolio on each REST gateway. The A and B gateways enforce this cap independently. Exceeding the limit returns HTTP 429."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a8:T6a0,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Returns the list of tradeable instruments, including `index_id` and `product_group`, optionally filtered by base currency, instrument kind, expiration status, instrument id, product group, and lifecycle state.\n\nThis endpoint requires no authentication, but it is served by the Starbase REST gateway and is reachable only through hosted colocation, a cross-connect, or AWS Private Link. The internet-accessible [classic JSON-RPC](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/json-rpc-overview) `public/get_instruments` method also documents `index_id` and `product_group`; backend rollout of those fields may temporarily differ between the two endpoints.\n\nFilter semantics (supplied filters are combined):\n- `currency` filters by the **base** currency of the instrument's currency pair (case-insensitive exact match, for example `BTC` or `ETH`). Omit `currency` to return instruments for every base currency. A value that is not a listed base currency, including `any`, matches no instrument: the call succeeds and `result` is an empty array. `any` is compared as a base-currency name.\n- `kind` filters by instrument type (case-insensitive match against the `kind` value enum).\n- `expired = true` returns only instruments whose `expiration_timestamp` is in the past; `expired = false` returns only non-expired instruments. Omit the parameter to get both.\n- `instrument_id` returns the instrument with that numeric id.\n- `product_group` filters by Starbase product group (case-insensitive match against `BTC`, `ETH`, `TIER_2`, `TIER_3`).\n- `state` filters by instrument lifecycle state (case-insensitive). Values match SBE `InstrumentStatus`: `open`, `inactive`, `settlement`, `delivered`, `locked`, `halted`."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1b:[\"$\",\"$L4e\",null,{\"scopedNav\":{\"global\":null,\"versions\":[{\"version\":\"Production\",\"tabs\":[{\"tab\":\"Overview\",\"groups\":[{\"group\":\"Introduction\",\"expanded\":false,\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Welcome to Deribit API\",\"description\":\"Deribit is a crypto derivatives exchange offering futures, options, and perpetuals. This documentation is your integration entry point for the API.\",\"keywords\":[\"Deribit API\",\"cryptocurrency API\",\"derivatives trading\",\"Bitcoin futures\",\"options trading\",\"WebSocket API\",\"FIX API\",\"trading API\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit API Documentation - Cryptocurrency Derivatives Trading API\",\"og:description\":\"Complete API documentation for Deribit cryptocurrency derivatives exchange. Integrate with JSON-RPC, WebSocket, and FIX APIs for trading futures, perpetuals, and options.\",\"og:type\":\"website\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API Documentation\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete API documentation for Deribit cryptocurrency derivatives exchange. Integrate with JSON-RPC, WebSocket, and FIX APIs.\",\"href\":\"\"},{\"title\":\"Quickstart Guide\",\"description\":\"Set up the Deribit API environment, send your first authenticated JSON-RPC request, and use the key endpoints to place an order in minutes.\",\"keywords\":[\"Deribit quickstart\",\"API tutorial\",\"get started\",\"first API call\",\"Deribit integration\",\"API setup\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit API Quickstart Guide - Get Started in Minutes\",\"og:description\":\"Get started with Deribit API in minutes. Learn how to create API keys, authenticate, and make your first API calls with step-by-step examples.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API Quickstart Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Get started with Deribit API in minutes. Step-by-step guide to creating API keys, authenticating, and making your first API calls.\",\"href\":\"/articles/deribit-quickstart\"}]},{\"group\":\"Authentication\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Creating new API key\",\"description\":\"Generate a new Deribit API key from the web interface or programmatically, including choosing scopes, IP restrictions, and secret handling tips.\",\"keywords\":[\"API key creation\",\"create API key\",\"API credentials\",\"client ID\",\"client secret\",\"API setup\",\"API configuration\"],\"og:title\":\"Creating Deribit API Keys - Frontend and API Methods\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to create Deribit API keys using the web interface or API. Configure scopes, IP whitelisting, and security settings.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Creating Deribit API Keys Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Step-by-step guide to creating Deribit API keys via web interface or API, including scope configuration and security settings.\",\"href\":\"/articles/creating-api-key\"},{\"title\":\"Authentication\",\"description\":\"OAuth 2.0-style authentication for private Deribit API requests, covering access tokens, refresh tokens, scopes, and signature-based login flows.\",\"keywords\":[\"Deribit authentication\",\"OAuth 2.0\",\"API keys\",\"access token\",\"refresh token\",\"client credentials\",\"client signature\",\"API security\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit API Authentication Guide - OAuth 2.0 and API Keys\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to authenticate with Deribit API using OAuth 2.0, manage API keys, handle access tokens, and implement secure authentication flows.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API Authentication Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to Deribit API authentication including OAuth 2.0, API keys, tokens, and security best practices.\",\"href\":\"/articles/authentication\"},{\"title\":\"Access Scope\",\"description\":\"OAuth scope controls read and write access for Deribit API tokens, letting you set granular permission levels for account, trade, and wallet actions.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"keywords\":[\"API scopes\",\"access scopes\",\"API permissions\",\"OAuth scopes\",\"API authorization\",\"permission levels\",\"read write access\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit API Access Scopes - Permission and Authorization Guide\",\"og:description\":\"Learn about Deribit API access scopes, permission levels, connection vs session scopes, and how to configure read-only or read-write access for your API keys.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API Access Scopes Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to Deribit API access scopes, permissions, and authorization levels for API keys.\",\"href\":\"/articles/access-scope\"},{\"title\":\"Security Keys\",\"description\":\"Hardware security keys and additional signing requirements for sensitive Deribit API methods like withdrawals, key management, and Travel Rule data.\",\"keywords\":[\"security keys\",\"2FA\",\"two-factor authentication\",\"TOTP\",\"API security\",\"authorization\",\"security confirmation\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit API Security Keys - Two-Factor Authentication Guide\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to use Security Keys and Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) with Deribit API for secure withdrawals, API key management, and sensitive operations.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API Security Keys Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to using Security Keys and 2FA with Deribit API for enhanced security on sensitive operations.\",\"href\":\"/articles/security-keys\"}]},{\"group\":\"Technical Information\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"API Usage Policy\",\"description\":\"Deribit fair-use API policy outlines acceptable traffic patterns, throttling rules, and consequences of abuse to keep exchange infrastructure healthy.\",\"keywords\":[\"API usage policy\",\"OTV ratio\",\"order to volume\",\"API guidelines\",\"rate limiting\",\"API best practices\",\"matching engine\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit API Usage Policy - Guidelines and Best Practices\",\"og:description\":\"Deribit API usage policy including Order to Volume (OTV) ratios, matching engine guidelines, and best practices for efficient API usage.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API Usage Policy\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete Deribit API usage policy with OTV ratios, matching engine guidelines, and API best practices.\",\"href\":\"/articles/api-usage-policy\"},{\"title\":\"Rate Limits\",\"description\":\"How credit-based rate limiting works on the Deribit API, including burst and sustained caps, matching engine limits, and per-tier request quotas.\",\"keywords\":[\"rate limits\",\"API rate limiting\",\"credit system\",\"throttling\",\"API quotas\",\"request limits\",\"matching engine\",\"non-matching engine\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit API Rate Limits - Credit-Based Rate Limiting System\",\"og:description\":\"Understand Deribit's credit-based rate limiting system, matching vs non-matching engine limits, tier-based limits, and how to optimize API usage.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API Rate Limits Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to Deribit's credit-based rate limiting system, tier limits, and API usage optimization.\",\"href\":\"/articles/rate-limits\"}]},{\"group\":\"Best Practices\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Connection Management\",\"description\":\"Best practices for Deribit WebSocket connection lifecycle including heartbeats, session versus connection tokens, and reliable reconnect strategies.\",\"keywords\":[\"connection management\",\"WebSocket connections\",\"session management\",\"connection limits\",\"API connections\",\"connection scopes\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit API Connection Management - Best Practices Guide\",\"og:description\":\"Learn best practices for managing Deribit API connections, WebSocket sessions, connection limits, and optimizing connection scopes for reliable API access.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API Connection Management Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Best practices for managing Deribit API connections, WebSocket sessions, and connection limits.\",\"href\":\"/articles/connection-management-best-practices\"},{\"title\":\"Market Data Collection\",\"description\":\"Efficient Deribit market data ingestion patterns covering snapshots, incremental updates, throttling, and channel selection per instrument.\",\"keywords\":[\"market data\",\"real-time data\",\"WebSocket subscriptions\",\"FIX market data\",\"order book updates\",\"data collection\",\"algorithmic trading\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Market Data Collection Best Practices - Real-Time Data Guide\",\"og:description\":\"Learn best practices for efficient market data collection on Deribit including WebSocket subscriptions, FIX feeds, raw vs aggregated data, and latency optimization.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Market Data Collection Best Practices\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to efficient market data collection and real-time data consumption on Deribit API.\",\"href\":\"/articles/market-data-collection-best-practices\"},{\"title\":\"Options Data Collection\",\"description\":\"Collect Deribit options market data efficiently, covering order books, ticker greeks, mark prices, implied volatility, combos, trades, and settlement data.\",\"keywords\":[\"options data\",\"options market data\",\"Deribit options\",\"greeks\",\"implied volatility\",\"mark price\",\"order book depth\",\"options collection\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Options Data Collection - Best Practices Guide\",\"og:description\":\"Learn best practices for collecting Deribit options market data, including order books, greeks, mark price/IV, trades, combos, and settlement data.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Options Data Collection Best Practices\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to collecting options market data from the Deribit API: order books, greeks, IV, trades, combos, and settlement.\",\"href\":\"/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices\"},{\"title\":\"Order Management\",\"description\":\"High-performance order management on Deribit, covering batching, cancel and replace flows, label usage, and how to avoid rate-limit throttling under load.\",\"keywords\":[\"order management\",\"trading best practices\",\"order execution\",\"latency optimization\",\"order cancellation\",\"advanced orders\",\"OCO\",\"OTO\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Order Management Best Practices - High-Performance Trading Guide\",\"og:description\":\"Learn best practices for efficient order management on Deribit including order submission, latency optimization, cancellation strategies, and advanced order types.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Order Management Best Practices\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to order management best practices for high-performance trading on Deribit API.\",\"href\":\"/articles/order-management-best-practices\"},{\"title\":\"Using the currency Parameter\",\"description\":\"Discover supported currencies with get_currencies, learn what currency selects on each Deribit method, and avoid invalid currency and spot routing errors.\",\"keywords\":[\"currency parameter\",\"settlement currency\",\"wallet currency\",\"supported currencies\",\"get_currencies\",\"invalid currency\",\"get_positions currency\",\"spot currency\",\"currency any\"],\"og:title\":\"Using the currency Parameter - Deribit API Guide\",\"og:description\":\"Choose the correct currency value for each Deribit API method, discover supported currencies at runtime, and avoid invalid currency and routed spot errors.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API currency Parameter Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"How to use the currency parameter correctly across positions, wallet and market data methods on the Deribit API.\",\"href\":\"/articles/currency-parameter\"}]},{\"group\":\"Guides\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Managing Deposits\",\"description\":\"Generate deposit addresses, check deposit status and history, and submit Travel Rule originator information using the Deribit deposit API endpoints.\",\"keywords\":[\"deposits API\",\"deposit addresses\",\"deposit history\",\"Travel Rule\",\"crypto deposits\",\"wallet API\",\"deposit management\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Deposits API - Managing Deposit Addresses and History\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to generate deposit addresses, check deposit history, and submit Travel Rule information using Deribit's deposits API.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Deposits API Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to managing deposits, generating addresses, and checking deposit history with Deribit API.\",\"href\":\"/articles/managing-deposits-api\"},{\"title\":\"Managing Transfers\",\"description\":\"Transfer funds between the main account and subaccounts or to other Deribit users using the API, including two-step confirmation flows for security.\",\"keywords\":[\"transfers API\",\"subaccount transfers\",\"account transfers\",\"wallet transfers\",\"transfer between accounts\",\"API transfers\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Transfers API - Transfer Funds Between Accounts\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to perform transfers between main accounts and subaccounts using Deribit's transfers API, including authentication and transfer methods.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Transfers API Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to transferring funds between main accounts and subaccounts using Deribit API.\",\"href\":\"/articles/managing-transfers-api\"},{\"title\":\"Managing Subaccounts\",\"description\":\"Create, rename, configure permissions, and manage Deribit subaccounts programmatically via API for team access control and portfolio segregation.\",\"keywords\":[\"subaccounts API\",\"subaccount management\",\"create subaccount\",\"subaccount configuration\",\"account management\",\"multi-account trading\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Subaccounts API - Managing Multiple Trading Accounts\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to create, configure, and manage subaccounts using Deribit's subaccounts API for risk management and client segregation.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Subaccounts API Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to creating and managing subaccounts with Deribit API for multi-account trading.\",\"href\":\"/articles/managing-subaccounts-api\"},{\"title\":\"Managing Withdrawals\",\"description\":\"Whitelist withdrawal addresses, create withdrawal requests, and handle Travel Rule compliance through Deribit API endpoints for crypto asset payouts.\",\"keywords\":[\"withdrawals API\",\"withdrawal addresses\",\"withdrawal history\",\"Travel Rule\",\"crypto withdrawals\",\"wallet API\",\"withdrawal management\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Withdrawals API - Managing Withdrawals and Addresses\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to manage withdrawal addresses, create withdrawals, check withdrawal history, and handle Travel Rule compliance using Deribit's withdrawals API.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Withdrawals API Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to managing withdrawals, addresses, and Travel Rule compliance with Deribit API.\",\"href\":\"/articles/managing-withdrawals-api\"},{\"title\":\"Coinbase Wallet API\",\"description\":\"Wallet API behavior for Coinbase-custodied Deribit accounts: network selection, deposit addresses, address book and CTN counterparties, and withdrawals.\",\"keywords\":[\"Coinbase wallet\",\"multi-network\",\"network selection\",\"deposit address\",\"withdrawals API\",\"address book\",\"Coinbase Travel Network\",\"CTN\",\"Travel Rule\",\"wallet API\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Coinbase Wallet API - Multi-Network Deposits and Withdrawals\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how network selection, address book entries, Travel Rule data and withdrawals work on the Deribit wallet API for Coinbase-custodied accounts.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Coinbase Wallet API Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Network selection, address book entries, CTN counterparties and withdrawals for Coinbase-custodied Deribit accounts.\",\"href\":\"/articles/coinbase-wallet-api\"},{\"title\":\"Moving Positions\",\"description\":\"Transfer open positions between Deribit subaccounts using the API, including required permissions, valuation, and settlement of moved contracts.\",\"keywords\":[\"position moves\",\"move positions\",\"subaccount positions\",\"position transfer\",\"position management\",\"portfolio management\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Moving Positions API - Transfer Positions Between Subaccounts\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to move positions between subaccounts within the same main account using Deribit's position moving API.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Moving Positions API Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to moving positions between subaccounts using Deribit API.\",\"href\":\"/articles/moving-positions-api\"},{\"title\":\"Block Trading\",\"description\":\"Negotiate and execute block trades between two counterparties on Deribit via API, including quote verification, approval, and settlement workflows.\",\"keywords\":[\"block trading\",\"block trades\",\"institutional trading\",\"large trades\",\"off-book trading\",\"negotiated trades\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Block Trading API - Execute Large Off-Book Trades\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to execute block trades between two parties using Deribit's block trading API for large institutional trades off the public order book.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Block Trading API Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to executing block trades between parties using Deribit API for institutional trading.\",\"href\":\"/articles/block-trading-api\"},{\"title\":\"Voice Broker Trading API\",\"description\":\"How voice brokers submit block trades for clients on Deribit and how clients approve, reject, and monitor those trades via API endpoints and events.\",\"keywords\":[\"voice broker\",\"broker trading\",\"block trade\",\"broker client\",\"trade confirmation\",\"institutional trading\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Voice Broker Trading API\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how voice brokers execute block trades on behalf of clients and how clients approve, reject, and monitor broker-executed trades via the Deribit API.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Voice Broker Trading API Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to voice broker trading on Deribit, covering how to execute block trades on behalf of clients and manage trade confirmations via the API.\",\"href\":\"/articles/voice-broker-trading-api\"},{\"title\":\"Asymmetric API Keys\",\"description\":\"Asymmetric API keys use public and private key pairs to sign Deribit requests, offering stronger authentication and reduced credential exposure risk.\",\"keywords\":[\"asymmetric API keys\",\"Ed25519\",\"RSA keys\",\"public private key\",\"cryptographic signatures\",\"API security\",\"key pairs\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Asymmetric API Keys - Enhanced Security with Public-Private Key Pairs\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to use asymmetric API keys (Ed25519 or RSA) with Deribit API for enhanced security. Generate key pairs, sign requests, and improve API security.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Asymmetric API Keys Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to using asymmetric API keys (Ed25519/RSA) with Deribit API for enhanced cryptographic security.\",\"href\":\"/articles/asymmetric-api-keys\"},{\"title\":\"Market Maker Protection (MMP) API Configuration\",\"description\":\"Configure MMP thresholds, freeze times, and reset behavior for market maker order flow on Deribit via API to guard against toxic fills and runaways.\",\"keywords\":[\"MMP\",\"Market Maker Protection\",\"risk management\",\"quote protection\",\"exposure limits\",\"trading risk\",\"MMP configuration\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Market Maker Protection (MMP) API Configuration Guide\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to configure and manage Market Maker Protection (MMP) settings using Deribit API to reduce exposure risk and protect quoting activity.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Market Maker Protection API Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to configuring Market Maker Protection (MMP) settings with Deribit API for risk management.\",\"href\":\"/articles/market-maker-protection\"},{\"title\":\"Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide\",\"description\":\"Deribit's Liquidity Support Program (LSP) transfers liquidated positions to designated participant accounts before falling back to auto-deleveraging (ADL).\",\"keywords\":[\"LSP\",\"Liquidity Support Program\",\"liquidation\",\"auto-deleveraging\",\"ADL\",\"risk management\",\"cooldown group\",\"reduce-only\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how Deribit's Liquidity Support Program (LSP) works, how to monitor LSP participation via the API, and what to expect if your position is liquidated or auto-deleveraged.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Liquidity Support Program API Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to Deribit's Liquidity Support Program (LSP): eligibility, cooldown groups, transfer pricing, and API monitoring.\",\"href\":\"/articles/lsp-api-guide\"},{\"title\":\"Accessing Historical Trades and Orders Using API\",\"description\":\"Use the historical parameter on Deribit API endpoints to retrieve past trades and orders beyond the default lookback window for backfills and audits.\",\"keywords\":[\"historical data\",\"historical trades\",\"historical orders\",\"trade history\",\"order history\",\"historical API\",\"data retrieval\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Historical Trades and Orders API - Access Historical Data\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to retrieve historical trade and order records using Deribit API, including retention periods and supported endpoints.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Historical Data API Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to accessing historical trades and orders using Deribit API with retention period information.\",\"href\":\"/articles/accessing-historical-trades-orders\"},{\"title\":\"Deribit Block RFQ API Walkthrough\",\"description\":\"Step-by-step Block RFQ API walkthrough for requesting quotes on large block trades from Deribit market makers and executing multi-leg strategies.\",\"keywords\":[\"Block RFQ\",\"Request for Quote\",\"block trading\",\"market makers\",\"institutional trading\",\"RFQ API\",\"quote requests\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Block RFQ API Walkthrough - Request Quotes for Large Block Trades\",\"og:description\":\"Complete walkthrough of Deribit's Block RFQ API for requesting quotes from market makers, managing RFQs, and executing large block trades.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Block RFQ API Walkthrough\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to using Deribit's Block RFQ API for requesting quotes and executing large block trades.\",\"href\":\"/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough\"},{\"title\":\"Mass Quotes Specifications\",\"description\":\"Use the Deribit mass quote API to submit many bid and ask pairs in a single request for lower latency during option and future market making.\",\"keywords\":[\"mass quotes\",\"multiple orders\",\"quote API\",\"low latency\",\"MMP groups\",\"market making\",\"quote management\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Mass Quotes Specifications - Low-Latency Order Placement\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to use Deribit's mass quote functionality to place multiple orders in a single request with reduced latency and Market Maker Protection groups.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Mass Quotes Specifications\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to Deribit's mass quote functionality for low-latency multiple order placement.\",\"href\":\"/articles/mass-quotes-specifications\"},{\"title\":\"Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments\",\"description\":\"Which Deribit spot instruments are matched on Deribit and which are routed to Coinbase Exchange, and how order entry and market data differ between them.\",\"keywords\":[\"spot instruments\",\"spot trading\",\"Coinbase routed spot\",\"CBE routed\",\"is_cbe_routed\",\"is_csr\",\"trade tape\",\"spot order types\",\"FIX spot trading\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit API - Spot Trading on Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments\",\"og:description\":\"Which spot instruments are matched on Deribit and which are routed to Coinbase Exchange, and how the API differs between the two.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API - Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Spot Trading\",\"twitter:description\":\"Order entry and market data differences between Deribit-matched and Coinbase-routed spot instruments.\",\"href\":\"/articles/spot-trading-venues\"},{\"title\":\"Coinbase International Exchange API Migration\",\"description\":\"How International Exchange API and FIX integrations connect to Deribit after the migration: keys, endpoints, instruments, orders, and positions.\",\"keywords\":[\"INTX migration\",\"Coinbase International Exchange\",\"Deribit API\",\"BTC_USDC-PERPETUAL\",\"API migration\",\"FIX migration\"],\"og:title\":\"Coinbase International Exchange API Migration - Deribit\",\"og:description\":\"Keys, endpoints, instrument names, and order attributes for International Exchange API and FIX integrations on Deribit.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Coinbase International Exchange API Migration\",\"twitter:description\":\"Endpoints, keys, instrument names, and order attributes for International Exchange integrations on Deribit.\",\"href\":\"/articles/intx-api-migration\"}]}]},{\"tab\":\"API Reference\",\"dropdowns\":[{\"dropdown\":\"JSON-RPC API\",\"icon\":\"code\",\"pages\":[{\"group\":\"Methods overview\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"JSON-RPC 2.0 Protocol\",\"description\":\"Deribit API uses JSON-RPC 2.0 for all API communications. This standardized protocol provides a simple and consistent way to make remote procedure calls.\",\"keywords\":[\"JSON-RPC 2.0\",\"RPC protocol\",\"API protocol\",\"WebSocket\",\"HTTP REST\",\"API requests\",\"remote procedure calls\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit JSON-RPC 2.0 Protocol Documentation\",\"og:description\":\"Complete guide to Deribit's JSON-RPC 2.0 API protocol. Learn request/response formats, WebSocket and HTTP transport, error handling, and best practices.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit JSON-RPC 2.0 Protocol Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to Deribit's JSON-RPC 2.0 API protocol including request formats, WebSocket, HTTP, and error handling.\",\"href\":\"/articles/json-rpc-overview\"},{\"title\":\"Error Codes\",\"description\":\"Complete reference of Deribit API error codes, HTTP status meanings, and guidance on handling common failure scenarios in production client code.\",\"keywords\":[\"API errors\",\"error codes\",\"error handling\",\"API troubleshooting\",\"error reference\",\"API debugging\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit API Error Codes Reference - Complete Error Handling Guide\",\"og:description\":\"Complete reference guide for all Deribit API error codes. Learn error handling strategies, retry logic, and troubleshooting techniques.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API Error Codes Reference\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete reference for all Deribit API error codes with handling strategies and troubleshooting guides.\",\"href\":\"/articles/errors\"},{\"title\":\"Using the currency Parameter\",\"description\":\"Discover supported currencies with get_currencies, learn what currency selects on each Deribit method, and avoid invalid currency and spot routing errors.\",\"keywords\":[\"currency parameter\",\"settlement currency\",\"wallet currency\",\"supported currencies\",\"get_currencies\",\"invalid currency\",\"get_positions currency\",\"spot currency\",\"currency any\"],\"og:title\":\"Using the currency Parameter - Deribit API Guide\",\"og:description\":\"Choose the correct currency value for each Deribit API method, discover supported currencies at runtime, and avoid invalid currency and routed spot errors.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API currency Parameter Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"How to use the currency parameter correctly across positions, wallet and market data methods on the Deribit API.\",\"href\":\"/articles/currency-parameter\"}]},{\"group\":\"Methods\",\"pages\":[{\"group\":\"Authentication\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"public/auth\",\"description\":\"$4f\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/auth\",\"keywords\":[\"public/auth\",\"grant_type\",\"client_id\",\"client_secret\",\"refresh_token\",\"timestamp\",\"signature\",\"nonce\",\"data\",\"state\",\"scope\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/auth\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/authentication/public-auth\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/exchange_token\",\"description\":\"Generates a token for a new subject id. This method can be used to switch between subaccounts.\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Fork and Exchange Tokens](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/authentication#fork-and-exchange-tokens)\\n- [Managing Subaccounts](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-subaccounts-api)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fexchange_token)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/exchange_token\",\"keywords\":[\"public/exchange_token\",\"refresh_token\",\"subject_id\",\"scope\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/exchange_token\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/authentication/public-exchange_token\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/fork_token\",\"description\":\"Generates a token for a new named session. This method can be used only with session scoped tokens.\\n\\n**📖 More Details:** [Fork and Exchange Tokens](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/authentication#fork-and-exchange-tokens)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Ffork_token)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/fork_token\",\"keywords\":[\"public/fork_token\",\"refresh_token\",\"session_name\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/fork_token\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/authentication/public-fork_token\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/logout\",\"description\":\"$50\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/logout\",\"keywords\":[\"private/logout\",\"invalidate_token\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/logout\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/authentication/private-logout\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Account Management\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"private/change_api_key_name\",\"description\":\"Updates the display name for an API key. The name is used for identification purposes in the API key list and does not affect the key's functionality or permissions.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Creating new API key on Deribit](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fchange_api_key_name)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/change_api_key_name\",\"keywords\":[\"private/change_api_key_name\",\"id\",\"name\",\"timestamp\",\"client_id\",\"client_secret\",\"public_key\",\"max_scope\",\"enabled\",\"default\",\"enabled_features\",\"ip_whitelist\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/change_api_key_name\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-change_api_key_name\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/change_margin_model\",\"description\":\"Changes the margin model for the authenticated account or a specified subaccount. Margin models determine how margin requirements are calculated (e.g., Standard Margin vs. Portfolio Margin).\\n\\nChanging the margin model may affect margin requirements, available funds, and trading capabilities. Use the `dry_run` parameter to preview the impact of the change before applying it.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Margin types and usage](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/25944811317149-Margin-types-and-usage)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fchange_margin_model)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/change_margin_model\",\"keywords\":[\"private/change_margin_model\",\"user_id\",\"margin_model\",\"dry_run\",\"old_state\",\"new_state\",\"currency\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/change_margin_model\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-change_margin_model\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/change_scope_in_api_key\",\"description\":\"Updates the scope (permissions) for an existing API key. The scope determines which operations the API key can perform (e.g., read-only, read-write, trading, etc.).\\n\\nWhen the scope is changed, the API key immediately loses access to operations outside the new scope. Applications using this key may need to be updated to reflect the new permissions.\\n\\n**[TFA required](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/security-keys)**\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Creating new API key on Deribit](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key)\\n- [Access Scope](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/access-scope)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fchange_scope_in_api_key)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/change_scope_in_api_key\",\"keywords\":[\"private/change_scope_in_api_key\",\"max_scope\",\"id\",\"timestamp\",\"client_id\",\"client_secret\",\"public_key\",\"enabled\",\"default\",\"name\",\"enabled_features\",\"ip_whitelist\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/change_scope_in_api_key\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-change_scope_in_api_key\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/change_subaccount_name\",\"description\":\"Updates the display name (username) for a subaccount. The new name is used for identification purposes and does not affect the subaccount's functionality or access.\\n\\nOnly the main account owner can change subaccount names.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Subaccounts](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-subaccounts-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write` and mainaccount\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fchange_subaccount_name)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/change_subaccount_name\",\"keywords\":[\"private/change_subaccount_name\",\"sid\",\"name\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/change_subaccount_name\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-change_subaccount_name\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/create_api_key\",\"description\":\"Creates a new API key with the specified scope and permissions. API keys are used for programmatic access to the Deribit API and can be restricted to specific operations and IP addresses.\\n\\nThe response includes both the API key ID and the secret key. Store the secret securely as it will not be displayed again. You can view the API key details (without the secret) using the `list_api_keys` method.\\n\\n**Note:** The new API key cannot be granted higher scopes than the API key used for authentication. Attempting to assign a scope that exceeds the authenticating key's permissions will result in an error.\\n\\n**[TFA required](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/security-keys)**\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Creating new API key on Deribit](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key)\\n- [Access Scope](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/access-scope)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcreate_api_key)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/create_api_key\",\"keywords\":[\"private/create_api_key\",\"max_scope\",\"name\",\"public_key\",\"enabled_features\",\"timestamp\",\"client_id\",\"client_secret\",\"enabled\",\"default\",\"ip_whitelist\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/create_api_key\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-create_api_key\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/create_subaccount\",\"description\":\"Creates a new subaccount under the authenticated main account. Subaccounts allow you to organize trading activities and manage risk separately from the main account.\\n\\nThis method takes no parameters. The new subaccount will be created with default settings and can be configured using other subaccount management methods.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Subaccounts](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-subaccounts-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write` and mainaccount\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcreate_subaccount)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/create_subaccount\",\"keywords\":[\"private/create_subaccount\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/create_subaccount\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-create_subaccount\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/delete_member\",\"description\":\"Deletes a Direct Access member from the account. Returns the resulting list of all members\\nconfigured for the account.\\n\\nThis method is dedicated to Starbase. See [Starbase Account Model](https://docs.deribit.com/starbase/account-model)\\nfor an explanation of Members, portfolios, and their relationship to Deribit accounts.\\n\\nRequires Direct Access trading to be enabled for the account.\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write` and mainaccount\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fdelete_member)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/delete_member\",\"keywords\":[\"private/delete_member\",\"member_id\",\"members\",\"is_direct_access_allowed\",\"main_uid\",\"name\",\"is_active\",\"accounts\",\"m_tstamp\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/delete_member\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-delete_member\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/disable_api_key\",\"description\":\"Disables an API key, preventing it from being used to authenticate API requests. The key remains in your account but cannot be used until it is re-enabled.\\n\\nThis is useful for temporarily suspending access without permanently deleting the key. All requests using this key will be rejected until it is enabled again.\\n\\n**[TFA required](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/security-keys)**\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Creating new API key on Deribit](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fdisable_api_key)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/disable_api_key\",\"keywords\":[\"private/disable_api_key\",\"id\",\"timestamp\",\"client_id\",\"client_secret\",\"public_key\",\"max_scope\",\"enabled\",\"default\",\"name\",\"enabled_features\",\"ip_whitelist\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/disable_api_key\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-disable_api_key\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/edit_api_key\",\"description\":\"Updates properties of an existing API key. You can modify the key name, scope, enabled status, features, and IP whitelist. At least one parameter must be provided.\\n\\nChanges take effect immediately. If you modify the scope, the API key will only have access to the newly specified permissions.\\n\\n**[TFA required](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/security-keys)**\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Creating new API key on Deribit](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key)\\n- [Access Scope](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/access-scope)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fedit_api_key)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/edit_api_key\",\"keywords\":[\"private/edit_api_key\",\"id\",\"max_scope\",\"name\",\"enabled\",\"enabled_features\",\"ip_whitelist\",\"timestamp\",\"client_id\",\"client_secret\",\"public_key\",\"default\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/edit_api_key\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-edit_api_key\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/enable_affiliate_program\",\"description\":\"Enables the affiliate program for the authenticated account. Once enabled, you can earn commissions by referring new users to Deribit.\\n\\nAfter enabling, you will receive a unique affiliate link that can be shared with potential users. Commissions are paid based on the trading activity of referred users.\\n\\n**📖 Related Support Article:** [Affiliate Program](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/25944777728797-Affiliate-Program)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fenable_affiliate_program)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/enable_affiliate_program\",\"keywords\":[\"private/enable_affiliate_program\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/enable_affiliate_program\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-enable_affiliate_program\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/enable_api_key\",\"description\":\"Enables a previously disabled API key, restoring its ability to authenticate API requests. The API key can be used immediately after being enabled.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Creating new API key on Deribit](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fenable_api_key)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/enable_api_key\",\"keywords\":[\"private/enable_api_key\",\"id\",\"timestamp\",\"client_id\",\"client_secret\",\"public_key\",\"max_scope\",\"enabled\",\"default\",\"name\",\"enabled_features\",\"ip_whitelist\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/enable_api_key\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-enable_api_key\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_access_log\",\"description\":\"Retrieves a log of API access attempts and authentication events for the authenticated account. The log includes information such as IP addresses, timestamps, API methods called, and authentication status.\\n\\nUse this method to monitor account security, review API usage patterns, and identify unauthorized access attempts. Results can be paginated using the `offset` and `count` parameters.\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_access_log)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_access_log\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_access_log\",\"offset\",\"count\",\"ip\",\"timestamp\",\"country\",\"city\",\"log\",\"data\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_access_log\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_access_log\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_account_summaries\",\"description\":\"Retrieves a per-currency list of account summaries for the authenticated user. Each summary includes balance, equity, available funds, and margin information for each currency.\\n\\nTo retrieve summaries for a specific subaccount, use the `subaccount_id` parameter. When the `extended` parameter is set to `true`, additional account details such as account ID, username, email, and account type are included. Prefer this method over looping `private/get_account_summary` per currency.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_account_summaries)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_account_summaries\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_account_summaries\",\"subaccount_id\",\"extended\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_account_summaries\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_account_summaries\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_account_summary\",\"description\":\"$51\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_account_summary\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_account_summary\",\"currency\",\"subaccount_id\",\"extended\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_account_summary\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_account_summary\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_affiliate_program_info\",\"description\":\"Retrieves information about the affiliate program status for the authenticated account. The response includes the number of referred affiliates, total payouts earned, pending payouts, and the unique affiliate referral link.\\n\\nUse this method to track your affiliate program performance and earnings.\\n\\n**📖 Related Support Article:** [Affiliate Program](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/25944777728797-Affiliate-Program)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_affiliate_program_info)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_affiliate_program_info\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_affiliate_program_info\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_affiliate_program_info\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_affiliate_program_info\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_currencies\",\"description\":\"Returns a list of cryptocurrencies available for the authenticated user's account.\\n\\nThis method takes no parameters. Drive wallet and balance requests from this list rather than hardcoding currencies or using `public/get_currencies`.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_currencies)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_currencies\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_currencies\",\"currency\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_currencies\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_currencies\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_email_language\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the currently configured language preference for email notifications. Returns the language code (e.g., `en`, `ko`, `zh`, `ja`, `ru`) that is used for all email communications sent to the account.\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_email_language)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_email_language\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_email_language\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_email_language\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_email_language\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_members\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the list of Direct Access members configured for the account. A member represents an\\nexternal identity (e.g. a FIX or Direct Access order gateway user) that can be granted Direct\\nAccess trading rights on the account or one of its subaccounts.\\n\\nThis method is dedicated to Starbase. See [Starbase Account Model](https://docs.deribit.com/starbase/account-model)\\nfor an explanation of Members, portfolios, and their relationship to Deribit accounts.\\n\\nWhen called from a subaccount, only members whose `accounts` include that subaccount are\\nreturned, and only the `name` and `is_active` fields are included for each of them.\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_members)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_members\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_members\",\"members\",\"is_direct_access_allowed\",\"member_id\",\"main_uid\",\"name\",\"is_active\",\"accounts\",\"m_tstamp\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_members\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_members\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_new_announcements\",\"description\":\"Retrieves only unread announcements for the authenticated account. Announcements are marked as read when you use the `set_announcement_as_read` method or view them through the web interface.\\n\\nThis method is useful for displaying notification badges or highlighting new announcements that require the user's attention.\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_new_announcements)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_new_announcements\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_new_announcements\",\"body\",\"publication_timestamp\",\"important\",\"confirmation\",\"title\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_new_announcements\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_new_announcements\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_position\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the open position for a specific instrument. Returns detailed position information including size, average entry price, mark price, unrealized P\u0026L, initial margin, maintenance margin, and other position-related metrics.\\n\\nIf no position exists for the specified instrument, the response will indicate a zero position.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_position)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_position\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_position\",\"instrument_name\",\"kind\",\"user_id\",\"average_price\",\"direction\",\"mark_price\",\"delta\",\"gamma\",\"vega\",\"theta\",\"index_price\",\"initial_margin\",\"maintenance_margin\",\"settlement_price\",\"total_profit_loss\",\"floating_profit_loss\",\"realized_profit_loss\",\"size\",\"size_currency\",\"average_price_usd\",\"floating_profit_loss_usd\",\"leverage\",\"realized_funding\",\"interest_value\",\"estimated_liquidation_price\",\"open_orders_margin\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_position\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_position\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_positions\",\"description\":\"Retrieves all open positions for the authenticated account. Returns position details including size, average entry price, mark price, unrealized P\u0026L, initial margin, maintenance margin, and other position-related information.\\n\\nResults can be filtered by currency and instrument kind (future, option, etc.). To retrieve positions for a specific subaccount, use the `subaccount_id` parameter. Spot holdings are balances, not positions — `kind: \\\"spot\\\"` is rejected. Prefer `currency: \\\"any\\\"` over looping currencies.\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_positions)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_positions\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_positions\",\"currency\",\"kind\",\"subaccount_id\",\"instrument_name\",\"user_id\",\"average_price\",\"direction\",\"mark_price\",\"delta\",\"gamma\",\"vega\",\"theta\",\"index_price\",\"initial_margin\",\"maintenance_margin\",\"settlement_price\",\"total_profit_loss\",\"floating_profit_loss\",\"realized_profit_loss\",\"size\",\"size_currency\",\"average_price_usd\",\"floating_profit_loss_usd\",\"leverage\",\"realized_funding\",\"interest_value\",\"estimated_liquidation_price\",\"open_orders_margin\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_positions\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_positions\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_subaccounts\",\"description\":\"Retrieves information about all subaccounts associated with the main account. Returns details such as subaccount IDs, names, and status.\\n\\nWhen called from a subaccount, the response includes limited details for the main account and full details for the subaccount initiating the request.\\n\\nSet the `with_portfolio` parameter to `true` to include portfolio information (balances, positions, etc.) in the response. By default, only subaccount metadata is returned.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Subaccounts](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-subaccounts-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_subaccounts)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_subaccounts\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_subaccounts\",\"with_portfolio\",\"username\",\"type\",\"email\",\"not_confirmed_email\",\"security_keys_enabled\",\"security_keys_assignments\",\"system_name\",\"receive_notifications\",\"is_password\",\"margin_model\",\"proof_id\",\"proof_id_signature\",\"login_enabled\",\"portfolio\",\"btc(example)\",\"margin_balance\",\"currency\",\"maintenance_margin\",\"initial_margin\",\"equity\",\"balance\",\"available_withdrawal_funds\",\"available_funds\",\"additional_reserve\",\"spot_reserve\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_subaccounts\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_subaccounts\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_subaccounts_details\",\"description\":\"Retrieves position details for all subaccounts for a specific currency. Returns positions aggregated across all subaccounts, including size, average entry price, mark price, and P\u0026L information.\\n\\nOptionally include open orders for each subaccount by setting the `with_open_orders` parameter to `true`.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Subaccounts](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-subaccounts-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_subaccounts_details)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_subaccounts_details\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_subaccounts_details\",\"currency\",\"with_open_orders\",\"uid\",\"positions\",\"open_orders\",\"instrument_name\",\"kind\",\"user_id\",\"average_price\",\"direction\",\"mark_price\",\"delta\",\"gamma\",\"vega\",\"theta\",\"index_price\",\"initial_margin\",\"maintenance_margin\",\"settlement_price\",\"total_profit_loss\",\"floating_profit_loss\",\"realized_profit_loss\",\"size\",\"size_currency\",\"average_price_usd\",\"floating_profit_loss_usd\",\"leverage\",\"realized_funding\",\"interest_value\",\"order_id\",\"order_state\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"time_in_force\",\"is_rebalance\",\"is_liquidation\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"price\",\"label\",\"post_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"api\",\"web\",\"mobile\",\"refresh_amount\",\"display_amount\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"filled_amount\",\"advanced\",\"implv\",\"usd\",\"triggered\",\"trigger\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"trigger_reference_price\",\"block_trade\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"replaced\",\"auto_replaced\",\"quote\",\"mmp_group\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trigger_order_id\",\"combo_order_id\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"app_name\",\"mmp_cancelled\",\"cancel_reason\",\"oto_order_ids\",\"trigger_fill_condition\",\"oco_ref\",\"primary_order_id\",\"is_secondary_oto\",\"is_primary_otoco\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_subaccounts_details\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_subaccounts_details\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_transaction_log\",\"description\":\"$52\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_transaction_log\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_transaction_log\",\"currency\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\",\"query\",\"count\",\"subaccount_id\",\"continuation\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_transaction_log\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_transaction_log\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_user_locks\",\"description\":\"Retrieves information about any account locks or restrictions currently active on the authenticated account. Account locks may be applied for security reasons, compliance requirements, or administrative purposes.\\n\\nThe response includes details about the type of lock, reason, and duration (if applicable). Some locks may prevent trading, withdrawals, or other account operations.\\n\\n**📖 Related Support Article:** [Emergency locking an account](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/25944602715805-Emergency-locking-an-account)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_user_locks)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_user_locks\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_user_locks\",\"currency\",\"enabled\",\"message\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_user_locks\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-get_user_locks\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/list_api_keys\",\"description\":\"Retrieves a list of all API keys associated with the authenticated account. The response includes key details such as ID, name, scope, creation date, last usage, and status (enabled/disabled), but does not include the secret keys for security reasons.\\n\\nUse this method to review and manage your API keys, check their permissions, and monitor their usage.\\n\\n**[TFA required](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/security-keys)**\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Creating new API key on Deribit](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Flist_api_keys)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/list_api_keys\",\"keywords\":[\"private/list_api_keys\",\"timestamp\",\"client_id\",\"client_secret\",\"public_key\",\"max_scope\",\"enabled\",\"default\",\"name\",\"enabled_features\",\"ip_whitelist\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/list_api_keys\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-list_api_keys\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/list_custody_accounts\",\"description\":\"Retrieves a list of all custody accounts associated with the authenticated account for a specific currency. Custody accounts are used for clients who require segregated custody of their assets.\\n\\nThe response includes custody account details such as account name, status, balances, and configuration settings.\\n\\n**📖 Related Support Article:** [Custody Options](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/26533163120413-Custody-Options)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Flist_custody_accounts)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/list_custody_accounts\",\"keywords\":[\"private/list_custody_accounts\",\"currency\",\"name\",\"balance\",\"pending_withdrawal_balance\",\"auto_deposit\",\"client_id\",\"external_id\",\"withdrawal_address\",\"withdrawal_address_change\",\"pending_withdrawal_addres\",\"deposit_address\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/list_custody_accounts\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-list_custody_accounts\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/pme/simulate\",\"description\":\"Calculates the Extended Risk Matrix (ERM) and detailed margin information for Portfolio Margin accounts. The ERM provides a comprehensive view of portfolio risk across different scenarios and market conditions.\\n\\nYou can calculate the ERM for a specific currency or for the entire Cross-Collateral portfolio. The response includes margin requirements, risk metrics, and scenario analysis that helps assess portfolio risk under various market conditions.\\n\\nUse this method to understand margin requirements and risk exposure before making trading decisions in a Portfolio Margin account.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Portfolio Margin](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/25944756247837-Portfolio-Margin)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fpme%2Fsimulate)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/pme/simulate\",\"keywords\":[\"private/pme/simulate\",\"currency\",\"add_positions\",\"simulated_positions\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/pme/simulate\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-simulate\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/remove_api_key\",\"description\":\"Permanently deletes an API key from your account. This operation cannot be undone. Once removed, the API key can no longer be used to authenticate requests, and all applications using this key will lose access.\\n\\nConsider disabling the key first if you want to temporarily suspend access, as disabled keys can be re-enabled later.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Creating new API key on Deribit](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fremove_api_key)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/remove_api_key\",\"keywords\":[\"private/remove_api_key\",\"id\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/remove_api_key\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-remove_api_key\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/remove_subaccount\",\"description\":\"Permanently removes a subaccount. The subaccount must be empty (no positions, no open orders, and zero balance) before it can be removed.\\n\\nThis operation cannot be undone. All subaccount data will be permanently deleted.\\n\\n**[TFA required](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/security-keys)**\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Subaccounts](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-subaccounts-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fremove_subaccount)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/remove_subaccount\",\"keywords\":[\"private/remove_subaccount\",\"subaccount_id\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/remove_subaccount\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-remove_subaccount\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/reset_api_key\",\"description\":\"Generates a new secret key for an existing API key while keeping the same key ID and other properties. This is useful if the secret has been compromised or needs to be rotated for security purposes.\\n\\nThe old secret becomes invalid immediately, and the new secret is returned in the response. Store the new secret securely as it will not be displayed again. All applications using the old secret will need to be updated with the new secret.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Creating new API key on Deribit](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/creating-api-key)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Freset_api_key)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/reset_api_key\",\"keywords\":[\"private/reset_api_key\",\"id\",\"timestamp\",\"client_id\",\"client_secret\",\"public_key\",\"max_scope\",\"enabled\",\"default\",\"name\",\"enabled_features\",\"ip_whitelist\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/reset_api_key\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-reset_api_key\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/set_announcement_as_read\",\"description\":\"Marks a specific announcement as read. Once marked as read, the announcement will no longer appear in the `get_new_announcements` response, though it will still be available through `get_announcements`.\\n\\nThis helps track which announcements have been viewed and reduces notification clutter.\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fset_announcement_as_read)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/set_announcement_as_read\",\"keywords\":[\"private/set_announcement_as_read\",\"announcement_id\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/set_announcement_as_read\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-set_announcement_as_read\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/set_disabled_trading_products\",\"description\":\"Configures which trading products (instruments, currencies, or instrument types) are disabled for a subaccount. Disabled products cannot be traded by the subaccount, providing a way to restrict trading activities.\\n\\nThis is useful for risk management and compliance purposes. Only the main account owner can modify trading product restrictions for subaccounts.\\n\\n**[TFA required](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/security-keys)**\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fset_disabled_trading_products)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/set_disabled_trading_products\",\"keywords\":[\"private/set_disabled_trading_products\",\"user_id\",\"trading_products\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/set_disabled_trading_products\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-set_disabled_trading_products\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/set_email_for_subaccount\",\"description\":\"Assigns an email address to a subaccount. This email can be used for direct login to the subaccount and for receiving notifications.\\n\\nThe email address owner will receive a confirmation email with a link to verify the email address. The email must be confirmed before it can be used for login.\\n\\n**[TFA required](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/security-keys)**\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Subaccounts](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-subaccounts-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fset_email_for_subaccount)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/set_email_for_subaccount\",\"keywords\":[\"private/set_email_for_subaccount\",\"sid\",\"email\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/set_email_for_subaccount\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-set_email_for_subaccount\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/set_email_language\",\"description\":\"Sets the preferred language for email notifications sent to the authenticated account. Supported languages include English (`en`), Korean (`ko`), Chinese (`zh`), Japanese (`ja`), and Russian (`ru`).\\n\\nAll future email notifications will be sent in the selected language. This setting does not affect the language of the web interface or API responses.\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fset_email_language)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/set_email_language\",\"keywords\":[\"private/set_email_language\",\"language\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/set_email_language\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-set_email_language\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/set_member\",\"description\":\"Creates a new Direct Access member, or edits an existing one. Returns the resulting list of all\\nmembers configured for the account.\\n\\nThis method is dedicated to Starbase. See [Starbase Account Model](https://docs.deribit.com/starbase/account-model)\\nfor an explanation of Members, portfolios, and their relationship to Deribit accounts.\\n\\nOmit `member_id` to create a new member; a non-empty `accounts` list is then required, and the\\nmember cannot be created inactive. Pass an existing `member_id` to edit that member's `name` or\\n`accounts` list, or to toggle its `is_active` state — toggling `is_active` and changing\\n`name`/`accounts` cannot be done in the same request, so a pure `is_active` toggle must resend\\nthe member's current `name` and `accounts` values.\\n\\nRequires Direct Access trading to be enabled for the account.\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write` and mainaccount\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fset_member)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/set_member\",\"keywords\":[\"private/set_member\",\"member_id\",\"name\",\"is_active\",\"accounts\",\"members\",\"is_direct_access_allowed\",\"main_uid\",\"m_tstamp\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/set_member\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-set_member\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/set_self_trading_config\",\"description\":\"Configures self-trading prevention settings for the account. Self-trading occurs when orders from the same account (or related subaccounts) match against each other.\\n\\nYou can configure whether self-trading is allowed, blocked, or allowed only for specific scenarios. Settings can be extended to apply to subaccounts as well. For Block RFQ trading, separate self-match prevention settings are available.\\n\\n**📖 Related Support Article:** [Account settings page](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/25944634289693-Account-settings-page#heading-4)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fset_self_trading_config)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/set_self_trading_config\",\"keywords\":[\"private/set_self_trading_config\",\"mode\",\"extended_to_subaccounts\",\"block_rfq_self_match_prevention\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/set_self_trading_config\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-set_self_trading_config\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/simulate_portfolio\",\"description\":\"Calculates portfolio margin requirements and risk metrics for simulated positions or the current portfolio. This method helps you understand margin requirements before opening new positions or assess the impact of potential trades.\\n\\nYou can simulate adding new positions to the current portfolio or calculate margin for a completely simulated portfolio. The response includes initial margin, maintenance margin, available funds, and other risk metrics.\\n\\n**Note:** This method has a restricted rate limit of not more than once per second due to the computational complexity of portfolio margin calculations.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Portfolio Margin](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/25944756247837-Portfolio-Margin)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fsimulate_portfolio)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/simulate_portfolio\",\"keywords\":[\"private/simulate_portfolio\",\"currency\",\"add_positions\",\"simulated_positions\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/simulate_portfolio\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-simulate_portfolio\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/toggle_notifications_from_subaccount\",\"description\":\"Enables or disables email and other notifications for a subaccount. When notifications are disabled, the subaccount will not receive email alerts, trade confirmations, or other notification messages.\\n\\nThis setting only affects notifications sent to the subaccount's email address. Notifications sent to the main account are not affected.\\n\\n**[TFA required](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/security-keys)**\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Subaccounts](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-subaccounts-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Ftoggle_notifications_from_subaccount)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/toggle_notifications_from_subaccount\",\"keywords\":[\"private/toggle_notifications_from_subaccount\",\"sid\",\"state\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/toggle_notifications_from_subaccount\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-toggle_notifications_from_subaccount\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/toggle_subaccount_login\",\"description\":\"Enables or disables direct login access for a subaccount. When login is disabled, the subaccount cannot be accessed directly using email and password authentication, but can still be accessed through the main account.\\n\\nIf login is disabled while an active session exists for the subaccount, that session will be immediately terminated.\\n\\n**[TFA required](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/security-keys)**\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Subaccounts](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-subaccounts-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Ftoggle_subaccount_login)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/toggle_subaccount_login\",\"keywords\":[\"private/toggle_subaccount_login\",\"sid\",\"state\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/toggle_subaccount_login\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/private-toggle_subaccount_login\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_announcements\",\"description\":\"Retrieves platform announcements and important notices. Announcements include system updates, maintenance schedules, new features, policy changes, and other important information.\\n\\nResults are returned in reverse chronological order (newest first). The default `start_timestamp` is the current time, and the `count` parameter must be between 1 and 50 (default is 5).\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_announcements)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_announcements\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_announcements\",\"start_timestamp\",\"count\",\"body\",\"publication_timestamp\",\"important\",\"confirmation\",\"title\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_announcements\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/account-management/public-get_announcements\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Block RFQ\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"private/accept_block_rfq\",\"description\":\"**Taker method**\\n\\nAllows Block RFQ taker to accept a quote by sending a single crossing price. The order can be either filled immediately (`fill_or_kill`) or remain active until cancelled (`good_til_cancelled`).\\n\\n**Note:** After Block RFQ creation, a grace period of 5 seconds begins, during which the taker cannot see quotes or trade the Block RFQ.\\n\\nUse [private/get_block_rfqs](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-get_block_rfqs) to retrieve Block RFQ information, or [private/cancel_block_rfq](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-cancel_block_rfq) to cancel a Block RFQ.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_rfq:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Faccept_block_rfq)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/accept_block_rfq\",\"keywords\":[\"private/accept_block_rfq\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"price\",\"amount\",\"direction\",\"hedge\",\"legs\",\"time_in_force\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/accept_block_rfq\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/private-accept_block_rfq\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/add_block_rfq_quote\",\"description\":\"**Maker method**\\n\\nAdds a quote to an existing Block RFQ. To calculate individual leg prices, use [private/get_leg_prices](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/combo-books/private-get_leg_prices).\\n\\nUse [private/get_block_rfqs](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-get_block_rfqs) to retrieve Block RFQ information, or [private/edit_block_rfq_quote](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-edit_block_rfq_quote) to modify an existing quote.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_rfq:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fadd_block_rfq_quote)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/add_block_rfq_quote\",\"keywords\":[\"private/add_block_rfq_quote\",\"label\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"amount\",\"direction\",\"legs\",\"hedge\",\"execution_instruction\",\"price\",\"expires_at\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"block_rfq_quote_id\",\"quote_state\",\"filled_amount\",\"replaced\",\"app_name\",\"quote_state_reason\",\"ratio\",\"instrument_name\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/add_block_rfq_quote\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/private-add_block_rfq_quote\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_all_block_rfq_quotes\",\"description\":\"**Maker method**\\n\\nCancels all user quotes in all Block RFQs. Optionally cancels all quotes in a specific RFQ if the `block_rfq_id` is provided.\\n\\n**Note:** Mass cancellation by label is not supported. This method will cancel all quotes regardless of their labels. To cancel a single quote, use [private/cancel_block_rfq_quote](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-cancel_block_rfq_quote).\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_rfq:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_all_block_rfq_quotes)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_all_block_rfq_quotes\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_all_block_rfq_quotes\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"detailed\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_all_block_rfq_quotes\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/private-cancel_all_block_rfq_quotes\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_block_rfq\",\"description\":\"**Taker method**\\n\\nCancels a Block RFQ using the specified `block_rfq_id`.\\n\\nUse [private/get_block_rfqs](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-get_block_rfqs) to retrieve Block RFQ information, or [private/create_block_rfq](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-create_block_rfq) to create a new Block RFQ.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_rfq:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_block_rfq)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_block_rfq\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_block_rfq\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"expiration_timestamp\",\"role\",\"state\",\"taker_rating\",\"makers\",\"amount\",\"min_trade_amount\",\"asks\",\"bids\",\"legs\",\"hedge\",\"combo_id\",\"label\",\"app_name\",\"mark_price\",\"disclosed\",\"taker\",\"index_prices\",\"included_in_taker_rating\",\"trades\",\"trade_trigger\",\"trade_allocations\",\"price\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"execution_instruction\",\"expires_at\",\"ratio\",\"instrument_name\",\"direction\",\"maker\",\"hedge_amount\",\"cancel_reason\",\"user_id\",\"client_info\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_block_rfq\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/private-cancel_block_rfq\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_block_rfq_quote\",\"description\":\"**Maker method**\\n\\nCancels a single Block RFQ quote. You can identify the quote to cancel using either:\\n\\n- `block_rfq_quote_id` - the unique ID of the quote\\n- `block_rfq_id` + `label` - the Block RFQ ID and the quote label\\n\\n**Note:** Mass cancellation by label is not supported. This method cancels only one quote at a time. To cancel all quotes, use [private/cancel_all_block_rfq_quotes](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-cancel_all_block_rfq_quotes).\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_rfq:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_block_rfq_quote)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_block_rfq_quote\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_block_rfq_quote\",\"block_rfq_quote_id\",\"label\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"quote_state\",\"execution_instruction\",\"price\",\"amount\",\"direction\",\"filled_amount\",\"legs\",\"hedge\",\"replaced\",\"app_name\",\"quote_state_reason\",\"ratio\",\"instrument_name\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_block_rfq_quote\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/private-cancel_block_rfq_quote\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_block_rfq_trigger\",\"description\":\"**Taker method**\\n\\nAllows Block RFQ taker to cancel an active trigger for a Block RFQ. The response includes the full Block RFQ object with the trade trigger state set to cancelled.\\n\\nUse [private/get_block_rfqs](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-get_block_rfqs) to retrieve Block RFQ information.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_rfq:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_block_rfq_trigger)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_block_rfq_trigger\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_block_rfq_trigger\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"expiration_timestamp\",\"role\",\"state\",\"taker_rating\",\"makers\",\"amount\",\"min_trade_amount\",\"asks\",\"bids\",\"legs\",\"hedge\",\"combo_id\",\"label\",\"app_name\",\"mark_price\",\"disclosed\",\"taker\",\"index_prices\",\"included_in_taker_rating\",\"trades\",\"trade_trigger\",\"trade_allocations\",\"price\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"execution_instruction\",\"expires_at\",\"ratio\",\"instrument_name\",\"direction\",\"maker\",\"hedge_amount\",\"cancel_reason\",\"user_id\",\"client_info\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_block_rfq_trigger\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/private-cancel_block_rfq_trigger\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/create_block_rfq\",\"description\":\"**Taker method**\\n\\nCreates a new Block RFQ. Use [private/get_block_rfqs](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-get_block_rfqs) to retrieve Block RFQ information.\\n\\n**Block RFQ pre-allocation:** The taker can split the total amount between different (sub)accounts using the `trade_allocations` parameter. The taker can also allocate to himself. Each allocation must specify either `user_id` (for direct allocation) or `client_info` object (for broker allocation), and `amount`.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_rfq:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcreate_block_rfq)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/create_block_rfq\",\"keywords\":[\"private/create_block_rfq\",\"legs\",\"trade_allocations\",\"hedge\",\"label\",\"makers\",\"disclosed\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"expiration_timestamp\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"role\",\"state\",\"taker_rating\",\"amount\",\"min_trade_amount\",\"asks\",\"bids\",\"combo_id\",\"app_name\",\"mark_price\",\"taker\",\"index_prices\",\"included_in_taker_rating\",\"trades\",\"trade_trigger\",\"price\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"execution_instruction\",\"expires_at\",\"ratio\",\"instrument_name\",\"direction\",\"maker\",\"hedge_amount\",\"cancel_reason\",\"user_id\",\"client_info\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/create_block_rfq\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/private-create_block_rfq\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/edit_block_rfq_quote\",\"description\":\"**Maker method**\\n\\nEdits a Block RFQ quote using the specified `block_rfq_quote_id`. Alternatively, you can use a combination of `block_rfq_id` and `label` to edit the quote.\\n\\nUse [private/add_block_rfq_quote](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-add_block_rfq_quote) to add new quotes, or [private/cancel_block_rfq_quote](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-cancel_block_rfq_quote) to cancel quotes.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_rfq:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fedit_block_rfq_quote)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/edit_block_rfq_quote\",\"keywords\":[\"private/edit_block_rfq_quote\",\"legs\",\"amount\",\"block_rfq_quote_id\",\"label\",\"hedge\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"price\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"quote_state\",\"execution_instruction\",\"direction\",\"filled_amount\",\"replaced\",\"app_name\",\"quote_state_reason\",\"ratio\",\"instrument_name\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/edit_block_rfq_quote\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/private-edit_block_rfq_quote\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_block_rfq_makers\",\"description\":\"Returns a list of all available Block RFQ makers. This method takes no parameters.\\n\\nUse this method to retrieve the list of makers that can be specified when creating a Block RFQ with [private/create_block_rfq](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-create_block_rfq).\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_rfq:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_block_rfq_makers)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_block_rfq_makers\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_block_rfq_makers\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_block_rfq_makers\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/private-get_block_rfq_makers\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_block_rfq_quotes\",\"description\":\"**Maker method**\\n\\nRetrieves all open quotes for Block RFQs. When a `block_rfq_id` is specified, only the open quotes for that particular Block RFQ will be returned. When a `label` is specified, all quotes with this label are returned. `block_rfq_quote_id` returns one specific quote.\\n\\nUse [private/add_block_rfq_quote](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-add_block_rfq_quote) to add quotes, or [private/get_block_rfqs](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-get_block_rfqs) to retrieve Block RFQ information.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_rfq:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_block_rfq_quotes)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_block_rfq_quotes\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_block_rfq_quotes\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"label\",\"block_rfq_quote_id\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"quote_state\",\"execution_instruction\",\"price\",\"amount\",\"direction\",\"filled_amount\",\"legs\",\"hedge\",\"replaced\",\"app_name\",\"quote_state_reason\",\"ratio\",\"instrument_name\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_block_rfq_quotes\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/private-get_block_rfq_quotes\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_block_rfq_user_info\",\"description\":\"Returns identity and rating information for the requesting account and its subaccounts. Includes both group-level and individual user-level alias data, if available.\\n\\nThis information is useful for understanding your Block RFQ maker identity and rating when participating in Block RFQ trades.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_rfq:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_block_rfq_user_info)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_block_rfq_user_info\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_block_rfq_user_info\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_block_rfq_user_info\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/private-get_block_rfq_user_info\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_block_rfqs\",\"description\":\"Returns a list of Block RFQs that were either created by the user or assigned to them as a maker, sorted in descending order.\\n\\n`trades` and `mark_price` are only visible for the filled Block RFQ. When a `block_rfq_id` is specified, only that particular Block RFQ will be returned. If called by a `taker`, response will additionally include `makers` list and `label` if previously provided. If called by the `maker`, the `trades` will include the maker's alias, but only for trades in which this maker participated. Can be optionally filtered by currency.\\n\\nUse [private/get_block_rfq_quotes](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-get_block_rfq_quotes) to retrieve quotes for Block RFQs.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_rfq:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_block_rfqs)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_block_rfqs\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_block_rfqs\",\"count\",\"state\",\"role\",\"continuation\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"currency\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_block_rfqs\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/private-get_block_rfqs\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_block_rfq_trades\",\"description\":\"Returns a list of recent Block RFQ trades. Can be optionally filtered by currency.\\n\\nThis is a public method that provides market data about completed Block RFQ trades. For private Block RFQ information, use [private/get_block_rfqs](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-rfq/private-get_block_rfqs).\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_block_rfq_trades)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_block_rfq_trades\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_block_rfq_trades\",\"currency\",\"continuation\",\"count\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_block_rfq_trades\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-rfq/public-get_block_rfq_trades\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Block Trade\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"private/approve_block_trade\",\"description\":\"$53\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/approve_block_trade\",\"keywords\":[\"private/approve_block_trade\",\"timestamp\",\"nonce\",\"role\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/approve_block_trade\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-trade/private-approve_block_trade\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/execute_block_trade\",\"description\":\"$54\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/execute_block_trade\",\"keywords\":[\"private/execute_block_trade\",\"timestamp\",\"nonce\",\"role\",\"trades\",\"counterparty_signature\",\"app_name\",\"broker_code\",\"broker_name\",\"trade_id\",\"trade_seq\",\"instrument_name\",\"starbase_timestamp\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"advanced\",\"order_id\",\"matching_id\",\"direction\",\"tick_direction\",\"index_price\",\"price\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"iv\",\"underlying_price\",\"liquidation\",\"liquidity\",\"fee\",\"fee_currency\",\"label\",\"state\",\"block_trade_id\",\"block_trade_leg_count\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"block_rfq_quote_id\",\"reduce_only\",\"post_only\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"api\",\"profit_loss\",\"mark_price\",\"legs\",\"combo_id\",\"combo_trade_id\",\"starbase_match_id\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trade_allocations\",\"user_id\",\"client_info\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/execute_block_trade\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-trade/private-execute_block_trade\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_block_trade\",\"description\":\"Returns information about a specific block trade identified by `block_trade_id`.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_block_trade)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_block_trade\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_block_trade\",\"id\",\"timestamp\",\"trades\",\"app_name\",\"broker_code\",\"broker_name\",\"trade_id\",\"trade_seq\",\"instrument_name\",\"starbase_timestamp\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"advanced\",\"order_id\",\"matching_id\",\"direction\",\"tick_direction\",\"index_price\",\"price\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"iv\",\"underlying_price\",\"liquidation\",\"liquidity\",\"fee\",\"fee_currency\",\"label\",\"state\",\"block_trade_id\",\"block_trade_leg_count\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"block_rfq_quote_id\",\"reduce_only\",\"post_only\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"api\",\"profit_loss\",\"mark_price\",\"legs\",\"combo_id\",\"combo_trade_id\",\"starbase_match_id\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trade_allocations\",\"user_id\",\"client_info\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_block_trade\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-trade/private-get_block_trade\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_block_trade_requests\",\"description\":\"$55\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_block_trade_requests\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_block_trade_requests\",\"broker_code\",\"nonce\",\"timestamp\",\"trades\",\"app_name\",\"username\",\"role\",\"user_id\",\"broker_name\",\"state\",\"counterparty_state\",\"combo_id\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_block_trade_requests\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-trade/private-get_block_trade_requests\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_block_trades\",\"description\":\"Returns a list of the user's block trades. If currency is not provided, returns block trades for all currencies. `block_rfq_id` can be provided to receive block trades related to that particular Block RFQ.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_block_trades)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_block_trades\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_block_trades\",\"currency\",\"count\",\"start_id\",\"end_id\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"broker_code\",\"timestamp\",\"trades\",\"app_name\",\"broker_name\",\"trade_id\",\"trade_seq\",\"instrument_name\",\"starbase_timestamp\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"advanced\",\"order_id\",\"matching_id\",\"direction\",\"tick_direction\",\"index_price\",\"price\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"iv\",\"underlying_price\",\"liquidation\",\"liquidity\",\"fee\",\"fee_currency\",\"label\",\"state\",\"block_trade_id\",\"block_trade_leg_count\",\"block_rfq_quote_id\",\"reduce_only\",\"post_only\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"api\",\"profit_loss\",\"mark_price\",\"legs\",\"combo_id\",\"combo_trade_id\",\"starbase_match_id\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trade_allocations\",\"user_id\",\"client_info\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_block_trades\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-trade/private-get_block_trades\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_broker_clients\",\"description\":\"$56\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_broker_clients\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_broker_clients\",\"client_id\",\"include_subaccounts\",\"client_name\",\"company_name\",\"broker_code\",\"main_user_id\",\"broker_sub_user_id\",\"lei\",\"brn\",\"links\",\"client_link_id\",\"user_id\",\"name\",\"note\",\"state\",\"confirmations_required\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_broker_clients\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-trade/private-get_broker_clients\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_broker_trade_requests\",\"description\":\"**Broker Method** Provides a list of broker block trade requests including pending approvals, declined trades, and expired trades. `timestamp` and `nonce` received in response can be used to approve or reject the pending broker block trade. This method takes no parameters.\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_broker_trade_requests)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_broker_trade_requests\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_broker_trade_requests\",\"timestamp\",\"state\",\"trades\",\"maker\",\"taker\",\"nonce\",\"amount\",\"direction\",\"price\",\"instrument_name\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_broker_trade_requests\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-trade/private-get_broker_trade_requests\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_broker_trades\",\"description\":\"**Broker Method** Returns list of broker block trades. If currency is not provided, returns broker block trades for all currencies.\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_broker_trades)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_broker_trades\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_broker_trades\",\"currency\",\"count\",\"start_id\",\"end_id\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_broker_trades\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-trade/private-get_broker_trades\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/invalidate_block_trade_signature\",\"description\":\"Invalidates a block trade signature, effectively cancelling the block trade. This can be called at any time before [private/execute_block_trade](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/block-trade/private-execute_block_trade) is called.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Finvalidate_block_trade_signature)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/invalidate_block_trade_signature\",\"keywords\":[\"private/invalidate_block_trade_signature\",\"signature\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/invalidate_block_trade_signature\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-trade/private-invalidate_block_trade_signature\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/reject_block_trade\",\"description\":\"$57\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/reject_block_trade\",\"keywords\":[\"private/reject_block_trade\",\"timestamp\",\"nonce\",\"role\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/reject_block_trade\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-trade/private-reject_block_trade\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/simulate_block_trade\",\"description\":\"Checks if a block trade can be executed without actually executing it. Use this method to verify that a block trade will succeed before proceeding with the actual execution.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fsimulate_block_trade)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/simulate_block_trade\",\"keywords\":[\"private/simulate_block_trade\",\"role\",\"trades\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/simulate_block_trade\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-trade/private-simulate_block_trade\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/verify_block_trade\",\"description\":\"Verifies and creates a block trade signature. This is the first step in the block trade workflow - the first party calls this method to generate a signature that must be shared with the second party.\\n\\n**Note:** In the API, the `direction` field is always expressed from the maker's perspective. This means that when you accept a block trade as a taker, the direction shown in the API represents the opposite side of your trade. For example, if you are buying puts as a taker, the API will show the operation as a \\\"sell put\\\" (maker's perspective), and you will be verifying and accepting a \\\"sell put\\\" block trade.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `block_trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fverify_block_trade)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/verify_block_trade\",\"keywords\":[\"private/verify_block_trade\",\"timestamp\",\"nonce\",\"role\",\"trades\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/verify_block_trade\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/block-trade/private-verify_block_trade\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Combo Books\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"private/create_combo\",\"description\":\"Verifies and creates a combo book or returns an existing combo matching the given trades. Combos allow trading on multiple instruments (futures and options) simultaneously as a single strategy.\\n\\nIf a combo matching the provided trades already exists, this method returns the existing combo. Otherwise, it creates a new combo book with the specified leg structure.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcreate_combo)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/create_combo\",\"keywords\":[\"private/create_combo\",\"trades\",\"instrument_id\",\"state\",\"state_timestamp\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"legs\",\"instrument_name\",\"amount\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/create_combo\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/combo-books/private-create_combo\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_leg_prices\",\"description\":\"Returns individual leg prices for a given combo structure based on an aggregated price of the strategy and the mark prices of the individual legs.\\n\\n**Note:** Leg prices change dynamically with mark price fluctuations, and the algorithm is calibrated only for conventional option structures and future spreads. This method supports both inverse strategies and known linear structures within a single currency pair.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_leg_prices)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_leg_prices\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_leg_prices\",\"legs\",\"price\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_leg_prices\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/combo-books/private-get_leg_prices\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_combo_details\",\"description\":\"Retrieves a live combo by `combo_id`: legs, combo `state`, `state_timestamp`, `creation_timestamp`, and `instrument_id`. This is not the full instrument spec — use `public/get_instrument` with the same ID for tick size, commissions, and book `state`.\\n\\nLooks up the live combo table only. Unknown IDs fail with `combo not found`; malformed IDs fail with `wrong format`. Expired or archivized combos that `public/get_combo_ids` no longer lists can still be loaded as instruments via `public/get_instrument`.\\n\\nUse [public/get_combo_ids](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/combo-books/public-get_combo_ids) to list live combo IDs.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_combo_details)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_combo_details\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_combo_details\",\"combo_id\",\"instrument_id\",\"state\",\"state_timestamp\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"legs\",\"instrument_name\",\"amount\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_combo_details\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/combo-books/public-get_combo_details\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_combo_ids\",\"description\":\"Retrieves combo IDs for a required settlement `currency`. `\\\"any\\\"` is not accepted here — use `public/get_combos` with `currency=any` for active combos across currencies.\\n\\n`state` defaults to `\\\"any\\\"`, which returns **active and inactive** IDs and excludes `closed`. Pass `\\\"active\\\"` or `\\\"inactive\\\"` to filter. Public clients cannot select `closed` or `archivized`.\\n\\nUse [public/get_combo_details](https://docs.deribit.com/api-reference/combo-books/public-get_combo_details) for legs and timestamps of a live combo. Archivized combos are not in this list; look them up with `public/get_instrument`.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_combo_ids)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_combo_ids\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_combo_ids\",\"currency\",\"state\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_combo_ids\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/combo-books/public-get_combo_ids\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_combos\",\"description\":\"$58\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_combos\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_combos\",\"currency\",\"instrument_id\",\"state\",\"state_timestamp\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"legs\",\"instrument_name\",\"amount\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_combos\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/combo-books/public-get_combos\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"LSP\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"private/get_lsp_participant_config\",\"description\":\"$59\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_lsp_participant_config\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_lsp_participant_config\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_lsp_participant_config\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/lsp/private-get_lsp_participant_config\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_lsp_participants\",\"description\":\"Lists the LSP (Liquidity Support Program) participant subaccounts configured under the authenticated main account.\\n\\nMust be called with an API key belonging to the main account — returns an error if called from a subaccount.\\n\\nUse the `detailed` parameter to include each participant's full configuration alongside its `user_id` and `enabled` state.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_lsp_participants)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_lsp_participants\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_lsp_participants\",\"detailed\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_lsp_participants\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/lsp/private-get_lsp_participants\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_lsp_participants_usage\",\"description\":\"$5a\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_lsp_participants_usage\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_lsp_participants_usage\",\"user_id\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_lsp_participants_usage\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/lsp/private-get_lsp_participants_usage\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_lsp_usage\",\"description\":\"$5b\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_lsp_usage\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_lsp_usage\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_lsp_usage\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/lsp/private-get_lsp_usage\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Market Data\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"public/get_apr_history\",\"description\":\"Retrieves historical Annual Percentage Rate (APR) data for yield-generating tokens. APR represents the annualized return rate for holding these tokens on Deribit.\\n\\nThis method is only applicable to yield-generating tokens: `USDE`, `STETH`, `USDC`, and `BUILD`. Use the `limit` parameter to specify the number of days to retrieve (default 365, maximum 365), and `before` to retrieve APR history before a specific epoch day.\\n\\n**📖 Related Support Article:** [Yield reward-bearing coins](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/31424939199261-Yield-reward-bearing-coins)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_apr_history)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_apr_history\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_apr_history\",\"currency\",\"limit\",\"before\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_apr_history\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_apr_history\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_book_summary_by_currency\",\"description\":\"Retrieves summary information such as open interest, 24-hour volume, best bid/ask prices, last trade price, and other market statistics for all instruments in a given currency.\\n\\nResults can be filtered by instrument kind (future, option, etc.). This method provides a quick overview of market activity across all instruments for a currency.\\n\\n**Note:** For real-time updates, we recommend using the WebSocket subscription to `ticker.{instrument_name}.{interval}` instead of polling this endpoint.\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\\n- [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_book_summary_by_currency)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_book_summary_by_currency\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_book_summary_by_currency\",\"currency\",\"kind\",\"instrument_name\",\"high\",\"low\",\"base_currency\",\"quote_currency\",\"volume\",\"bid_price\",\"ask_price\",\"mid_price\",\"mark_price\",\"last\",\"open_interest\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"estimated_delivery_price\",\"volume_usd\",\"volume_notional\",\"current_funding\",\"funding_8h\",\"mark_iv\",\"interest_rate\",\"underlying_index\",\"underlying_price\",\"price_change\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_book_summary_by_currency\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_book_summary_by_currency\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_book_summary_by_instrument\",\"description\":\"Retrieves summary information such as open interest, 24-hour volume, best bid/ask prices, last trade price, mark price, and other market statistics for a specific instrument.\\n\\nThis method provides a quick overview of current market activity and liquidity for a single instrument.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_book_summary_by_instrument)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_book_summary_by_instrument\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_book_summary_by_instrument\",\"instrument_name\",\"high\",\"low\",\"base_currency\",\"quote_currency\",\"volume\",\"bid_price\",\"ask_price\",\"mid_price\",\"mark_price\",\"last\",\"open_interest\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"estimated_delivery_price\",\"volume_usd\",\"volume_notional\",\"current_funding\",\"funding_8h\",\"mark_iv\",\"interest_rate\",\"underlying_index\",\"underlying_price\",\"price_change\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_book_summary_by_instrument\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_book_summary_by_instrument\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_contract_size\",\"description\":\"$5c\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_contract_size\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_contract_size\",\"instrument_name\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_contract_size\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_contract_size\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_currencies\",\"description\":\"Retrieves all cryptocurrencies supported by the Deribit API. Returns a list of available currencies with their codes and basic information.\\n\\nThis method takes no parameters and is useful for discovering which currencies are available for trading on the platform.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_currencies)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_currencies\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_currencies\",\"withdrawal_fee\",\"withdrawal_priorities\",\"min_withdrawal_fee\",\"currency\",\"currency_long\",\"min_confirmations\",\"coin_type\",\"in_cross_collateral_pool\",\"apr\",\"network_fee\",\"network_currency\",\"decimals\",\"currency_uuid\",\"coinbase_networks\",\"name\",\"value\",\"resource_name\",\"display_name\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_currencies\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_currencies\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_delivery_prices\",\"description\":\"Retrieves historical delivery prices for a given index. Delivery prices are the settlement prices used when futures or options contracts expire and are settled.\\n\\nResults can be paginated using the `offset` and `count` parameters. This method is useful for analyzing historical settlement prices and understanding how contracts have been settled over time.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_delivery_prices)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_delivery_prices\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_delivery_prices\",\"index_name\",\"offset\",\"count\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_delivery_prices\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_delivery_prices\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_expirations\",\"description\":\"$5d\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_expirations\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_expirations\",\"currency\",\"kind\",\"currency_pair\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_expirations\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_expirations\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_funding_chart_data\",\"description\":\"Retrieves funding rate chart data points for a PERPETUAL instrument within a given time period. The data is formatted for use in charting applications and includes funding rate values at regular intervals.\\n\\nUse the `length` parameter to specify the time period for which to retrieve chart data. This method is useful for visualizing funding rate trends over time.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_funding_chart_data)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_funding_chart_data\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_funding_chart_data\",\"instrument_name\",\"length\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_funding_chart_data\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_funding_chart_data\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_funding_rate_history\",\"description\":\"Retrieves hourly historical funding rate (interest rate) data for a PERPETUAL instrument over a specified time period. Funding rates are periodic payments exchanged between long and short positions in perpetual contracts.\\n\\nThe response includes hourly funding rate values, which can be used to analyze funding rate trends and calculate historical funding costs. This method is applicable only for PERPETUAL instruments.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_funding_rate_history)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_funding_rate_history\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_funding_rate_history\",\"instrument_name\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\",\"timestamp\",\"prev_index_price\",\"index_price\",\"interest_1h\",\"interest_8h\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_funding_rate_history\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_funding_rate_history\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_funding_rate_value\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the funding rate (interest rate) value for a perpetual instrument over a specified time period. Funding rates are periodic payments exchanged between long and short positions in perpetual contracts.\\n\\nThis method is applicable only for PERPETUAL instruments. The funding rate is typically expressed as a percentage and is used to keep the perpetual contract price aligned with the underlying index price.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_funding_rate_value)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_funding_rate_value\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_funding_rate_value\",\"instrument_name\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_funding_rate_value\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_funding_rate_value\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_historical_volatility\",\"description\":\"Provides historical volatility data for a given cryptocurrency. Historical volatility measures the degree of price variation over a past period and is useful for risk assessment and option pricing.\\n\\nThe response includes volatility statistics calculated from historical price movements. This data can be used for portfolio risk analysis and understanding market conditions.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_historical_volatility)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_historical_volatility\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_historical_volatility\",\"currency\",\"timestamp\",\"value\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_historical_volatility\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_historical_volatility\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_index_price\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the current index price value for a given index name. Index prices are used as reference prices for mark price calculations and settlement.\\n\\nUse `get_index_price_names` or `get_supported_index_names` to retrieve available index names.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_index_price)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_index_price\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_index_price\",\"index_name\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_index_price\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_index_price\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_index_price_names\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the identifiers (names) of all supported price indexes. Price indexes are reference prices used for mark price calculations, settlement, and other market operations.\\n\\nWhen the `extended` parameter is set to `true`, the response includes additional information such as whether future combo creation and option combo creation are enabled for each index.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_index_price_names)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_index_price_names\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_index_price_names\",\"extended\",\"name\",\"future_combo_creation_enabled\",\"option_combo_creation_enabled\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_index_price_names\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_index_price_names\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_instrument\",\"description\":\"$5e\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_instrument\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_instrument\",\"instrument_name\",\"kind\",\"settlement_currency\",\"counter_currency\",\"base_currency\",\"quote_currency\",\"min_trade_amount\",\"instrument_id\",\"is_active\",\"settlement_period\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"tick_size\",\"tick_size_steps\",\"expiration_timestamp\",\"strike\",\"option_type\",\"future_type\",\"instrument_type\",\"contract_size\",\"lot_size\",\"maker_commission\",\"taker_commission\",\"max_liquidation_commission\",\"maker_max_commission\",\"taker_max_commission\",\"liquidation_max_commission\",\"settlement_max_commission\",\"margin_params\",\"trading_bandwidth_fraction\",\"perpetual_dempener\",\"perpetual_max_funding\",\"block_trade_commission\",\"block_trade_tick_size\",\"block_trade_min_trade_amount\",\"max_leverage\",\"max_non_default_leverage\",\"price_index\",\"underlying_type\",\"state\",\"base_currency_uuid\",\"quote_currency_uuid\",\"index_id\",\"product_group\",\"is_csr\",\"is_cbe_routed\",\"above_price\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_instrument\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_instrument\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_instruments\",\"description\":\"$5f\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_instruments\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_instruments\",\"currency\",\"kind\",\"expired\",\"extended\",\"settlement_currency\",\"counter_currency\",\"base_currency\",\"quote_currency\",\"min_trade_amount\",\"instrument_name\",\"instrument_id\",\"is_active\",\"settlement_period\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"tick_size\",\"tick_size_steps\",\"expiration_timestamp\",\"strike\",\"option_type\",\"future_type\",\"instrument_type\",\"contract_size\",\"lot_size\",\"maker_commission\",\"taker_commission\",\"max_liquidation_commission\",\"maker_max_commission\",\"taker_max_commission\",\"liquidation_max_commission\",\"settlement_max_commission\",\"margin_params\",\"trading_bandwidth_fraction\",\"perpetual_dempener\",\"perpetual_max_funding\",\"block_trade_commission\",\"block_trade_tick_size\",\"block_trade_min_trade_amount\",\"max_leverage\",\"max_non_default_leverage\",\"price_index\",\"underlying_type\",\"state\",\"base_currency_uuid\",\"quote_currency_uuid\",\"index_id\",\"product_group\",\"is_csr\",\"is_cbe_routed\",\"above_price\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_instruments\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_instruments\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_last_settlements_by_currency\",\"description\":\"$60\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_last_settlements_by_currency\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_last_settlements_by_currency\",\"currency\",\"type\",\"count\",\"continuation\",\"search_start_timestamp\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_last_settlements_by_currency\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_last_settlements_by_currency\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_last_settlements_by_instrument\",\"description\":\"$61\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_last_settlements_by_instrument\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_last_settlements_by_instrument\",\"instrument_name\",\"type\",\"count\",\"continuation\",\"search_start_timestamp\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_last_settlements_by_instrument\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_last_settlements_by_instrument\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_last_trades_by_currency\",\"description\":\"$62\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_last_trades_by_currency\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_last_trades_by_currency\",\"currency\",\"kind\",\"start_id\",\"end_id\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\",\"count\",\"sorting\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_last_trades_by_currency\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_last_trades_by_currency\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_last_trades_by_currency_and_time\",\"description\":\"$63\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_last_trades_by_currency_and_time\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_last_trades_by_currency_and_time\",\"currency\",\"kind\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\",\"count\",\"sorting\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_last_trades_by_currency_and_time\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_last_trades_by_currency_and_time\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_last_trades_by_instrument\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the latest trades that have occurred for a specific instrument. Returns trade details including price, amount, direction, timestamp, and trade ID.\\n\\nResults can be filtered by sequence number range or timestamp range. Use the `count` parameter to limit the number of trades returned, and `sorting` to control the order (ascending or descending by trade ID).\\n\\n**Note:** For spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, this call is not supported. Use [Get product trades](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/api-reference/exchange-api/rest-api/products/get-product-trades) directly for full trade history.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_last_trades_by_instrument)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_last_trades_by_instrument\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_last_trades_by_instrument\",\"instrument_name\",\"start_seq\",\"end_seq\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\",\"count\",\"sorting\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_last_trades_by_instrument\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_last_trades_by_instrument\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_last_trades_by_instrument_and_time\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the latest trades that have occurred for a specific instrument within a specified time range. Returns trade details including price, amount, direction, timestamp, and trade ID.\\n\\nUse the `count` parameter to limit the number of trades returned, and `sorting` to control the order (ascending or descending by trade ID). This method is useful for analyzing trading activity over specific time periods.\\n\\n**Note:** For spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, this call is not supported. Use [Get product trades](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/api-reference/exchange-api/rest-api/products/get-product-trades) directly for full trade history.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_last_trades_by_instrument_and_time)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_last_trades_by_instrument_and_time\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_last_trades_by_instrument_and_time\",\"instrument_name\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\",\"count\",\"sorting\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_last_trades_by_instrument_and_time\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_last_trades_by_instrument_and_time\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_mark_price_history\",\"description\":\"Retrieves 5-minute historical mark price data for an instrument. Mark prices are used for margin calculations and position valuations.\\n\\n**Note:** Currently, mark price history is available only for a subset of options that participate in volatility index calculations. All other instruments, including futures and perpetuals, will return an empty list.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_mark_price_history)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_mark_price_history\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_mark_price_history\",\"instrument_name\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_mark_price_history\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_mark_price_history\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_order_book\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the order book (bids and asks) for a given instrument, along with other market values such as best bid/ask prices, last trade price, mark price, and index price.\\n\\nThe order book depth can be controlled using the `depth` parameter, which accepts values from 1 to 10000. The response includes price levels sorted by price (bids descending, asks ascending).\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_order_book)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_order_book\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_order_book\",\"instrument_name\",\"depth\",\"timestamp\",\"state\",\"stats\",\"open_interest\",\"best_bid_price\",\"best_bid_amount\",\"best_ask_price\",\"best_ask_amount\",\"index_price\",\"min_price\",\"max_price\",\"mark_price\",\"last_price\",\"underlying_price\",\"underlying_index\",\"interest_rate\",\"bid_iv\",\"ask_iv\",\"mark_iv\",\"greeks\",\"funding_8h\",\"current_funding\",\"delivery_price\",\"settlement_price\",\"bids\",\"asks\",\"volume\",\"low\",\"high\",\"price_change\",\"volume_usd\",\"delta\",\"gamma\",\"rho\",\"theta\",\"vega\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_order_book\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_order_book\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_order_book_by_instrument_id\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the order book (bids and asks) for a given instrument ID, along with other market values such as best bid/ask prices, last trade price, mark price, and index price.\\n\\nThis method is similar to `get_order_book` but uses instrument ID instead of instrument name. The order book depth can be controlled using the `depth` parameter, which accepts values from 1 to 10000.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_order_book_by_instrument_id)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_order_book_by_instrument_id\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_order_book_by_instrument_id\",\"instrument_id\",\"depth\",\"instrument_name\",\"timestamp\",\"state\",\"stats\",\"open_interest\",\"best_bid_price\",\"best_bid_amount\",\"best_ask_price\",\"best_ask_amount\",\"index_price\",\"min_price\",\"max_price\",\"mark_price\",\"last_price\",\"underlying_price\",\"underlying_index\",\"interest_rate\",\"bid_iv\",\"ask_iv\",\"mark_iv\",\"greeks\",\"funding_8h\",\"current_funding\",\"delivery_price\",\"settlement_price\",\"bids\",\"asks\",\"volume\",\"low\",\"high\",\"price_change\",\"volume_usd\",\"delta\",\"gamma\",\"rho\",\"theta\",\"vega\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_order_book_by_instrument_id\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_order_book_by_instrument_id\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_supported_index_names\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the identifiers (names) of all supported price indexes, optionally filtered by index type. Price indexes are reference prices used for mark price calculations, settlement, and other market operations.\\n\\nUse the `type` parameter to filter indexes by type (e.g., spot, futures, etc.). This method helps discover available indexes for use with other API methods.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_supported_index_names)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_supported_index_names\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_supported_index_names\",\"type\",\"name\",\"future_combo_creation_enabled\",\"option_combo_creation_enabled\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_supported_index_names\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_supported_index_names\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_trade_volumes\",\"description\":\"Retrieves aggregated 24-hour trade volumes for different instrument types and currencies. The volume statistics include all executed trades across the platform.\\n\\n**Note:** Position moves are not included in this volume. Block trades and Block RFQ trades are included in the volume calculations.\\n\\nUse the `extended` parameter to include additional volume statistics and breakdowns.\\n\\n**Note:** For currencies with spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, `spot_volume` is omitted, as are `spot_volume_7d` and `spot_volume_30d` when `extended` is used. Use [Get all product volume](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/api-reference/exchange-api/rest-api/products/get-all-product-volume) for venue spot volume.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_trade_volumes)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_trade_volumes\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_trade_volumes\",\"extended\",\"currency\",\"calls_volume\",\"puts_volume\",\"futures_volume\",\"spot_volume\",\"calls_volume_7d\",\"puts_volume_7d\",\"futures_volume_7d\",\"spot_volume_7d\",\"calls_volume_30d\",\"puts_volume_30d\",\"futures_volume_30d\",\"spot_volume_30d\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_trade_volumes\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_trade_volumes\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_tradingview_chart_data\",\"description\":\"Retrieves publicly available market data formatted for generating TradingView-compatible candle charts. The data includes open, high, low, close (OHLC) prices and volume for specified time intervals.\\n\\nUse the `chart_resolution` parameter to specify the candle interval (e.g., 1m, 5m, 1h, 1d). This method provides the standard format used by TradingView and other charting platforms.\\n\\n**Note:** For spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, this call is not supported. Use [Get product candles](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/api-reference/exchange-api/rest-api/products/get-product-candles) instead.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_tradingview_chart_data)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_tradingview_chart_data\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_tradingview_chart_data\",\"instrument_name\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\",\"resolution\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_tradingview_chart_data\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_tradingview_chart_data\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_volatility_index_data\",\"description\":\"Retrieves volatility index (VIX) chart data formatted as candles. Volatility indexes measure market expectations of future volatility and are useful for risk assessment and trading strategies.\\n\\nUse the `vix_resolution` parameter to specify the candle interval. The data shows historical volatility index values over time and is formatted for use in charting applications.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_volatility_index_data)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_volatility_index_data\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_volatility_index_data\",\"currency\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\",\"resolution\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_volatility_index_data\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_volatility_index_data\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/ticker\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the ticker (24-hour statistics) for a specific instrument. The ticker includes the last trade price, best bid/ask prices, 24-hour high/low, 24-hour volume, open interest, mark price, and other market statistics.\\n\\nThis is a lightweight method for getting current market data for a single instrument. For real-time updates, consider using WebSocket subscriptions to ticker channels.\\n\\n**Note:** For spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, `volume_notional` and `volume_usd` are omitted from `stats`.\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n- [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fticker)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/ticker\",\"keywords\":[\"public/ticker\",\"instrument_name\",\"timestamp\",\"state\",\"stats\",\"open_interest\",\"best_bid_price\",\"best_bid_amount\",\"best_ask_price\",\"best_ask_amount\",\"index_price\",\"min_price\",\"max_price\",\"mark_price\",\"last_price\",\"underlying_price\",\"underlying_index\",\"interest_rate\",\"bid_iv\",\"ask_iv\",\"mark_iv\",\"greeks\",\"funding_8h\",\"current_funding\",\"interest_value\",\"delivery_price\",\"settlement_price\",\"estimated_delivery_price\",\"is_anchor_breached\",\"anchor_min_price\",\"anchor_max_price\",\"volume\",\"low\",\"high\",\"price_change\",\"volume_usd\",\"delta\",\"gamma\",\"rho\",\"theta\",\"vega\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/ticker\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-ticker\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/get_index_chart_data\",\"description\":\"Returns historical price index chart data for the specified index name and time range. The data is formatted for use in charting applications and shows price index values over time.\\n\\nUse the `range` parameter to specify the time period for which to retrieve chart data. This method is useful for visualizing price index trends and historical movements.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_index_chart_data)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_index_chart_data\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_index_chart_data\",\"index_name\",\"range\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_index_chart_data\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/market-data/public-get_index_chart_data\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Session Management\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"private/disable_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"description\":\"Disable Cancel On Disconnect for the connection.\\n\\nWhen change is applied for the account, then every newly opened connection will start with **inactive** Cancel on Disconnect.\\n\\n**WebSocket Only:** This method is designed exclusively for WebSocket connections. Attempting to use it via REST/HTTP will result in an error response.\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fdisable_cancel_on_disconnect)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/disable_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"keywords\":[\"private/disable_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"scope\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/disable_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/session-management/private-disable_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/enable_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"description\":\"$64\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/enable_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"keywords\":[\"private/enable_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"scope\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/enable_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/session-management/private-enable_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"description\":\"Read current Cancel On Disconnect configuration for the account.\\n\\n**Scope:** `account:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_cancel_on_disconnect)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"scope\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/session-management/private-get_cancel_on_disconnect\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/disable_heartbeat\",\"description\":\"Stop sending heartbeat messages. This method takes no parameters.\\n\\n**WebSocket Only:** This method is designed exclusively for WebSocket connections. Attempting to use it via REST/HTTP will result in an error response.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fdisable_heartbeat)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/disable_heartbeat\",\"keywords\":[\"public/disable_heartbeat\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/disable_heartbeat\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/session-management/public-disable_heartbeat\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/set_heartbeat\",\"description\":\"Signals the WebSocket connection to send and request heartbeats. Heartbeats can be used to detect stale connections.\\n\\nWhen heartbeats have been set up, the API server will send `heartbeat` messages and `test_request` messages. Your software should respond to `test_request` messages by sending a `/api/v2/public/test` request. If your software fails to do so, the API server will immediately close the connection. If your account is configured to cancel on disconnect, any orders opened over the connection will be cancelled.\\n\\n**WebSocket Only:** This method is designed exclusively for WebSocket connections. Attempting to use it via REST/HTTP will result in an error response.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fset_heartbeat)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/set_heartbeat\",\"keywords\":[\"public/set_heartbeat\",\"interval\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/set_heartbeat\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/session-management/public-set_heartbeat\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Subscription Management\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"private/subscribe\",\"description\":\"Subscribe to one or more channels. The name of the channel determines what information will be provided, and in what form.\\n\\nFor a complete list of available subscription channels and their notification formats, see [Notifications and Subscriptions](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/notifications).\\n\\n**Note - This method has distinct API rate limiting requirements:** Sustained rate: ~3.3 requests/second. For more information, see [Rate Limits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/rate-limits).\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Market Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/market-data-collection-best-practices)\\n- [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fsubscribe)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/subscribe\",\"keywords\":[\"private/subscribe\",\"channels\",\"label\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/subscribe\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/subscription-management/private-subscribe\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/unsubscribe\",\"description\":\"Unsubscribe from one or more channels. The response contains only the channels that were successfully unsubscribed in this request.\\n\\nFor a complete list of available subscription channels and their notification formats, see [Notifications and Subscriptions](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/notifications).\\n\\n**Note:** The `result` field in the response contains only the channels that were successfully processed and unsubscribed from this specific request. It does not include all previously subscribed topics. If a channel in the request is invalid, not subscribed, or fails validation, it will not appear in the result.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Funsubscribe)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/unsubscribe\",\"keywords\":[\"private/unsubscribe\",\"channels\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/unsubscribe\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/subscription-management/private-unsubscribe\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/unsubscribe_all\",\"description\":\"Unsubscribe from all the channels subscribed so far. This method takes no parameters.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Funsubscribe_all)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/unsubscribe_all\",\"keywords\":[\"private/unsubscribe_all\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/unsubscribe_all\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/subscription-management/private-unsubscribe_all\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/subscribe\",\"description\":\"Subscribe to one or more channels. This is the same method as `/private/subscribe`, but it can only be used for 'public' channels.\\n\\nFor a complete list of available subscription channels and their notification formats, see [Notifications and Subscriptions](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/notifications).\\n\\n**Note - This method has distinct API rate limiting requirements:** Sustained rate: ~3.3 requests/second. For more information, see [Rate Limits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/rate-limits).\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Market Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/market-data-collection-best-practices)\\n- [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fsubscribe)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/subscribe\",\"keywords\":[\"public/subscribe\",\"channels\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/subscribe\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/subscription-management/public-subscribe\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/unsubscribe\",\"description\":\"Unsubscribe from one or more channels. The response contains only the channels that were successfully unsubscribed in this request.\\n\\nFor a complete list of available subscription channels and their notification formats, see [Notifications and Subscriptions](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/notifications).\\n\\n**Note:** The `result` field in the response contains only the channels that were successfully processed and unsubscribed from this specific request. It does not include all previously subscribed topics. If a channel in the request is invalid, not subscribed, or fails validation, it will not appear in the result.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Funsubscribe)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/unsubscribe\",\"keywords\":[\"public/unsubscribe\",\"channels\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/unsubscribe\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/subscription-management/public-unsubscribe\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/unsubscribe_all\",\"description\":\"Unsubscribe from all the channels subscribed so far. This method takes no parameters.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Funsubscribe_all)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/unsubscribe_all\",\"keywords\":[\"public/unsubscribe_all\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/unsubscribe_all\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/subscription-management/public-unsubscribe_all\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Supporting\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"public/get_time\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the current time (in milliseconds). This API endpoint can be used to check the clock skew between your software and Deribit's systems.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_time)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/get_time\",\"keywords\":[\"public/get_time\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/get_time\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/supporting/public-get_time\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/hello\",\"description\":\"Method used to introduce the client software connected to Deribit platform over websocket. Provided data may have an impact on the maintained connection and will be collected for internal statistical purposes. In response, Deribit will also introduce itself.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fhello)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/hello\",\"keywords\":[\"public/hello\",\"client_name\",\"client_version\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/hello\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/supporting/public-hello\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/status\",\"description\":\"Method used to get information about locked currencies\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fstatus)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/status\",\"keywords\":[\"public/status\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/status\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/supporting/public-status\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"public/test\",\"description\":\"Tests the connection to the API server, and returns its version. You can use this to make sure the API is reachable, and matches the expected version.\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Ftest)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"public/test\",\"keywords\":[\"public/test\",\"expected_result\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /public/test\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/supporting/public-test\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Trading\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"private/buy\",\"description\":\"Places a buy order for an instrument. Supports various order types including limit, market, stop, and advanced order types (stop-limit, take-profit, take-profit-limit, trailing-stop, etc.).\\n\\nYou can specify order parameters such as price, quantity, time-in-force, post-only, reduce-only, and trigger conditions. Orders can be labeled for easier management and tracking.\\n\\n**Note:** For spot orders routed to Coinbase Exchange, fills come back asynchronously. It is recommended to receive fills from the `user.trades` channel.\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Order Management Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/order-management-best-practices)\\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fbuy)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/buy\",\"keywords\":[\"private/buy\",\"instrument_name\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"type\",\"label\",\"price\",\"time_in_force\",\"display_amount\",\"post_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"trigger\",\"advanced\",\"mmp\",\"valid_until\",\"linked_order_type\",\"trigger_fill_condition\",\"otoco_config\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/buy\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-buy\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel\",\"description\":\"Cancels a specific order identified by its order ID. The order must be open (not yet filled or cancelled) to be cancelled successfully.\\n\\nOnce cancelled, the order is removed from the order book and cannot be restored. Any unfilled portion of the order will be cancelled.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel\",\"order_id\",\"order_state\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"time_in_force\",\"is_rebalance\",\"is_liquidation\",\"instrument_name\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"direction\",\"price\",\"label\",\"post_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"api\",\"web\",\"mobile\",\"refresh_amount\",\"display_amount\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"filled_amount\",\"average_price\",\"advanced\",\"implv\",\"usd\",\"triggered\",\"trigger\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"trigger_reference_price\",\"block_trade\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"replaced\",\"auto_replaced\",\"quote\",\"mmp_group\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trigger_order_id\",\"combo_order_id\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"app_name\",\"mmp_cancelled\",\"cancel_reason\",\"oto_order_ids\",\"trigger_fill_condition\",\"oco_ref\",\"primary_order_id\",\"is_secondary_oto\",\"is_primary_otoco\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-cancel\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_all\",\"description\":\"Cancels all open orders and trigger orders for the authenticated account across all currencies and instrument kinds. This is a bulk cancellation operation useful for quickly clearing all active orders.\\n\\nUse the `detailed` parameter to receive a list of all cancelled orders. The `freeze_quotes` parameter can be used to freeze quotes instead of cancelling them.\\n\\nSet `include_starbase_orders` to `true` to also cancel the subaccount's Starbase direct-access open orders; the number cancelled is included in the returned cancelled-order count. This flag cannot be combined with `detailed`, and `freeze_quotes` is not enforced for Starbase orders.\\n\\n**Note:** This operation cannot be undone. All open orders will be permanently cancelled.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_all)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_all\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_all\",\"detailed\",\"freeze_quotes\",\"include_starbase_orders\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_all\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-cancel_all\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_all_by_currency\",\"description\":\"Cancels all open orders for a specific currency. This is useful for quickly clearing all orders across multiple instruments in a currency.\\n\\nOrders can be optionally filtered by instrument kind (future, option, etc.) and/or order type (limit, market, stop, etc.). Use the `detailed` parameter to receive a list of all cancelled orders.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_all_by_currency)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_all_by_currency\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_all_by_currency\",\"currency\",\"kind\",\"type\",\"detailed\",\"freeze_quotes\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_all_by_currency\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-cancel_all_by_currency\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_all_by_currency_pair\",\"description\":\"Cancels all open orders for a specific currency pair. This is useful for quickly clearing all orders across instruments in a currency pair.\\n\\nOrders can be optionally filtered by instrument kind (future, option, etc.) and/or order type (limit, market, stop, etc.). Use the `detailed` parameter to receive a list of all cancelled orders.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_all_by_currency_pair)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_all_by_currency_pair\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_all_by_currency_pair\",\"currency_pair\",\"kind\",\"type\",\"detailed\",\"freeze_quotes\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_all_by_currency_pair\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-cancel_all_by_currency_pair\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_all_by_instrument\",\"description\":\"Cancels all open orders for a specific instrument. This is useful for quickly clearing all orders for a single instrument.\\n\\nOrders can be optionally filtered by order type (limit, market, stop, etc.). Use the `detailed` parameter to receive a list of all cancelled orders. The `include_combos` parameter can be used to include combo orders in the cancellation.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_all_by_instrument)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_all_by_instrument\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_all_by_instrument\",\"instrument_name\",\"type\",\"detailed\",\"include_combos\",\"freeze_quotes\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_all_by_instrument\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-cancel_all_by_instrument\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_all_by_kind_or_type\",\"description\":\"Cancels all open orders in one or more currencies, optionally filtered by instrument kind and/or order type. This provides flexible bulk cancellation across multiple currencies.\\n\\nSpecify one or more currencies, and optionally filter by instrument kind (future, option, etc.) and/or order type (limit, market, stop, etc.). Use the `detailed` parameter to receive a list of all cancelled orders.\\n\\n`include_starbase_orders` only applies to a full cancel-all (order type `all`); it is ignored when cancelling a specific order type such as `quote`.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_all_by_kind_or_type)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_all_by_kind_or_type\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_all_by_kind_or_type\",\"currency\",\"kind\",\"type\",\"detailed\",\"freeze_quotes\",\"include_starbase_orders\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_all_by_kind_or_type\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-cancel_all_by_kind_or_type\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_by_label\",\"description\":\"Cancels all orders (including trigger orders) that have a specific label. This is useful for managing groups of related orders that share the same label.\\n\\nOrders can be cancelled across all currencies or filtered to a specific currency. When cancelling by currency, the currency queue is used for processing.\\n\\n**Rate Limits:** When called without the `currency` parameter, this method is subject to `cancel_all` rate limits. Different rate limit values may apply for per-currency cancels versus calls without providing the currency parameter.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_by_label)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_by_label\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_by_label\",\"label\",\"currency\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_by_label\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-cancel_by_label\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_quotes\",\"description\":\"Cancels quotes (mass quote orders) based on various criteria. This method provides flexible options for cancelling quotes:\\n\\n- `delta`: Cancels quotes within a delta range defined by `min_delta` and `max_delta`\\n- `quote_set_id`: Cancels quotes by a specific Quote Set identifier\\n- `instrument`: Cancels all quotes associated with a particular instrument\\n- `kind`: Cancels all quotes for a certain instrument kind\\n- `currency`: Cancels all quotes in a specified currency\\n- `currency_pair`: Cancels all quotes in a specified currency pair\\n- `all`: Cancels all quotes\\n\\nUse the `detailed` parameter to receive a list of all cancelled quotes.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_quotes)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_quotes\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_quotes\",\"detailed\",\"freeze_quotes\",\"cancel_type\",\"min_delta\",\"max_delta\",\"quote_set_id\",\"instrument_name\",\"kind\",\"currency\",\"currency_pair\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_quotes\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-cancel_quotes\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/close_position\",\"description\":\"Places a reduce-only order to close an existing position. Reduce-only orders can only reduce or close a position; they cannot open a new position or increase an existing one.\\n\\nYou can specify whether to use a market or limit order. If using a limit order, provide the price. The order will automatically be set to reduce-only to ensure it only closes the position.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fclose_position)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/close_position\",\"keywords\":[\"private/close_position\",\"instrument_name\",\"type\",\"price\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/close_position\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-close_position\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/edit\",\"description\":\"Modifies an existing order by changing its price, amount, and/or other properties such as time-in-force, post-only, reduce-only, trigger conditions, or advanced order type.\\n\\nThe order is identified by its order ID. Only open orders can be edited. Changes take effect immediately and may result in the order being filled if the new price matches the market.\\n\\n**Note:** For spot orders routed to Coinbase Exchange, fills come back asynchronously. It is recommended to receive fills from the `user.trades` channel.\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Order Management Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/order-management-best-practices)\\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fedit)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/edit\",\"keywords\":[\"private/edit\",\"order_id\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"price\",\"post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"advanced\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"mmp\",\"valid_until\",\"display_amount\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/edit\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-edit\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/edit_by_label\",\"description\":\"Modifies an order identified by its label. This method works only when there is exactly one open order with the specified label.\\n\\nYou can change the order's price, amount, and/or other properties such as time-in-force, post-only, reduce-only, trigger conditions, or advanced order type. Changes take effect immediately.\\n\\n**Note:** For spot orders routed to Coinbase Exchange, fills come back asynchronously. It is recommended to receive fills from the `user.trades` channel.\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Order Management Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/order-management-best-practices)\\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fedit_by_label)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/edit_by_label\",\"keywords\":[\"private/edit_by_label\",\"label\",\"instrument_name\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"price\",\"post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"advanced\",\"trigger_price\",\"mmp\",\"valid_until\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/edit_by_label\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-edit_by_label\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_margins\",\"description\":\"Calculates margin requirements for a hypothetical order on a given instrument. Returns initial margin and maintenance margin for the specified instrument, quantity, and price.\\n\\nThis method is useful for estimating margin requirements before placing an order, helping to ensure sufficient funds are available and understanding the margin impact of potential trades.\\n\\nFor spot instruments, `amount_type` selects whether `amount` is a base currency quantity (fees charged on top) or a total quote currency spend (fees included).\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_margins)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_margins\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_margins\",\"instrument_name\",\"amount\",\"amount_type\",\"price\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_margins\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_margins\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_mmp_config\",\"description\":\"$65\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_mmp_config\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_mmp_config\",\"index_name\",\"mmp_group\",\"block_rfq\",\"interval\",\"frozen_time\",\"quantity_limit\",\"delta_limit\",\"vega_limit\",\"max_quote_quantity\",\"trade_count_limit\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_mmp_config\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_mmp_config\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_mmp_status\",\"description\":\"Retrieves Market Maker Protection (MMP) status for a triggered index or MMP group. Returns the live MMP state including whether MMP is enabled or triggered, remaining frozen time (if triggered), whether quoting is currently allowed, and any active freeze conditions.\\n\\nIf the `index_name` parameter is not provided, a list of all triggered MMP statuses is returned. This method lets you track whether protection is active and when quoting will resume.\\n\\nFor Mass Quotes, specify the `mmp_group` parameter to check status for a specific MMP group. Set `block_rfq` to `true` to retrieve MMP status for Block RFQ (requires `block_rfq:read` scope).\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Market Maker Protection API Configuration](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/market-maker-protection)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read` or `block_rfq:read` (when `block_rfq` = `true`)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_mmp_status)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_mmp_status\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_mmp_status\",\"index_name\",\"mmp_group\",\"block_rfq\",\"frozen_until\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_mmp_status\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_mmp_status\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_open_orders\",\"description\":\"Retrieves a list of all open orders for the authenticated account across all currencies. Open orders are orders that have been placed but not yet filled or cancelled.\\n\\nResults can be filtered by instrument kind and order type. This method provides a comprehensive view of all active orders.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_open_orders)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_open_orders\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_open_orders\",\"kind\",\"type\",\"order_id\",\"order_state\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"time_in_force\",\"is_rebalance\",\"is_liquidation\",\"instrument_name\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"direction\",\"price\",\"label\",\"post_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"api\",\"web\",\"mobile\",\"refresh_amount\",\"display_amount\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"filled_amount\",\"average_price\",\"advanced\",\"implv\",\"usd\",\"triggered\",\"trigger\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"trigger_reference_price\",\"block_trade\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"replaced\",\"auto_replaced\",\"quote\",\"mmp_group\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trigger_order_id\",\"combo_order_id\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"app_name\",\"mmp_cancelled\",\"cancel_reason\",\"oto_order_ids\",\"trigger_fill_condition\",\"oco_ref\",\"primary_order_id\",\"is_secondary_oto\",\"is_primary_otoco\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_open_orders\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_open_orders\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_open_orders_by_currency\",\"description\":\"Retrieves a list of all open orders for a specific currency. Open orders are orders that have been placed but not yet filled or cancelled.\\n\\nResults can be filtered by instrument kind and order type. This method provides a view of all active orders within a currency.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_open_orders_by_currency)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_open_orders_by_currency\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_open_orders_by_currency\",\"currency\",\"kind\",\"type\",\"order_id\",\"order_state\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"time_in_force\",\"is_rebalance\",\"is_liquidation\",\"instrument_name\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"direction\",\"price\",\"label\",\"post_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"api\",\"web\",\"mobile\",\"refresh_amount\",\"display_amount\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"filled_amount\",\"average_price\",\"advanced\",\"implv\",\"usd\",\"triggered\",\"trigger\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"trigger_reference_price\",\"block_trade\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"replaced\",\"auto_replaced\",\"quote\",\"mmp_group\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trigger_order_id\",\"combo_order_id\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"app_name\",\"mmp_cancelled\",\"cancel_reason\",\"oto_order_ids\",\"trigger_fill_condition\",\"oco_ref\",\"primary_order_id\",\"is_secondary_oto\",\"is_primary_otoco\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_open_orders_by_currency\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_open_orders_by_currency\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_open_orders_by_instrument\",\"description\":\"Retrieves a list of all open orders for a specific instrument. Open orders are orders that have been placed but not yet filled or cancelled.\\n\\nResults can be filtered by order type. This method is useful for checking active orders for a particular instrument.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_open_orders_by_instrument)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_open_orders_by_instrument\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_open_orders_by_instrument\",\"instrument_name\",\"type\",\"order_id\",\"order_state\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"time_in_force\",\"is_rebalance\",\"is_liquidation\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"direction\",\"price\",\"label\",\"post_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"api\",\"web\",\"mobile\",\"refresh_amount\",\"display_amount\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"filled_amount\",\"average_price\",\"advanced\",\"implv\",\"usd\",\"triggered\",\"trigger\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"trigger_reference_price\",\"block_trade\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"replaced\",\"auto_replaced\",\"quote\",\"mmp_group\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trigger_order_id\",\"combo_order_id\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"app_name\",\"mmp_cancelled\",\"cancel_reason\",\"oto_order_ids\",\"trigger_fill_condition\",\"oco_ref\",\"primary_order_id\",\"is_secondary_oto\",\"is_primary_otoco\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_open_orders_by_instrument\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_open_orders_by_instrument\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_open_orders_by_label\",\"description\":\"Retrieves a list of all open orders that have a specific label within a given currency. This is useful for tracking and managing groups of related orders that share the same label.\\n\\nOpen orders are orders that have been placed but not yet filled or cancelled. The label helps organize and identify related orders.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_open_orders_by_label)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_open_orders_by_label\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_open_orders_by_label\",\"currency\",\"label\",\"order_id\",\"order_state\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"time_in_force\",\"is_rebalance\",\"is_liquidation\",\"instrument_name\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"direction\",\"price\",\"post_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"api\",\"web\",\"mobile\",\"refresh_amount\",\"display_amount\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"filled_amount\",\"average_price\",\"advanced\",\"implv\",\"usd\",\"triggered\",\"trigger\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"trigger_reference_price\",\"block_trade\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"replaced\",\"auto_replaced\",\"quote\",\"mmp_group\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trigger_order_id\",\"combo_order_id\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"app_name\",\"mmp_cancelled\",\"cancel_reason\",\"oto_order_ids\",\"trigger_fill_condition\",\"oco_ref\",\"primary_order_id\",\"is_secondary_oto\",\"is_primary_otoco\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_open_orders_by_label\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_open_orders_by_label\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_order_history_by_currency\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the order history for a specific currency. The history includes orders that have been partially or fully filled, as well as cancelled orders (if `include_unfilled_orders` is set to true).\\n\\nResults can be filtered by instrument kind and paginated using `offset` and `count` parameters, or using continuation tokens. Use `include_old_orders` to include orders from before a certain date, and `historical` to retrieve historical order data.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Accessing Historical Trades and Orders Using API](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/accessing-historical-trades-orders)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_order_history_by_currency)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_order_history_by_currency\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_order_history_by_currency\",\"currency\",\"kind\",\"count\",\"offset\",\"include_old\",\"include_unfilled\",\"with_continuation\",\"continuation\",\"historical\",\"order_id\",\"order_state\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"time_in_force\",\"is_rebalance\",\"is_liquidation\",\"instrument_name\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"direction\",\"price\",\"label\",\"post_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"api\",\"web\",\"mobile\",\"refresh_amount\",\"display_amount\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"filled_amount\",\"average_price\",\"advanced\",\"implv\",\"usd\",\"triggered\",\"trigger\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"trigger_reference_price\",\"block_trade\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"replaced\",\"auto_replaced\",\"quote\",\"mmp_group\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trigger_order_id\",\"combo_order_id\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"app_name\",\"mmp_cancelled\",\"cancel_reason\",\"oto_order_ids\",\"trigger_fill_condition\",\"oco_ref\",\"primary_order_id\",\"is_secondary_oto\",\"is_primary_otoco\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_order_history_by_currency\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_order_history_by_currency\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_order_history_by_instrument\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the order history for a specific instrument. The history includes orders that have been partially or fully filled, as well as cancelled orders (if `include_unfilled_orders` is set to true).\\n\\nResults can be paginated using `offset` and `count` parameters, or using continuation tokens. Use `include_old_orders` to include orders from before a certain date, and `historical` to retrieve historical order data.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Accessing Historical Trades and Orders Using API](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/accessing-historical-trades-orders)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_order_history_by_instrument)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_order_history_by_instrument\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_order_history_by_instrument\",\"instrument_name\",\"count\",\"offset\",\"include_old\",\"include_unfilled\",\"with_continuation\",\"continuation\",\"historical\",\"order_id\",\"order_state\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"time_in_force\",\"is_rebalance\",\"is_liquidation\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"direction\",\"price\",\"label\",\"post_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"api\",\"web\",\"mobile\",\"refresh_amount\",\"display_amount\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"filled_amount\",\"average_price\",\"advanced\",\"implv\",\"usd\",\"triggered\",\"trigger\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"trigger_reference_price\",\"block_trade\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"replaced\",\"auto_replaced\",\"quote\",\"mmp_group\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trigger_order_id\",\"combo_order_id\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"app_name\",\"mmp_cancelled\",\"cancel_reason\",\"oto_order_ids\",\"trigger_fill_condition\",\"oco_ref\",\"primary_order_id\",\"is_secondary_oto\",\"is_primary_otoco\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_order_history_by_instrument\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_order_history_by_instrument\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_order_margin_by_ids\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the initial margin requirements for one or more orders identified by their order IDs. Initial margin is the amount of funds required to open a position with these orders.\\n\\nThis method is useful for calculating margin requirements before placing orders, helping to ensure sufficient funds are available.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_order_margin_by_ids)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_order_margin_by_ids\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_order_margin_by_ids\",\"ids\",\"order_id\",\"initial_margin\",\"initial_margin_currency\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_order_margin_by_ids\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_order_margin_by_ids\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_order_state\",\"description\":\"$66\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_order_state\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_order_state\",\"order_id\",\"order_state\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"time_in_force\",\"is_rebalance\",\"is_liquidation\",\"instrument_name\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"direction\",\"price\",\"label\",\"post_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"api\",\"web\",\"mobile\",\"refresh_amount\",\"display_amount\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"filled_amount\",\"average_price\",\"advanced\",\"implv\",\"usd\",\"triggered\",\"trigger\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"trigger_reference_price\",\"block_trade\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"replaced\",\"auto_replaced\",\"quote\",\"mmp_group\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trigger_order_id\",\"combo_order_id\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"app_name\",\"mmp_cancelled\",\"cancel_reason\",\"oto_order_ids\",\"trigger_fill_condition\",\"oco_ref\",\"primary_order_id\",\"is_secondary_oto\",\"is_primary_otoco\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_order_state\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_order_state\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_order_state_by_label\",\"description\":\"$67\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_order_state_by_label\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_order_state_by_label\",\"currency\",\"label\",\"order_id\",\"order_state\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"time_in_force\",\"is_rebalance\",\"is_liquidation\",\"instrument_name\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_last_update_timestamp\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"direction\",\"price\",\"post_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"api\",\"web\",\"mobile\",\"refresh_amount\",\"display_amount\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"filled_amount\",\"average_price\",\"advanced\",\"implv\",\"usd\",\"triggered\",\"trigger\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"trigger_reference_price\",\"block_trade\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"replaced\",\"auto_replaced\",\"quote\",\"mmp_group\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trigger_order_id\",\"combo_order_id\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"app_name\",\"mmp_cancelled\",\"cancel_reason\",\"oto_order_ids\",\"trigger_fill_condition\",\"oco_ref\",\"primary_order_id\",\"is_secondary_oto\",\"is_primary_otoco\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_order_state_by_label\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_order_state_by_label\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_settlement_history_by_currency\",\"description\":\"$68\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_settlement_history_by_currency\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_settlement_history_by_currency\",\"currency\",\"type\",\"count\",\"continuation\",\"search_start_timestamp\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_settlement_history_by_currency\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_settlement_history_by_currency\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_settlement_history_by_instrument\",\"description\":\"Retrieves settlement, delivery, and bankruptcy events for a specific instrument that have affected your account.\\n\\n**Settlement vs. delivery:** Settlement is a daily event (at 08:00 UTC) for futures and perpetual positions that converts unrealized profit and loss into realized profit and loss. Option positions do not settle. Delivery is a one-time event that occurs when a futures or options contract expires — any remaining open position is closed at the delivery price. Delivery does not apply to perpetual or spot instruments. Both events take place at 08:00 UTC, which is why they are sometimes conflated.\\n\\nResults can be filtered by settlement type and timestamp. Use pagination parameters (`count` and `continuation`) to retrieve large settlement histories. This method is useful for tracking settlement events for a specific instrument.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_settlement_history_by_instrument)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_settlement_history_by_instrument\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_settlement_history_by_instrument\",\"instrument_name\",\"type\",\"count\",\"continuation\",\"search_start_timestamp\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_settlement_history_by_instrument\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_settlement_history_by_instrument\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_trigger_order_history\",\"description\":\"Retrieves a detailed log of all trigger orders (stop orders, take-profit orders, etc.) for the authenticated account. The log includes trigger order creation, activation, execution, and cancellation events.\\n\\nResults can be filtered by currency and instrument name. Use pagination parameters (`count` and `continuation`) to retrieve large trigger order histories. This is useful for tracking trigger order activity and debugging trigger order behavior.\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_trigger_order_history)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_trigger_order_history\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_trigger_order_history\",\"currency\",\"instrument_name\",\"count\",\"continuation\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_trigger_order_history\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_trigger_order_history\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_user_trades_by_currency\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the latest user trades that have occurred for instruments in a specific currency. Returns trade details including price, amount, direction, timestamp, trade ID, and order ID for all instruments in the currency.\\n\\nResults can be filtered by instrument kind, trade ID range, or timestamp range. Use the `count` parameter to limit the number of trades returned, and `sorting` to control the order. To retrieve trades for a specific subaccount, use the `subaccount_id` parameter. Use `historical` to retrieve historical trade data.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Accessing Historical Trades and Orders Using API](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/accessing-historical-trades-orders)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_user_trades_by_currency)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_user_trades_by_currency\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_user_trades_by_currency\",\"currency\",\"kind\",\"start_id\",\"end_id\",\"count\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\",\"sorting\",\"historical\",\"subaccount_id\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_user_trades_by_currency\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_user_trades_by_currency\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_user_trades_by_currency_and_time\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the latest user trades that have occurred for instruments in a specific currency within a specified time range. Returns trade details including price, amount, direction, timestamp, trade ID, and order ID for all instruments in the currency.\\n\\nResults can be filtered by instrument kind. Use the `count` parameter to limit the number of trades returned, and `sorting` to control the order. Use `historical` to retrieve historical trade data. This method is useful for analyzing trading activity across a currency over specific time periods.\\n\\nMain accounts may use the `subaccount_id` parameter to retrieve trade data for a specific subaccount (requires `mainaccount` scope).\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Accessing Historical Trades and Orders Using API](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/accessing-historical-trades-orders)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_user_trades_by_currency_and_time)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_user_trades_by_currency_and_time\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_user_trades_by_currency_and_time\",\"currency\",\"kind\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\",\"count\",\"sorting\",\"historical\",\"subaccount_id\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_user_trades_by_currency_and_time\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_user_trades_by_currency_and_time\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_user_trades_by_instrument\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the latest user trades that have occurred for a specific instrument. Returns trade details including price, amount, direction, timestamp, trade ID, and order ID.\\n\\nResults can be filtered by sequence number range or timestamp range. Use the `count` parameter to limit the number of trades returned, and `sorting` to control the order (ascending or descending by trade ID). Use `historical` to retrieve historical trade data.\\n\\nMain accounts may use the `subaccount_id` parameter to retrieve trade data for a specific subaccount (requires `mainaccount` scope).\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Accessing Historical Trades and Orders Using API](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/accessing-historical-trades-orders)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_user_trades_by_instrument)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_user_trades_by_instrument\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_user_trades_by_instrument\",\"instrument_name\",\"start_seq\",\"end_seq\",\"count\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\",\"historical\",\"sorting\",\"subaccount_id\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_user_trades_by_instrument\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_user_trades_by_instrument\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_user_trades_by_instrument_and_time\",\"description\":\"Retrieves the latest user trades that have occurred for a specific instrument within a specified time range. Returns trade details including price, amount, direction, timestamp, trade ID, and order ID.\\n\\nUse the `count` parameter to limit the number of trades returned, and `sorting` to control the order (ascending or descending by trade ID). Use `historical` to retrieve historical trade data. This method is useful for analyzing trading activity over specific time periods.\\n\\nMain accounts may use the `subaccount_id` parameter to retrieve trade data for a specific subaccount (requires `mainaccount` scope).\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Accessing Historical Trades and Orders Using API](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/accessing-historical-trades-orders)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_user_trades_by_instrument_and_time)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_user_trades_by_instrument_and_time\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_user_trades_by_instrument_and_time\",\"instrument_name\",\"start_timestamp\",\"end_timestamp\",\"count\",\"sorting\",\"historical\",\"subaccount_id\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_user_trades_by_instrument_and_time\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_user_trades_by_instrument_and_time\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_user_trades_by_order\",\"description\":\"Retrieves all trades that were executed from a specific order. When an order is filled, it may result in multiple trades (partial fills). This method returns all trades associated with a given order ID.\\n\\nResults can be sorted in ascending or descending order by trade ID. Use `historical` to retrieve historical trade data. This is useful for tracking how an order was filled and analyzing execution quality.\\n\\nMain accounts may use the `subaccount_id` parameter to retrieve trade data for a specific subaccount (requires `mainaccount` scope).\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Accessing Historical Trades and Orders Using API](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/accessing-historical-trades-orders)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_user_trades_by_order)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_user_trades_by_order\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_user_trades_by_order\",\"order_id\",\"sorting\",\"historical\",\"subaccount_id\",\"trade_id\",\"trade_seq\",\"instrument_name\",\"timestamp\",\"starbase_timestamp\",\"starbase_order_id\",\"starbase_client_order_id\",\"order_type\",\"original_order_type\",\"advanced\",\"matching_id\",\"direction\",\"tick_direction\",\"index_price\",\"price\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"iv\",\"underlying_price\",\"liquidation\",\"liquidity\",\"fee\",\"fee_currency\",\"label\",\"state\",\"block_trade_id\",\"block_trade_leg_count\",\"block_rfq_id\",\"block_rfq_quote_id\",\"reduce_only\",\"post_only\",\"mmp\",\"risk_reducing\",\"api\",\"profit_loss\",\"mark_price\",\"legs\",\"combo_id\",\"combo_trade_id\",\"starbase_match_id\",\"quote_set_id\",\"quote_id\",\"trade_allocations\",\"user_id\",\"client_info\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_user_trades_by_order\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-get_user_trades_by_order\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/mass_quote\",\"description\":\"$69\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/mass_quote\",\"keywords\":[\"private/mass_quote\",\"wait_for_response\",\"detailed\",\"quote_id\",\"mmp_group\",\"valid_until\",\"quotes\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/mass_quote\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-mass_quote\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/move_positions\",\"description\":\"$6a\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/move_positions\",\"keywords\":[\"private/move_positions\",\"currency\",\"source_uid\",\"target_uid\",\"trades\",\"instrument_name\",\"direction\",\"price\",\"amount\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/move_positions\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-move_positions\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/reset_mmp\",\"description\":\"$6b\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/reset_mmp\",\"keywords\":[\"private/reset_mmp\",\"index_name\",\"mmp_group\",\"block_rfq\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/reset_mmp\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-reset_mmp\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/sell\",\"description\":\"Places a sell order for an instrument. Supports various order types including limit, market, stop, and advanced order types (stop-limit, take-profit, take-profit-limit, trailing-stop, etc.).\\n\\nYou can specify order parameters such as price, quantity, time-in-force, post-only, reduce-only, and trigger conditions. Orders can be labeled for easier management and tracking. Market Maker Protection (MMP) can be enabled to prevent excessive quoting.\\n\\n**Note:** For spot orders routed to Coinbase Exchange, fills come back asynchronously. It is recommended to receive fills from the `user.trades` channel.\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Order Management Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/order-management-best-practices)\\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n\\n**Scope:** `trade:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fsell)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/sell\",\"keywords\":[\"private/sell\",\"instrument_name\",\"amount\",\"contracts\",\"type\",\"label\",\"price\",\"time_in_force\",\"display_amount\",\"post_only\",\"reject_post_only\",\"reduce_only\",\"trigger_price\",\"trigger_offset\",\"trigger\",\"advanced\",\"mmp\",\"valid_until\",\"linked_order_type\",\"trigger_fill_condition\",\"otoco_config\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/sell\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-sell\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/set_mmp_config\",\"description\":\"$6c\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/set_mmp_config\",\"keywords\":[\"private/set_mmp_config\",\"index_name\",\"interval\",\"frozen_time\",\"mmp_group\",\"quantity_limit\",\"delta_limit\",\"vega_limit\",\"max_quote_quantity\",\"block_rfq\",\"trade_count_limit\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/set_mmp_config\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/trading/private-set_mmp_config\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Wallet\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"private/add_to_address_book\",\"description\":\"$6d\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/add_to_address_book\",\"keywords\":[\"private/add_to_address_book\",\"currency\",\"type\",\"address\",\"network\",\"tag\",\"counterparty_id\",\"label\",\"beneficiary_vasp_name\",\"beneficiary_vasp_did\",\"beneficiary_vasp_website\",\"beneficiary_first_name\",\"beneficiary_last_name\",\"beneficiary_company_name\",\"beneficiary_address\",\"agreed\",\"personal\",\"extra_currencies\",\"name\",\"country\",\"financial_institution\",\"account\",\"account_location\",\"entity_type\",\"wallet_type\",\"is_self\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"info_required\",\"status\",\"waiting_timestamp\",\"requires_confirmation\",\"requires_confirmation_change\",\"requires_security_key\",\"kind\",\"updated_timestamp\",\"network_display_name\",\"beneficiary_created\",\"beneficiary_updated\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/add_to_address_book\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-add_to_address_book\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_transfer_by_id\",\"description\":\"Cancel a pending transfer by its ID. This method allows you to cancel a transfer that has not yet been processed. Once a transfer is processed, it cannot be cancelled.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Transfers](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-transfers-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_transfer_by_id)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_transfer_by_id\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_transfer_by_id\",\"currency\",\"id\",\"created_timestamp\",\"type\",\"amount\",\"other_side\",\"state\",\"direction\",\"updated_timestamp\",\"nonce\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_transfer_by_id\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-cancel_transfer_by_id\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/cancel_withdrawal\",\"description\":\"Cancels a pending withdrawal request. This method allows you to cancel a withdrawal that has not yet been processed. Once a withdrawal is processed, it cannot be cancelled.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcancel_withdrawal)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/cancel_withdrawal\",\"keywords\":[\"private/cancel_withdrawal\",\"currency\",\"id\",\"address\",\"amount\",\"confirmed_timestamp\",\"created_timestamp\",\"fee\",\"priority\",\"state\",\"transaction_id\",\"updated_timestamp\",\"nonce\",\"transfer_idem\",\"network\",\"network_display_name\",\"destination_tag\",\"payment_id\",\"source_ctn_id\",\"destination_ctn_id\",\"clearance_state\",\"note\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/cancel_withdrawal\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-cancel_withdrawal\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/coinbase/estimate_withdrawal_fee\",\"description\":\"Estimates the network fee for a withdrawal on the given currency and network. **Available to institutional Coinbase wallet type accounts only.**\\n\\nThe `network_name` parameter is not validated against `coinbase_networks`; it is passed through to the custodian. The networks available for each currency are returned by `public/get_currencies` in the `coinbase_networks` field.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fcoinbase%2Festimate_withdrawal_fee)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/coinbase/estimate_withdrawal_fee\",\"keywords\":[\"private/coinbase/estimate_withdrawal_fee\",\"currency\",\"network_name\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/coinbase/estimate_withdrawal_fee\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-estimate_withdrawal_fee\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/create_deposit_address\",\"description\":\"$6e\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/create_deposit_address\",\"keywords\":[\"private/create_deposit_address\",\"currency\",\"network\",\"label\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"address\",\"type\",\"kind\",\"updated_timestamp\",\"status\",\"waiting_timestamp\",\"requires_confirmation\",\"requires_confirmation_change\",\"requires_security_key\",\"info_required\",\"network_display_name\",\"tag\",\"name\",\"country\",\"financial_institution\",\"account\",\"account_location\",\"entity_type\",\"wallet_type\",\"is_self\",\"beneficiary_created\",\"beneficiary_updated\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/create_deposit_address\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-create_deposit_address\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/delete_address_beneficiary\",\"description\":\"Deletes beneficiary information for a specific address.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fdelete_address_beneficiary)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/delete_address_beneficiary\",\"keywords\":[\"private/delete_address_beneficiary\",\"currency\",\"address\",\"tag\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/delete_address_beneficiary\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-delete_address_beneficiary\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_address_beneficiary\",\"description\":\"Retrieves beneficiary information for a specific address. Returns the stored beneficiary details including VASP information, personal details, and wallet type classification.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_address_beneficiary)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_address_beneficiary\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_address_beneficiary\",\"currency\",\"address\",\"tag\",\"user_id\",\"agreed\",\"personal\",\"unhosted\",\"beneficiary_vasp_name\",\"beneficiary_vasp_did\",\"beneficiary_vasp_website\",\"beneficiary_first_name\",\"beneficiary_last_name\",\"beneficiary_company_name\",\"beneficiary_address\",\"created\",\"updated\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_address_beneficiary\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-get_address_beneficiary\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_address_book\",\"description\":\"$6f\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_address_book\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_address_book\",\"currency\",\"type\",\"address\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"label\",\"beneficiary_vasp_name\",\"beneficiary_vasp_did\",\"beneficiary_vasp_website\",\"beneficiary_first_name\",\"beneficiary_last_name\",\"beneficiary_company_name\",\"beneficiary_address\",\"agreed\",\"personal\",\"info_required\",\"status\",\"waiting_timestamp\",\"requires_confirmation\",\"requires_confirmation_change\",\"requires_security_key\",\"kind\",\"updated_timestamp\",\"network\",\"network_display_name\",\"tag\",\"name\",\"country\",\"financial_institution\",\"account\",\"account_location\",\"entity_type\",\"wallet_type\",\"is_self\",\"beneficiary_created\",\"beneficiary_updated\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_address_book\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-get_address_book\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_current_deposit_address\",\"description\":\"Retrieve the current deposit address for the specified currency. Returns the most recently created or used deposit address for receiving funds.\\n\\n**Coinbase wallet type**\\n\\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts the `network` parameter is required and selects the blockchain network of the deposit address. The networks available for each currency are returned by `public/get_currencies` in the `coinbase_networks` field. Returns `null` when no deposit address exists for the given currency and network. This method is available to institutional Coinbase accounts only.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Deposits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-deposits-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_current_deposit_address)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_current_deposit_address\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_current_deposit_address\",\"currency\",\"network\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"address\",\"type\",\"kind\",\"label\",\"updated_timestamp\",\"status\",\"waiting_timestamp\",\"requires_confirmation\",\"requires_confirmation_change\",\"requires_security_key\",\"info_required\",\"network_display_name\",\"tag\",\"name\",\"country\",\"financial_institution\",\"account\",\"account_location\",\"entity_type\",\"wallet_type\",\"is_self\",\"beneficiary_created\",\"beneficiary_updated\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_current_deposit_address\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-get_current_deposit_address\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_deposits\",\"description\":\"Retrieve the latest user deposits. Returns a list of deposit transactions with their status, amounts, addresses, confirmations, and other relevant details.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Deposits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-deposits-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_deposits)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_deposits\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_deposits\",\"currency\",\"count\",\"offset\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_deposits\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-get_deposits\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_reward_eligibility\",\"description\":\"Returns reward eligibility status and APR data for all supported currencies.\\n\\nThis method takes no parameters.\\n\\n**📖 Related Support Article:** [Yield reward-bearing coins](https://support.deribit.com/hc/en-us/articles/31424939199261-Yield-reward-bearing-coins)\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_reward_eligibility)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_reward_eligibility\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_reward_eligibility\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_reward_eligibility\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-get_reward_eligibility\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_transfers\",\"description\":\"Retrieve the user's transfers list. Returns a list of internal transfers between accounts, subaccounts, or to other users, including their status, amounts, and other relevant details.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Transfers](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-transfers-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_transfers)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_transfers\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_transfers\",\"currency\",\"count\",\"offset\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_transfers\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-get_transfers\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/get_withdrawals\",\"description\":\"Retrieve the latest user withdrawals. Returns a list of withdrawal requests with their status, amounts, addresses, and other relevant details.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fget_withdrawals)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/get_withdrawals\",\"keywords\":[\"private/get_withdrawals\",\"currency\",\"count\",\"offset\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/get_withdrawals\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-get_withdrawals\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/list_address_beneficiaries\",\"description\":\"Lists address beneficiaries with optional filtering and pagination. Returns all saved beneficiary information for addresses, with support for filtering by currency, address, wallet type, VASP details, and date ranges.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Flist_address_beneficiaries)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/list_address_beneficiaries\",\"keywords\":[\"private/list_address_beneficiaries\",\"currency\",\"address\",\"tag\",\"created_before\",\"created_after\",\"updated_before\",\"updated_after\",\"personal\",\"unhosted\",\"beneficiary_vasp_name\",\"beneficiary_vasp_did\",\"beneficiary_vasp_website\",\"limit\",\"continuation\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/list_address_beneficiaries\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-list_address_beneficiaries\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/remove_from_address_book\",\"description\":\"Removes an entry from the address book. This method allows you to delete a saved address that is no longer needed.\\n\\n**Coinbase wallet type**\\n\\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts the required parameters are `currency` (portfolio currencies or `\\\"all\\\"`) and `type`, plus one of `address` or `id` (the entry identifier returned by `private/get_address_book`). Use `network` and `tag` together with `address` to disambiguate entries sharing the same address.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fremove_from_address_book)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/remove_from_address_book\",\"keywords\":[\"private/remove_from_address_book\",\"currency\",\"type\",\"address\",\"network\",\"tag\",\"id\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/remove_from_address_book\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-remove_from_address_book\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/save_address_beneficiary\",\"description\":\"Saves beneficiary information for an address. This method allows you to store beneficiary details required for compliance purposes, including VASP information, personal details, and wallet type classification.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fsave_address_beneficiary)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/save_address_beneficiary\",\"keywords\":[\"private/save_address_beneficiary\",\"currency\",\"address\",\"tag\",\"agreed\",\"personal\",\"unhosted\",\"beneficiary_vasp_name\",\"beneficiary_vasp_did\",\"beneficiary_vasp_website\",\"beneficiary_first_name\",\"beneficiary_last_name\",\"beneficiary_company_name\",\"beneficiary_address\",\"user_id\",\"created\",\"updated\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/save_address_beneficiary\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-save_address_beneficiary\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/set_address_requires_security_key\",\"description\":\"Sets whether withdrawals to the given address book address require a security key. Returns the updated address book entry.\\n\\n**Coinbase wallet type**\\n\\nFor Coinbase wallet type accounts the entry is identified by one of `address` or `id` (the entry identifier returned by `private/get_address_book`) instead of `address` alone. Use `network` and `tag` together with `address` to disambiguate entries sharing the same address. The `mainaccount` scope is not required for Coinbase wallet type accounts.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write` and mainaccount\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fset_address_requires_security_key)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/set_address_requires_security_key\",\"keywords\":[\"private/set_address_requires_security_key\",\"currency\",\"type\",\"address\",\"network\",\"tag\",\"id\",\"value\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"label\",\"beneficiary_vasp_name\",\"beneficiary_vasp_did\",\"beneficiary_vasp_website\",\"beneficiary_first_name\",\"beneficiary_last_name\",\"beneficiary_company_name\",\"beneficiary_address\",\"agreed\",\"personal\",\"info_required\",\"status\",\"waiting_timestamp\",\"requires_confirmation\",\"requires_confirmation_change\",\"requires_security_key\",\"kind\",\"updated_timestamp\",\"network_display_name\",\"name\",\"country\",\"financial_institution\",\"account\",\"account_location\",\"entity_type\",\"wallet_type\",\"is_self\",\"beneficiary_created\",\"beneficiary_updated\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/set_address_requires_security_key\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-set_address_requires_security_key\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/set_clearance_originator\",\"description\":\"Sets originator of the deposit\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fset_clearance_originator)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/set_clearance_originator\",\"keywords\":[\"private/set_clearance_originator\",\"deposit_id\",\"originator\",\"currency\",\"address\",\"amount\",\"state\",\"transaction_id\",\"source_address\",\"received_timestamp\",\"updated_timestamp\",\"note\",\"clearance_state\",\"refund_transaction_id\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/set_clearance_originator\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-set_clearance_originator\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/set_coinbase_subaccount_withdrawals_allowed\",\"description\":\"Allows or disallows withdrawals from subaccounts. Can be called only by the main account; subaccounts receive a `forbidden` error. The setting applies to Coinbase wallet type withdrawals — when disabled, `private/withdraw` requests from subaccounts of a Coinbase wallet type account are rejected.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Withdrawals](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-withdrawals-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fset_coinbase_subaccount_withdrawals_allowed)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/set_coinbase_subaccount_withdrawals_allowed\",\"keywords\":[\"private/set_coinbase_subaccount_withdrawals_allowed\",\"enabled\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/set_coinbase_subaccount_withdrawals_allowed\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-set_coinbase_subaccount_withdrawals_allowed\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/submit_transfer_between_subaccounts\",\"description\":\"Transfer funds between two subaccounts or between a subaccount and the main account.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Transfers](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-transfers-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallets:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fsubmit_transfer_between_subaccounts)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/submit_transfer_between_subaccounts\",\"keywords\":[\"private/submit_transfer_between_subaccounts\",\"currency\",\"amount\",\"destination\",\"source\",\"nonce\",\"created_timestamp\",\"type\",\"other_side\",\"state\",\"direction\",\"updated_timestamp\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/submit_transfer_between_subaccounts\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-submit_transfer_between_subaccounts\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/submit_transfer_to_subaccount\",\"description\":\"Transfer funds from the main account to a subaccount.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Transfers](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-transfers-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallets:read_write`\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fsubmit_transfer_to_subaccount)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/submit_transfer_to_subaccount\",\"keywords\":[\"private/submit_transfer_to_subaccount\",\"currency\",\"amount\",\"destination\",\"created_timestamp\",\"type\",\"other_side\",\"state\",\"direction\",\"updated_timestamp\",\"nonce\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/submit_transfer_to_subaccount\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-submit_transfer_to_subaccount\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/submit_transfer_to_user\",\"description\":\"Transfer funds to another user. This method allows you to send funds from your main account to another Deribit user's account. The transfer is processed internally and does not require blockchain transactions.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Managing Transfers](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/managing-transfers-api)\\n\\n**Scope:** `wallet:read_write` and mainaccount\\n\\n[Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fprivate%2Fsubmit_transfer_to_user)\\n\\n\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/submit_transfer_to_user\",\"keywords\":[\"private/submit_transfer_to_user\",\"currency\",\"amount\",\"destination\",\"created_timestamp\",\"type\",\"other_side\",\"state\",\"direction\",\"updated_timestamp\",\"nonce\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/submit_transfer_to_user\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-submit_transfer_to_user\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/update_in_address_book\",\"description\":\"$70\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/update_in_address_book\",\"keywords\":[\"private/update_in_address_book\",\"currency\",\"type\",\"address\",\"network\",\"tag\",\"id\",\"label\",\"beneficiary_vasp_name\",\"beneficiary_vasp_did\",\"beneficiary_vasp_website\",\"beneficiary_first_name\",\"beneficiary_last_name\",\"beneficiary_company_name\",\"beneficiary_address\",\"agreed\",\"personal\",\"name\",\"country\",\"financial_institution\",\"account\",\"account_location\",\"entity_type\",\"wallet_type\",\"is_self\",\"kind\",\"creation_timestamp\",\"updated_timestamp\",\"status\",\"waiting_timestamp\",\"requires_confirmation\",\"requires_confirmation_change\",\"requires_security_key\",\"info_required\",\"network_display_name\",\"beneficiary_created\",\"beneficiary_updated\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/update_in_address_book\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-update_in_address_book\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true},{\"title\":\"private/withdraw\",\"description\":\"$71\",\"deprecated\":null,\"version\":null,\"og:title\":\"private/withdraw\",\"keywords\":[\"private/withdraw\",\"currency\",\"address\",\"amount\",\"network\",\"tag\",\"id\",\"priority\",\"nonce\",\"confirmed_timestamp\",\"created_timestamp\",\"fee\",\"state\",\"transaction_id\",\"updated_timestamp\",\"transfer_idem\",\"network_display_name\",\"destination_tag\",\"payment_id\",\"source_ctn_id\",\"destination_ctn_id\",\"clearance_state\",\"note\"],\"openapi\":\"/specifications/deribit_openapi.json get /private/withdraw\",\"href\":\"/api-reference/wallet/private-withdraw\",\"autogeneratedByOpenApi\":true}]}]}]},{\"dropdown\":\"Subscription Channels\",\"icon\":\"rss\",\"groups\":[{\"group\":\"Introduction\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Notifications\",\"description\":\"Subscribe to Deribit WebSocket notification channels for real-time order updates, trade fills, market data changes, and account events across sessions.\",\"keywords\":[\"WebSocket subscriptions\",\"real-time notifications\",\"market data subscriptions\",\"order book updates\",\"account notifications\",\"subscription channels\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit API Notifications and Subscriptions - Real-Time Data Guide\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to subscribe to Deribit API notifications for real-time market data, order book updates, account changes, and trading events via WebSocket.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit API Notifications Guide\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to Deribit API notifications and WebSocket subscriptions for real-time market data and account updates.\",\"href\":\"/articles/notifications\"}]},{\"group\":\"Websockets\",\"pages\":[{\"group\":\"Platform\",\"pages\":[{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json platform_state\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/platform/platform_state\",\"title\":\"platform_state \",\"description\":\"Platform state notifications.\\n\\nUse this channel to monitor whether the Deribit platform is operational and to detect maintenance periods or partial outages that may affect trading, authentication, or market data.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json platform_state.public_methods_state\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/platform/platform_statepublic_methods_state\",\"title\":\"platform_state.public_methods_state \",\"description\":\"Notifications indicating whether unauthenticated (public) requests are currently allowed.\\n\\nThis is useful for monitoring service availability for public endpoints (e.g., market data) without authentication.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Announcements\",\"pages\":[{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json announcements\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/announcements/announcements\",\"title\":\"announcements \",\"description\":\"General announcements concerning the Deribit platform.\\n\\nSubscribe to receive operational messages such as maintenance notices, incidents, and important platform updates.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Orderbook\",\"pages\":[{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json book.(instrument_name).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/orderbook/bookinstrument_nameinterval\",\"title\":\"book.(instrument_name).(interval) \",\"description\":\"$72\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json book.(instrument_name).(group).(depth).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/orderbook/bookinstrument_namegroupdepthinterval\",\"title\":\"book.(instrument_name).(group).(depth).(interval) \",\"description\":\"Aggregated order book updates for a specific instrument.\\n\\nNotifications are sent once per specified `interval`, with prices grouped (rounded) according to `group`, and the book truncated to the specified `depth` (number of price levels).\\n\\nThe `asks` and `bids` fields are both lists of `[price, amount]` pairs.\\n\\n- `price`: price level, rounded according to `group` (USD per BTC)\\n- `amount`: total amount at that price level\\n\\nFor Starbase-routed instruments, the published price levels include accepted mass-quote liquidity.\\n\\n**Units:** For perpetual and inverse futures the amount is in USD units. For options and linear futures it is in the underlying base currency coin.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Market Data\",\"pages\":[{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json ticker.(instrument_name).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/tickerinstrument_nameinterval\",\"title\":\"ticker.(instrument_name).(interval) \",\"description\":\"$73\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json incremental_ticker.(instrument_name)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/incremental_tickerinstrument_name\",\"title\":\"incremental_ticker.(instrument_name) \",\"description\":\"Real-time ticker updates for an instrument, delivered as a snapshot followed by incremental updates.\\n\\n- The first notification contains the full ticker snapshot.\\n- Subsequent notifications contain only fields that changed since the previous update.\\n\\nThis event is sent at most once per second.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json perpetual.(instrument_name).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/perpetualinstrument_nameinterval\",\"title\":\"perpetual.(instrument_name).(interval) \",\"description\":\"Provide current interest rate - but only for **perpetual** instruments. Other types won't generate any notification.\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json quote.(instrument_name)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/quoteinstrument_name\",\"title\":\"quote.(instrument_name) \",\"description\":\"Best bid/ask price and size for a specific instrument.\\n\\nThis subscription provides top-of-book updates (best bid and best ask) without the full depth of the order book. Use it when you only need the current spread and top sizes.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json deribit_price_index.(index_name)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/deribit_price_indexindex_name\",\"title\":\"deribit_price_index.(index_name) \",\"description\":\"Deribit index price updates for the given `index_name` (current index value).\\n\\nUse this channel to track the real-time value of a Deribit index (e.g., `btc_usd`), which is used across pricing, margining, and settlement-related calculations.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json deribit_price_ranking.(index_name)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/deribit_price_rankingindex_name\",\"title\":\"deribit_price_ranking.(index_name) \",\"description\":\"Price ranking updates for the component exchanges used to calculate the Deribit index.\\n\\nUse this channel to see per-exchange price contributions that feed into the index calculation for the given `index_name`.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json deribit_price_statistics.(index_name)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/deribit_price_statisticsindex_name\",\"title\":\"deribit_price_statistics.(index_name) \",\"description\":\"Basic statistics for the Deribit index.\\n\\nProvides statistical information related to the given `index_name` (e.g., aggregated stats derived from index updates). Useful for monitoring index behavior over time.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json deribit_volatility_index.(index_name)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/deribit_volatility_indexindex_name\",\"title\":\"deribit_volatility_index.(index_name) \",\"description\":\"Volatility index updates for the given `index_name`.\\n\\nUse this channel to receive volatility index values (e.g., DVOL-like measures) as they update.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json markprice.options.(index_name)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/markpriceoptionsindex_name\",\"title\":\"markprice.options.(index_name) \",\"description\":\"Options mark price updates for the given `index_name`.\\n\\nUse this channel to receive mark prices for options under the given index, useful for valuation, risk monitoring, and P\u0026L calculations.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json estimated_expiration_price.(index_name)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/estimated_expiration_priceindex_name\",\"title\":\"estimated_expiration_price.(index_name) \",\"description\":\"Estimated expiration (delivery) price updates for the given `index_name`.\\n\\nProvides calculated estimates of the ending price used around expirations/settlement. Useful for monitoring expected settlement levels.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json chart.trades.(instrument_name).(resolution)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/charttradesinstrument_nameresolution\",\"title\":\"chart.trades.(instrument_name).(resolution) \",\"description\":\"Publicly available market data used to generate a TradingView trade candle chart.\\n\\nDuring a single resolution period, many events can be sent, each with updated values for the recent period.\\n\\n**Notice:** When there is no trade during the requested resolution period (e.g. 1 minute), a filling sample is generated which uses data from the last available trade candle (open and close values).\\n\\n**Note:** For spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, this channel is not supported. Use [Get product candles](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/api-reference/exchange-api/rest-api/products/get-product-candles) instead.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json instrument.creation.(kind).(currency)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/instrumentcreationkindcurrency\",\"title\":\"instrument.creation.(kind).(currency) \",\"description\":\"Notification published once when an instrument is created, carrying full instrument data in the same format as `public/get_instruments`.\\n\\nThe notification fires exactly once at creation time, regardless of the instrument's initial state.\\n\\n**Subscription examples:**\\n\\n| Channel | Description |\\n|---|---|\\n| `instrument.creation.any.any` | All instruments |\\n| `instrument.creation.future.BTC` | BTC futures only |\\n| `instrument.creation.option.any` | All options |\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json instrument.state.(kind).(currency)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/market-data/instrumentstatekindcurrency\",\"title\":\"instrument.state.(kind).(currency) \",\"description\":\"Notifications about new or terminated instruments of a given kind in a given currency.\\n\\nUse this channel to track instrument lifecycle events (new listings, expirations/terminations) without polling.\\n\\n**Note:** Our system does not send notifications when currencies are locked. Users are advised to subscribe to the [platform_state](https://docs.deribit.com/subscriptions/platform/platform_state) channel to monitor the state of currencies actively.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Trades\",\"pages\":[{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json trades.(instrument_name).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/trades/tradesinstrument_nameinterval\",\"title\":\"trades.(instrument_name).(interval) \",\"description\":\"Trade notifications for a specific instrument.\\n\\nUse this channel to receive executed trades as they happen for the given instrument. The `interval` controls how frequently trade events are aggregated.\\n\\n**Note:** For spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, this channel is not supported. Use the [`matches` channel](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/exchange/websocket-feed/channels) for the full trade tape. For user trades, orders and changes, use the `user` channels.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json trades.(kind).(currency).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/trades/tradeskindcurrencyinterval\",\"title\":\"trades.(kind).(currency).(interval) \",\"description\":\"Trade notifications across all instruments for a given kind and currency.\\n\\nUse this channel when you want a consolidated stream of trades across all instruments of a specific `kind` (e.g., futures, options) and `currency`. The `interval` controls aggregation frequency.\\n\\n**Note:** For spot instruments routed to Coinbase Exchange, this channel is not supported with `kind` = `spot`: the subscription is rejected for any currency that is the base or the quote of a routed pair, and for `currency` = `any` whenever any pair is routed. Other kinds are unaffected. Use the [`matches` channel](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/exchange/websocket-feed/channels) for the full trade tape.\\n\\n**📖 Related Articles:** \\n- [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)\\n- [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)\\n- [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Block Trade\",\"pages\":[{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json block_trade_confirmations\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/block-trade/block_trade_confirmations\",\"title\":\"block_trade_confirmations \",\"description\":\"Provides notifications regarding block trade approval. Subscribe to this channel to receive notifications about pending block trades that require your approval.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json block_trade_confirmations.(currency)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/block-trade/block_trade_confirmationscurrency\",\"title\":\"block_trade_confirmations.(currency) \",\"description\":\"Provides notifications regarding block trade approval. Supports filtering by currency. Subscribe to this channel to receive notifications about pending block trades that require your approval, filtered by a specific currency.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Block Trading](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-trading-api)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"User\",\"pages\":[{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.mmp_trigger.(index_name)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/usermmp_triggerindex_name\",\"title\":\"user.mmp_trigger.(index_name) \",\"description\":\"$74\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.portfolio.(currency)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/userportfoliocurrency\",\"title\":\"user.portfolio.(currency) \",\"description\":\"$75\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.trades.(instrument_name).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/usertradesinstrument_nameinterval\",\"title\":\"user.trades.(instrument_name).(interval) \",\"description\":\"User trade notifications for a specific instrument.\\n\\nReceive private trade events for your account for the given instrument. The `interval` controls how frequently events are aggregated.\\n\\n**Block RFQ trades:** Trades resulting from Block RFQ execution are included in this channel. These trades carry the following additional fields:\\n- `block_rfq_id` — ID of the Block RFQ.\\n- `block_trade_id` — ID of the resulting block trade.\\n- `block_rfq_quote_id` — ID of the accepted quote (present on the **maker** side only).\\n- `order_id` — always present for direct trade participants (makers and takers).\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.trades.(kind).(currency).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/usertradeskindcurrencyinterval\",\"title\":\"user.trades.(kind).(currency).(interval) \",\"description\":\"User trade notifications across all instruments for a given kind and currency.\\n\\nReceive a consolidated stream of your private trades across all instruments matching the specified `kind` and `currency`. The `interval` controls aggregation frequency.\\n\\n**Block RFQ trades:** Trades resulting from Block RFQ execution are included in this channel. See `user.trades.{instrument_name}.{interval}` for the complete list of Block RFQ-specific fields.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.combo_trades.(instrument_name).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/usercombo_tradesinstrument_nameinterval\",\"title\":\"user.combo_trades.(instrument_name).(interval) \",\"description\":\"User trade notifications for a specific combo instrument.\\n\\nTrades include a `legs` field describing the underlying legs of the combo. The `interval` controls aggregation frequency.\\n\\n**Block RFQ trades:** Block RFQ does not support combo instruments. RFQ-executed trades do not appear in this channel.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.combo_trades.(kind).(currency).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/usercombo_tradeskindcurrencyinterval\",\"title\":\"user.combo_trades.(kind).(currency).(interval) \",\"description\":\"User trade notifications across all combo instruments for a given kind and currency.\\n\\nTrades include a `legs` field describing the underlying legs. The `interval` controls aggregation frequency.\\n\\n**Block RFQ trades:** Block RFQ does not support combo instruments. RFQ-executed trades do not appear in this channel.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.orders.(instrument_name).raw\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/userordersinstrument_nameraw\",\"title\":\"user.orders.(instrument_name).raw \",\"description\":\"User order updates for a specific instrument (raw stream).\\n\\nUse this channel to receive private order updates for the given instrument with the highest granularity (raw). Prefer this for real-time order state tracking.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.orders.(instrument_name).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/userordersinstrument_nameinterval\",\"title\":\"user.orders.(instrument_name).(interval) \",\"description\":\"User order updates for a specific instrument (aggregated).\\n\\nUse this channel to receive private order updates for the given instrument, aggregated according to `interval`.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.orders.(kind).(currency).raw\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/userorderskindcurrencyraw\",\"title\":\"user.orders.(kind).(currency).raw \",\"description\":\"User order updates across all instruments for a given kind and currency (raw stream).\\n\\nUse this channel to receive private order updates across all matching instruments with the highest granularity (raw).\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.orders.(kind).(currency).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/userorderskindcurrencyinterval\",\"title\":\"user.orders.(kind).(currency).(interval) \",\"description\":\"User order updates across all instruments for a given kind and currency (aggregated).\\n\\nUse this channel to receive private order updates across all matching instruments, aggregated according to `interval`.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.changes.(instrument_name).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/userchangesinstrument_nameinterval\",\"title\":\"user.changes.(instrument_name).(interval) \",\"description\":\"User change stream (orders, trades, and related updates) for a specific instrument.\\n\\nThis channel provides a consolidated private update stream for your account for the given instrument. Use it when you want a single feed instead of subscribing to orders and trades separately.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.changes.(kind).(currency).(interval)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/userchangeskindcurrencyinterval\",\"title\":\"user.changes.(kind).(currency).(interval) \",\"description\":\"User change stream (orders, trades, and related updates) across all instruments for a given kind and currency.\\n\\nThis channel provides a consolidated private update stream for your account across all matching instruments. Use it when you want a single feed instead of subscribing to orders and trades separately.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.access_log\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/useraccess_log\",\"title\":\"user.access_log \",\"description\":\"Security event notifications for the account.\\n\\nUse this channel to monitor account-related security events (e.g., access log entries) and build alerting around suspicious activity.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.lock\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/userlock\",\"title\":\"user.lock \",\"description\":\"Notifications when the account is locked or unlocked.\\n\\nUse this channel to react to account lock events (e.g., pause trading workflows) and to detect when access is restored.\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.liquidation\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/userliquidation\",\"title\":\"user.liquidation \",\"description\":\"$76\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.isolated.liquidation\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/userisolatedliquidation\",\"title\":\"user.isolated.liquidation \",\"description\":\"Lets a **main** account observe the liquidation, ADL, and LSP activity of all of its **isolated-margin subaccounts**, without subscribing to each subaccount's own `user.liquidation` channel individually.\\n\\nEvery event on this channel is a fan-out copy of an event also delivered on the affected subaccount's own `user.liquidation` channel — the payload is identical, including `isolated: true` and the subaccount's `user_id`. The main account's *own* liquidation activity is never delivered here; it stays on the main account's regular `user.liquidation` channel.\\n\\nRequires the `account:read` scope on an API key belonging to the **main account**, and is only available while isolated margin is enabled on the platform.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Liquidity Support Program (LSP) API Guide](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/lsp-api-guide)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json user.lsp\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/user/userlsp\",\"title\":\"user.lsp \",\"description\":\"$77\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true}]},{\"group\":\"Block Rfq\",\"pages\":[{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json block_rfq.maker.(currency)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/block-rfq/block_rfqmakercurrency\",\"title\":\"block_rfq.maker.(currency) \",\"description\":\"$78\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json block_rfq.taker.(currency)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/block-rfq/block_rfqtakercurrency\",\"title\":\"block_rfq.taker.(currency) \",\"description\":\"Get notifications about the state of your Block RFQ. `trades` are only visible if the Block RFQ was filled.\\n\\n**Note:** After Block RFQ creation, a grace period of 5 seconds begins, during which the taker cannot see quotes or trade the Block RFQ.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json block_rfq.maker.quotes.(currency)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/block-rfq/block_rfqmakerquotescurrency\",\"title\":\"block_rfq.maker.quotes.(currency) \",\"description\":\"Get notifications about the state of your Block RFQ quotes. Subscribe to this channel to receive real-time updates when your quotes are added, edited, cancelled, or when quotes are accepted by takers.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true},{\"asyncapi\":\"specifications/deribit_asyncapi.json block_rfq.trades.(currency)\",\"href\":\"/subscriptions/block-rfq/block_rfqtradescurrency\",\"title\":\"block_rfq.trades.(currency) \",\"description\":\"Get notifications about recent Block RFQ trades. This is a public channel that provides market data about completed Block RFQ trades.\\n\\n**📖 Related Article:** [Deribit Block RFQ API walkthrough](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/block-rfq-api-walkthrough)\\n\",\"version\":null,\"autogeneratedByAsyncApi\":true}]}]}]},{\"dropdown\":\"FIX API\",\"icon\":\"bolt\",\"pages\":[{\"group\":\"Overview\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Deribit Production FIX API Overview\",\"description\":\"Overview of the Deribit production FIX 4.4 subset covering endpoints, supported message types, and how the live FIX gateway differs from the upcoming one.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"keywords\":[\"FIX API\",\"FIX protocol\",\"institutional trading\",\"FIX 4.4\",\"financial information exchange\",\"trading protocol\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit FIX API Overview - Institutional Trading Protocol\",\"og:description\":\"Complete overview of Deribit's FIX API for institutional trading. Learn about connection endpoints, message structure, session management, and order execution.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit FIX API Overview\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to Deribit's FIX API for institutional trading including endpoints, message types, and protocol specifications.\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/overview\"}]},{\"group\":\"Session Management\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Logon(A) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"Logon(A) authenticates and establishes a session on the Deribit production FIX API, covering credentials, heartbeat interval, and cancel-on-disconnect setup.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"keywords\":[\"FIX logon\",\"FIX authentication\",\"FIX session\",\"FIX connection\",\"FIX protocol\",\"session management\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit FIX Logon Message - Session Authentication\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to use the FIX Logon message to authenticate and establish a FIX session with Deribit, including authentication parameters and heartbeat configuration.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit FIX Logon Message\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to FIX Logon message for authenticating FIX sessions with Deribit.\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/logon\"},{\"title\":\"Logout(5) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"Logout(5) terminates a session on the Deribit production FIX API, describing the proper shutdown sequence and Cancel on Disconnect behavior on exit.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"keywords\":[\"FIX logout\",\"FIX session termination\",\"FIX disconnect\",\"session management\",\"FIX protocol\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit FIX Logout Message - Session Termination\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to properly terminate a FIX session using the Logout message, including Cancel on Disconnect behavior and connection closure.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit FIX Logout Message\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to FIX Logout message for terminating FIX sessions with Deribit.\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/logout\"},{\"title\":\"Heartbeat(0) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"Heartbeat(0) message exchanged between counterparties to verify the Deribit production FIX session is alive and detect connection loss during idle periods.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/heartbeat\"},{\"title\":\"Test Request(1) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"TestRequest(1) solicits a Heartbeat response from the counterparty to verify the Deribit production FIX session is responsive during idle connection periods.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/test-request\"},{\"title\":\"Resend Request(2) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"ResendRequest(2) recovers missed FIX messages from the Deribit production sequence gap by asking the counterparty to resend a specified message range.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/resend-request\"},{\"title\":\"Reject(3) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"Reject(3) is the session-level reject sent by the Deribit production FIX server for malformed messages or protocol violations, with tag-level reason codes.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/reject\"},{\"title\":\"Sequence Reset(4) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"SequenceReset(4) repositions FIX sequence numbers on the Deribit production FIX session to recover from gaps or apply a graceful counterparty reset.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/sequence-reset\"}]},{\"group\":\"Market Data\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Security List Request(x) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"SecurityListRequest(x) requests the full list of tradable instruments from the Deribit production FIX API, filterable by underlying and product kind.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/security-list-request\"},{\"title\":\"Security List(y) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"SecurityList(y) is the server response containing the tradable instrument catalogue for the Deribit production FIX API, returned per SecurityListRequest.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/security-list\"},{\"title\":\"Market Data Request(V) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"FIX Market Data Request subscribes to order book data and market updates. Learn how to request snapshots and incremental updates via FIX.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"keywords\":[\"FIX market data\",\"order book subscription\",\"FIX subscriptions\",\"market data request\",\"FIX protocol\",\"real-time data\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit FIX Market Data Request - Subscribe to Order Book Data\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to request market data subscriptions using FIX Market Data Request message for order book snapshots and incremental updates.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit FIX Market Data Request\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to requesting market data subscriptions using FIX Market Data Request message on Deribit.\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/market-data-request\"},{\"title\":\"Market Data Request Reject(Y) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"MarketDataRequestReject(Y) is the Deribit production FIX API server response when a MarketDataRequest is refused, listing reject reason codes and remediation.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/market-data-request-reject\"},{\"title\":\"Market Data Snapshot (W) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"MarketDataSnapshotFullRefresh(W) delivers the initial full order book snapshot on the Deribit production FIX API before incremental updates begin streaming.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/market-data-snapshot\"},{\"title\":\"Market Data Incremental Refresh(X) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"MarketDataIncrementalRefresh(X) delivers incremental order book updates and trade events on the Deribit production FIX API after a snapshot subscription.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/market-data-incremental\"},{\"title\":\"Security Status Request(e) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"SecurityStatusRequest(e) subscribes to trading status updates for an instrument on the Deribit production FIX API, covering halts, resumes, and settlement.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/security-status-request\"},{\"title\":\"Security Status(f) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"SecurityStatus(f) is the server-pushed notification of trading status changes such as halt, resume, or settlement for a Deribit production FIX instrument.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/security-status\"}]},{\"group\":\"Order Management\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"New Order Single(D) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"NewOrderSingle(D) submits new orders to the Deribit production FIX API, covering order types, parameters, and how to place limit, market, and advanced orders.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"keywords\":[\"FIX new order\",\"FIX order placement\",\"FIX trading\",\"order submission\",\"FIX protocol\",\"limit orders\",\"market orders\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit FIX New Order Single - Submit Orders via FIX\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to submit new orders to Deribit using FIX New Order Single message, including order types, parameters, and advanced order features.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit FIX New Order Single\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to submitting orders using FIX New Order Single message on Deribit.\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/new-order-single\"},{\"title\":\"Order Cancel Request(F) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"FIX Order Cancel Request cancels existing orders. Learn how to cancel orders by order ID, client order ID, or label using FIX protocol.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"keywords\":[\"FIX cancel order\",\"order cancellation\",\"FIX order management\",\"cancel request\",\"FIX protocol\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit FIX Order Cancel Request - Cancel Orders via FIX\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to cancel orders using FIX Order Cancel Request message, including cancellation by order ID, client order ID, or custom label.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit FIX Order Cancel Request\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to cancelling orders using FIX Order Cancel Request message on Deribit.\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/order-cancel-request\"},{\"title\":\"Order Cancel Reject(9) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"OrderCancelReject(9) is the server reject for a cancel or cancel/replace request on the Deribit production FIX API, including reason codes for the failure.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/order-cancel-reject\"},{\"title\":\"Order Cancel/Replace Request(G) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"OrderCancelReplaceRequest(G) modifies the price or quantity of a working order on the Deribit production FIX API without cancelling and resubmitting it.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/order-cancel-replace\"},{\"title\":\"Order Mass Cancel Request(q) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"OrderMassCancelRequest(q) cancels all open orders matching filters like instrument, side, or underlying in one Deribit production FIX API message.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/order-mass-cancel-request\"},{\"title\":\"Order Mass Cancel Report(r) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"OrderMassCancelReport(r) is the server report confirming or rejecting a mass cancel operation on the Deribit production FIX API, with affected order counts.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/order-mass-cancel-report\"},{\"title\":\"Order Mass Status Request(AF) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"OrderMassStatusRequest(AF) requests the current status of many open orders in a single call on the Deribit production FIX API for efficient reconciliation.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/order-mass-status-request\"},{\"title\":\"Execution Reports(8) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"FIX Execution Reports provide order status updates and trade confirmations. Learn how to receive and interpret execution reports for order changes and fills.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"keywords\":[\"FIX execution reports\",\"order status\",\"trade confirmations\",\"FIX notifications\",\"order updates\",\"FIX protocol\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit FIX Execution Reports - Order Status and Trade Confirmations\",\"og:description\":\"Learn how to receive and interpret FIX Execution Reports for order status updates, trade confirmations, and order change notifications from Deribit.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit FIX Execution Reports\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to FIX Execution Reports for order status and trade confirmations on Deribit.\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/execution-reports\"}]},{\"group\":\"Position Management\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Request For Positions(AN) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"RequestForPositions(AN) requests a snapshot of open positions from the Deribit production FIX API, returned to the client as PositionReport messages.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/request-for-positions\"},{\"title\":\"Position Report(AP) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"PositionReport(AP) is the server-pushed report of open positions on the Deribit production FIX API, sent in response to a RequestForPositions or trade update.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/position-report\"}]},{\"group\":\"User Management\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"User Request(BE) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"UserRequest(BE) requests user status changes such as logging users in or out of the Deribit production FIX API session for account-level control.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/user-request\"},{\"title\":\"User Response(BF) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"UserResponse(BF) is the server response to a UserRequest on the Deribit production FIX API, reporting the current user status after processing.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/user-response\"}]},{\"group\":\"Market Maker Protection\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"MMProtection Limits (MM) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"MMProtectionLimits(MM) sets market maker protection thresholds such as quantity, delta, and frozen time on the Deribit production FIX API endpoint.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/mmprotection-limits\"},{\"title\":\"MMProtection Limits Result (MR) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"MMProtectionLimitsResult(MR) is the server response with current MMP settings or a reject on the Deribit production FIX market maker protection endpoint.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/mmprotection-limits-result\"},{\"title\":\"MMProtection Reset(MZ) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"MMProtectionReset(MZ) clears a triggered market maker protection freeze on the Deribit production FIX API so quoting can resume after an MMP event.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/mmprotection-reset\"}]},{\"group\":\"Mass Quoting\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Mass Quote(i) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"MassQuote(i) submits many two-sided quotes in a single message on the Deribit production FIX API, letting market makers reduce quoting latency at scale.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/mass-quote\"},{\"title\":\"Mass Quote Acknowledgement(b) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"MassQuoteAcknowledgement(b) is the server acknowledgement for a MassQuote submission on Deribit production FIX, with per-quote status and reject reasons.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/mass-quote-acknowledgement\"},{\"title\":\"Quote Cancel(Z) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"QuoteCancel(Z) cancels one or many previously submitted mass quotes on the Deribit production FIX API without needing to submit any replacement quotes.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/quote-cancel\"}]},{\"group\":\"Trade Capture\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"TradeCaptureReportRequest(AD) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"TradeCaptureReportRequest(AD) requests historical or streaming trade capture reports on the Deribit production FIX API, filterable by trade criteria.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/trade-capture-report-request\"},{\"title\":\"TradeCaptureReportRequestAck(AQ) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"TradeCaptureReportRequestAck(AQ) acknowledges a TradeCaptureReportRequest on the Deribit production FIX API and indicates whether reports will follow.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/trade-capture-report-request-ack\"},{\"title\":\"TradeCaptureReport(AE) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"TradeCaptureReport(AE) delivers executed trade details on the Deribit production FIX API in response to a TradeCaptureReportRequest or as unsolicited updates.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/trade-capture-report\"}]},{\"group\":\"Security Definition\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Security Definition Request(c) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"SecurityDefinitionRequest(c) requests detailed contract definitions for one instrument on the Deribit production FIX API before market data subscription.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/security-definition-request\"},{\"title\":\"Security Definition(d) (Production FIX API)\",\"description\":\"SecurityDefinition(d) is the server response describing an instrument's contract terms and trading parameters on the Deribit production FIX API.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/fix-api/production/security-definition\"}]}]},{\"dropdown\":\"Starbase API\",\"icon\":\"rocket\",\"pages\":[{\"group\":\"Introduction\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Starbase API Overview\",\"description\":\"Introduction to Deribit Starbase covering the low-latency binary and FIX API stack, gateway architecture, product scope, and migration from legacy SBE.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"keywords\":[\"Starbase API\",\"binary protocol\",\"institutional trading\",\"multicast\",\"gateway connectivity\"],\"og:title\":\"Deribit Starbase API Overview - High-Performance Binary Protocol\",\"og:description\":\"Complete overview of Deribit's Starbase API including Binary API, multicast channels, and gateway connectivity for institutional trading.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Deribit Starbase API Overview\",\"twitter:description\":\"Complete guide to Deribit's Starbase high-performance binary protocol API for institutional trading.\",\"href\":\"/starbase/overview\"},{\"title\":\"Starbase Connectivity Quickstart\",\"description\":\"Plan Starbase network access, assign a Member before creating API keys, connect to test gateways and multicast feeds, and prepare for production.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"keywords\":[\"Starbase quickstart\",\"Member\",\"API key\",\"connectivity\",\"LD4\",\"cross-connect\",\"AWS Private Link\",\"SBE\",\"multicast\",\"FIX Drop Copy\"],\"og:title\":\"Starbase Connectivity Quickstart\",\"og:description\":\"Step-by-step guide to assigning a Starbase Member, creating API keys, connecting to gateways and multicast feeds, and preparing for production.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Starbase Connectivity Quickstart\",\"twitter:description\":\"Assign a Member, create Starbase API keys, validate gateway and multicast connectivity, and prepare a resilient production deployment.\",\"href\":\"/starbase/quickstart\"},{\"title\":\"Creating and Assigning a Member\",\"description\":\"Create a Starbase Member on the main account and assign every subaccount that will trade before you generate API keys.\",\"keywords\":[\"Starbase Member\",\"create Member\",\"assign Member\",\"No active member\",\"Direct Access\",\"portfolio\"],\"og:title\":\"Creating and Assigning a Starbase Member\",\"og:description\":\"Create a Starbase Member, assign main-account and subaccount UIDs, and avoid the No active member error before creating API keys.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Creating and Assigning a Starbase Member\",\"twitter:description\":\"How to create a Starbase Member and assign accounts before creating API keys.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/starbase/creating-member\"},{\"title\":\"Creating a Starbase API Key\",\"description\":\"Create Starbase API keys, pick Starbase-specific scopes, and resolve the No active member error after the target account belongs to a Member.\",\"keywords\":[\"Starbase API key\",\"create Starbase key\",\"SBE API key\",\"FIX Drop Copy\",\"SBE Order Entry\",\"REST\"],\"og:title\":\"Creating Starbase API Keys\",\"og:description\":\"Step-by-step guide to creating API keys for Starbase with the correct scopes after Member assignment.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Creating Starbase API Keys\",\"twitter:description\":\"How to create Starbase API keys and configure scopes for the Starbase matching engine.\",\"mode\":\"wide\",\"href\":\"/starbase/creating-api-key\"},{\"title\":\"Production Readiness Checklist\",\"description\":\"Readiness checklist for clients onboarding to Starbase SBE order entry: Member setup, API key scopes, MMP risk bypass, SBE XMLs, and logon testing.\",\"keywords\":[\"Starbase\",\"checklist\",\"production readiness\",\"SBE order entry\",\"MMP\",\"risk bypass\",\"SBE XML\"],\"og:title\":\"Starbase Production Readiness Checklist\",\"og:description\":\"Confirm Member setup, API key scopes, MMP risk bypass, the latest SBE XMLs, and session logon for Starbase order entry.\",\"og:type\":\"article\",\"twitter:title\":\"Starbase Production Rea